ers/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/6e491e6191604ec09b023cb6b0d82351f6af6fc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-03T06:12:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-03T06:12:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Refactor /courses hub page\n\nThe previous design stacked four ~600px identical cards vertically —\nno hierarchy, no differentiation, no ecosystem context. Refactored\ninto a structured page with five purposeful sections:\n\n1. Hero\n   - Strong positioning (\"Cloud Native Security & Production\n     Engineering Courses\") aligned with the rest of the site.\n   - Aggregate stats: total courses, total modules, total labs, $0.\n   - Subtle gradient backdrop to anchor the brand identity.\n\n2. Featured course\n   - Highlights the newest course (highest id) with a larger,\n     theme-coloured card and target-audience checklist.\n   - Currently surfaces the new Distributed Systems Engineering\n     course in orange/amber.\n\n3. All courses grid (2-col on desktop)\n   - Compact, themed cards instead of vertical full-width slabs.\n   - Per-course color theme + icon (cyan SPIFFE/SPIRE,\n     purple Cloud Native Security, pink RAG, orange Distributed\n     Systems) so they''re visually differentiable at a glance.\n   - Stats row, top-5 tags + \"+N more\", instructor attribution,\n     and a directional CTA.\n   - line-clamp-3 on subtitle keeps every card consistent height.\n\n4. Suggested learning paths (3 tracks)\n   - Distributed Systems Track: DSE → CNS → SPIFFE/SPIRE\n   - Security Engineer Track: CNS → SPIFFE/SPIRE → Simulators\n   - AI Infrastructure Track: DSE → RAG → AI Infra Security game\n   Each path numbers the steps with linked anchors.\n\n5. Beyond the courses (ecosystem)\n   - Security Simulators (10 games), Cheatsheets (operational\n     references), Engineering Blog (long-form deep dives).\n   - Closes the loop: hub doesn''t just list courses, it positions\n     them inside the broader learning ecosystem.\n\nImplementation:\n- Single CourseTheme map keyed by course slug; class strings written\n  literally so Tailwind detects them at build time.\n- computed() signals for totals and featured-course selection.\n- Total file: 280 lines (was 107) but covers far more surface and is\n  fully theme-driven so adding a 5th course is just a CourseTheme\n  entry plus the existing course data.\n\nProduction build verified clean.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0126dj1HZL7BMD66DmDm6DUa","tree":{"sha":"a488de0402c0019d0170096465d6bc79cdd61886","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/git/trees/a488de0402c0019d0170096465d6bc79cdd61886"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/git/commits/6e491e6191604ec09b023cb6b0d82351f6af6fc8","verification":{"payload":"tree a488de0402c0019d0170096465d6bc79cdd61886\nparent fc1d79e3683aa280fe59fab2bdc73bb41b18d8f3\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1777788752 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1777788752 +0000\n\nRefactor /courses hub page\n\nThe previous design stacked four ~600px identical cards vertically —\nno hierarchy, no differentiation, no ecosystem context. Refactored\ninto a structured page with five purposeful sections:\n\n1. Hero\n   - Strong positioning (\"Cloud Native Security & Production\n     Engineering Courses\") aligned with the rest of the site.\n   - Aggregate stats: total courses, total modules, total labs, $0.\n   - Subtle gradient backdrop to anchor the brand identity.\n\n2. Featured course\n   - Highlights the newest course (highest id) with a larger,\n     theme-coloured card and target-audience checklist.\n   - Currently surfaces the new Distributed Systems Engineering\n     course in orange/amber.\n\n3. All courses grid (2-col on desktop)\n   - Compact, themed cards instead of vertical full-width slabs.\n   - Per-course color theme + icon (cyan SPIFFE/SPIRE,\n     purple Cloud Native Security, pink RAG, orange Distributed\n     Systems) so they''re visually differentiable at a glance.\n   - Stats row, top-5 tags + \"+N more\", instructor attribution,\n     and a directional CTA.\n   - line-clamp-3 on subtitle keeps every card consistent height.\n\n4. Suggested learning paths (3 tracks)\n   - Distributed Systems Track: DSE → CNS → SPIFFE/SPIRE\n   - Security Engineer Track: CNS → SPIFFE/SPIRE → Simulators\n   - AI Infrastructure Track: DSE → RAG → AI Infra Security game\n   Each path numbers the steps with linked anchors.\n\n5. Beyond the courses (ecosystem)\n   - Security Simulators (10 games), Cheatsheets (operational\n     references), Engineering Blog (long-form deep dives).\n   - Closes the loop: hub doesn''t just list courses, it positions\n     them inside the broader learning ecosystem.\n\nImplementation:\n- Single CourseTheme map keyed by course slug; class strings written\n  literally so Tailwind detects them at build time.\n- computed() signals for totals and featured-course selection.\n- Total file: 280 lines (was 107) but covers far more surface and is\n  fully theme-driven so adding a 5th course is just a CourseThem