kwDOR5J1D9oAKGVkOGQ0NDM0N2M5ZDZmMmY4MDIxZjgzM2FjMGE1MGU4YThhZTUyYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commit/4513f9d5e9e9aeeec1e7c4f9a715e6445e1965f5","sha":"4513f9d5e9e9aeeec1e7c4f9a715e6445e1965f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/4513f9d5e9e9aeeec1e7c4f9a715e6445e1965f5"}],"sha":"ed8d44347c9d6f2f8021f833ac0a50e8a8ae52c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/ed8d44347c9d6f2f8021f833ac0a50e8a8ae52c1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/4513f9d5e9e9aeeec1e7c4f9a715e6445e1965f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-02T20:00:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-02T20:00:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add Distributed Systems Engineering course (12 modules)\n\nA production-grade, beginner-friendly but deeply practical course on\ndistributed systems engineering — architecture-first, diagram-heavy,\nhands-on labs every module, completely free.\n\nCourse structure:\n\n  1. Foundations of Distributed Systems\n     CAP/PACELC, latency/availability/fault-tolerance math, consistency\n     models, why distribute (failure isolation, scaling, autonomy).\n\n  2. Networking & Distributed Communication\n     TCP/HTTP-2/gRPC, service discovery, load balancing, retries with\n     backoff & budgets, connection pooling, DNS as risk surface.\n\n  3. Event-Driven & Asynchronous Systems\n     Queues vs pub/sub vs event streaming, Kafka in production,\n     delivery guarantees, idempotency, backpressure, consumer lag.\n\n  4. Distributed Data Management\n     Single-leader/multi-leader/leaderless replication, sharding, hash\n     vs range partitioning, consistent hashing, quorum math (W+R>N),\n     consistency models in practice.\n\n  5. Consensus & Coordination\n     Raft step-by-step, Paxos vs Raft, cluster sizing (2N+1),\n     distributed locking with fencing tokens, etcd/Zookeeper/Consul\n     operational discipline.\n\n  6. Scalability Engineering\n     Stateless services, multi-layer caching, CDN edge, Kubernetes\n     HPA/VPA/Karpenter, distributed rate limiting (Redis Lua),\n     bottleneck identification.\n\n  7. Reliability & Failure Engineering\n     Circuit breakers (CLOSED/OPEN/HALF-OPEN), bulkheads, graceful\n     degradation, chaos engineering with Chaos Mesh/Gremlin, breaking\n     cascading failures.\n\n  8. Distributed Security & Zero Trust (differentiator module)\n     Zero Trust principle, mTLS, SPIFFE/SPIRE workload identity, OPA\n     authz with Rego, federation across trust domains. Cross-links to\n     the Mastering SPIFFE & SPIRE deep-dive course.\n\n  9. Observability & Debugging\n     OpenTelemetry, distributed tracing, four golden signals,\n     structured logging, correlation IDs, SLOs and error budgets, the\n     incident-triage flow that actually works.\n\n  10. Kubernetes & Cloud Native Distributed Systems\n      Cluster architecture, Service/Ingress/Gateway API, service\n      meshes (Istio/Linkerd/Cilium), StatefulSets, autoscaling, PDBs,\n      multi-AZ topology spread.\n\n  11. Real-World Failure Scenarios\n      Retry storms, cache stampedes, split brain, hot partitions,\n      queue overload, DNS outages, service-discovery failures,\n      cascading failure propagation, post-incident reviews.\n\n  12. Production System Design & Capstone\n      Multi-region active-active vs active-passive, RPO/RTO and DR\n      drills, capacity planning, cost engineering, real production\n      case studies (Kafka/Cassandra/Spanner), full capstone\n      architecture exercise.\n\nEach module includes:\n- 800–1500 word body with production-grade content\n- An inline SVG architecture diagram\n- 2–3 hands-on labs with repo paths, steps, and difficulty\n- Key takeaways\n- Glossary\n- Selected callouts (whyThisMatters, productionNotes, commonMistakes)\n\nPlus:\n- Course landing page (id 4)\n- 2 SEO landing pages\n- 6 course-level FAQs\n- Three explicit routes: /courses/distributed-systems-engineering,\n  /:moduleSlug, /:moduleSlug/slides\n- 13 sitemap.xml entries (landing + 12 modules)\n- 13 generate-routes.js static HTML stubs\n\nInternal linking is dense to existing content:\n- Distributed Systems Algorithms blog (algorithm-level depth)\n- Caching Strategies blog (caching internals)\n- Rate Limiting Algorithms blog (rate-limiter internals)\n- Mastering SPIFFE & SPIRE course (Module 8 prerequisite path)\n- Cloud Native Security Engineering course (Module 8 + Kubernetes)\n- Kubernetes Security Simulator (hands-on operational practice)\n- Zero Trust Network Builder (workload identity practice)\n- Incident Response Simulator (Module 11 alignment)\n\nProduction build verified: 442kB initial bundle, 12 module stubs +\nlanding page generated to /dist, all routes resolve.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0126dj1HZL7BMD66DmDm6DUa","tree":{"sha":"4f397673a916bcf4d38ae8e7ea40b74ee71fad56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanan