ring with Chaos Mesh/Gremlin, breaking\n     cascading failures.\n\n  8. Distributed Security & Zero Trust (differentiator module)\n     Zero Trust principle, mTLS, SPIFFE/SPIRE workload identity, OPA\n     authz with Rego, federation across trust domains. Cross-links to\n     the Mastering SPIFFE & SPIRE deep-dive course.\n\n  9. Observability & Debugging\n     OpenTelemetry, distributed tracing, four golden signals,\n     structured logging, correlation IDs, SLOs and error budgets, the\n     incident-triage flow that actually works.\n\n  10. Kubernetes & Cloud Native Distributed Systems\n      Cluster architecture, Service/Ingress/Gateway API, service\n      meshes (Istio/Linkerd/Cilium), StatefulSets, autoscaling, PDBs,\n      multi-AZ topology spread.\n\n  11. Real-World Failure Scenarios\n      Retry storms, cache stampedes, split brain, hot partitions,\n      queue overload, DNS outages, service-discovery failures,\n      cascading failure propagation, post-incident reviews.\n\n  12. Production System Design & Capstone\n      Multi-region active-active vs active-passive, RPO/RTO and DR\n      drills, capacity planning, cost engineering, real production\n      case studies (Kafka/Cassandra/Spanner), full capstone\n      architecture exercise.\n\nEach module includes:\n- 800–1500 word body with production-grade content\n- An inline SVG architecture diagram\n- 2–3 hands-on labs with repo paths, steps, and difficulty\n- Key takeaways\n- Glossary\n- Selected callouts (whyThisMatters, productionNotes, commonMistakes)\n\nPlus:\n- Course landing page (id 4)\n- 2 SEO landing pages\n- 6 course-level FAQs\n- Three explicit routes: /courses/distributed-systems-engineering,\n  /:moduleSlug, /:moduleSlug/slides\n- 13 sitemap.xml entries (landing + 12 modules)\n- 13 generate-routes.js static HTML stubs\n\nInternal linking is dense to existing content:\n- Distributed Systems Algorithms blog (algorithm-level depth)\n- Caching Strategies blog (caching internals)\n- Rate Limiting Algorithms blog (rate-limiter internals)\n- Mastering SPIFFE & SPIRE course (Module 8 prerequisite path)\n- Cloud Native Security Engineering course (Module 8 + Kubernetes)\n- Kubernetes Security Simulator (hands-on operational practice)\n- Zero Trust Network Builder (workload identity practice)\n- Incident Response Simulator (Module 11 alignment)\n\nProduction build verified: 442kB initial bundle, 12 module stubs +\nlanding page generated to /dist, all routes resolve.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0126dj1HZL7BMD66DmDm6DUa\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI3ONjct\n8pMs8m5Xlkl2BGmqLQ1qNirdozF7AX+aONJ1xfD0Mxv8t3F/H9r1jQrk+zcCHkVjeWlzVEAUlPx6\nWQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-02T20:00:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commit/4513f9d5e9e9aeeec1e7c4f9a715e6445e1965f5","node_id":"C_kwDOR5J1D9oAKDQ1MTNmOWQ1ZTllOWFlZWVjMWU3YzRmOWE3MTVlNjQ0NWUxOTY1ZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commit/e30e71a6aea1fd9cfa93ed5135ba5a8801e654b5","sha":"e30e71a6aea1fd9cfa93ed5135ba5a8801e654b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/e30e71a6aea1fd9cfa93ed5135ba5a8801e654b5"}],"sha":"4513f9d5e9e9aeeec1e7c4f9a715e6445e1965f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/4513f9d5e9e9aeeec1e7c4f9a715e6445e1965f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/e30e71a6aea1fd9cfa93ed5135ba5a8801e654b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-02T19:17:08Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-02T19:17:08Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Close all gaps from the 4-blog production-engineering plan\n\nAudit-driven follow-up to the 4-blog plan (distributed systems,\nrate limiting, caching, scheduling). Closes every gap identified\nagainst the original brief.\n\nConclusion sections — added an explicit \"Conclusion\" H2 to all four\nblogs, separating the synthesis from the existing \"Where to Go Next\"\nlearning-path block. Each Conclusion summarises the high-leverage\nproduction takeaways for that topic so the reader walks away with\nthe operational distillation, not just the link list.\n\nMulti-region rate limiting — expanded into a full H3 section with\nthe three-model trade-off (per-region independent, global aggregation\nwith regional caches, globally-routed rate-limit service) and the\npractical layered pattern most teams converge on. Cross-links the\nCAP discussion in the distributed-systems blog.\n\nMesos coverage — expanded the scheduling blog''s Mesos section from\ntwo sentences to four paragraphs covering the two-level scheduler\nmodel (master + frameworks like Marathon, Aurora, Spark/Hadoop\nframeworks), why the model lost to Kubernetes operationally, and\nhow the Mesos design ideas resurface in the K8s scheduling\nframework, Yunikorn, and Yarn capacity scheduler.\n\nSix required diagrams — added every plan-named diagram that was\ndiscussed in prose but not drawn:\n  • Consistency models comparison (blog 1)\n  • Cache invalidation flow (CDC pipeline) (blog 3)\n  • Distributed cache topology (Redis Cluster) (blog 3)\n  • Multi-region cache architecture (blog 3)\n  • Task orchestration pipeline (Airflow DAG) (blog 4)\n  • Workload placement (pack vs spread) (blog 4)\n\nReusable callout patterns — added five callout component classes to\nsrc/styles.css covering the plan-named educational components:\n  .callout.callout-production   (ProductionNotes)\n  .callout.callout-security     (SecurityWarning)\n  .callout.callout-performance  (PerformanceTip)\n  .callout.callout-mistake      (CommonMistake)\n  .callout.callout-troubleshoot (TroubleshootingSection)\nThe classes work inside [innerHTML]-rendered blog HTML without\nrequiring an Angular component refactor; each callout supports a\n<strong> label rendered as the title plus a <p> body, with semantic\nicons and dark-theme-compatible colors. Applied 9 callouts across\nthe 4 blogs to demonstrate the pattern.\n\nExternal SVG assets — created 16 standalone SVG files at the\nplan-specified paths:\n  /public/assets/blogs/distributed-systems/  (5 SVGs)\n  /public/assets/blogs/rate-limiting/        (3 SVGs)\n  /public/assets/blogs/caching/              (4 SVGs)\n  /public/assets/blogs/scheduling/           (4 SVGs)\nThe blogs continue to render the visuals via inline SVG (which\npreserves aria-labels, scales crisply, and avoids extra HTTP\nrequests); the standalone files are reusable assets for future\ncontent (cheatsheets, courses, social previews).\n\nCheatsheet links audit — verified that /cheatsheets/devsecops,\n/cheatsheets/runtime-security, and /cheatsheets/service-mesh all\nexist as registered routes (the earlier audit had a truncated grep);\nno game links were broken. No changes needed.\n\nBuild verification: 442kB initial, 16 SVG assets under 24KB\ncombined, all 4 blog content chunks updated.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0126dj1HZL7BMD66DmDm6DUa","tree":{"sha":"43f6363b840a72c68424e0dbf97342dc53230eec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/git/trees/43f6363b840a72c68424e0dbf97342dc53230eec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/git/commits/e30e71a6aea1fd9cfa93ed5135ba5a8801e654b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 43f6363b840a72c68424e0dbf97342dc53230eec\nparent 5463ff32537ec2a724f2cf3da186d32315a8ebb6\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1777749428 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1777749428 +0000\n\nClose all gaps from the 4-blog production-engineering plan\n\nAudit-driven follow-up to the 4-blog plan (distributed systems,\nrate limiting, caching, scheduling). Closes every gap identified\nagainst the original brief.\n\nConclusion sections — added an explicit \"Conclusion\" H2 to all four\nblogs, separating the synthesis from the existing \"Where to Go Next\"\