laude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commit/e30e71a6aea1fd9cfa93ed5135ba5a8801e654b5","node_id":"C_kwDOR5J1D9oAKGUzMGU3MWE2YWVhMWZkOWNmYTkzZWQ1MTM1YmE1YTg4MDFlNjU0YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commit/5463ff32537ec2a724f2cf3da186d32315a8ebb6","sha":"5463ff32537ec2a724f2cf3da186d32315a8ebb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/5463ff32537ec2a724f2cf3da186d32315a8ebb6"}],"sha":"e30e71a6aea1fd9cfa93ed5135ba5a8801e654b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/e30e71a6aea1fd9cfa93ed5135ba5a8801e654b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/5463ff32537ec2a724f2cf3da186d32315a8ebb6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-02T18:15:02Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-02T18:15:02Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add 4 production-engineering deep dives to the blog\n\nFour long-form, production-grade infrastructure-engineering posts that\nestablish CodersSecret as a production-engineering and cloud-native\narchitecture authority. Each post is 4,000-5,000 words with inline\nSVG architecture diagrams, real-code examples, production case\nstudies, common pitfalls, observability guidance, security\nconsiderations, an FAQ section, and internal links to the existing\ncourses, glossary, and security simulators.\n\n1. Distributed Systems Algorithms (id 87, featured) — CAP and PACELC,\n   Paxos vs Raft consensus with leader-election internals, etcd /\n   Consul / CockroachDB in production, leader election beyond\n   consensus (Kafka, Sentinel, K8s leases), distributed locking with\n   fencing tokens, replication models (single/multi/leaderless),\n   quorum math (W+R>N), partitioning strategies, consistent hashing\n   with virtual nodes, gossip and SWIM, vector clocks and CRDTs,\n   consistency model hierarchy, and real failure scenarios (split\n   brain, clock skew, stuck etcd). Inline SVGs for the CAP triangle,\n   Raft state transitions, replication models, quorum overlap, and\n   the consistent-hashing ring with vnodes.\n\n2. Rate Limiting Algorithms (id 86) — fixed/sliding window, sliding\n   window log, sliding window counter with linear interpolation,\n   token bucket and leaky bucket, distributed rate limiting (Redis\n   Lua scripts, local + reconcile, edge-first origin-aware), NGINX\n   limit_req, Envoy local + global, Kubernetes ingress annotations,\n   adaptive rate limiting (AIMD, concurrency limits, Little''s Law),\n   DDoS mitigation patterns, and 4 common pitfalls. Inline SVGs for\n   sliding window counter, token bucket, and the distributed\n   rate-limiter architecture.\n\n3. Caching Strategies (id 85) — cache-aside vs read-through vs\n   write-through vs write-back, the multi-layer hierarchy from\n   browser through CDN to origin, Redis topologies (single,\n   sentinel, cluster), Memcached, CDN edge caching, six invalidation\n   strategies (TTL, explicit, CDC, write-through, surrogate keys,\n   versioned keys), thundering herd / cache stampede with three\n   defences (lock-and-recompute, probabilistic early expiration,\n   stale-while-revalidate), hot keys and hot partitions with four\n   mitigations, eviction policies, multi-region caching, database\n   buffer pools, Kubernetes patterns, and security considerations\n   including web cache deception. Inline SVGs for the access\n   patterns, hierarchy, and stampede defence.\n\n4. Scheduling Systems (id 84) — Kubernetes scheduler internals\n   (filter and score plugins), preemption, topology spread, custom\n   schedulers and the scheduling framework, bin packing heuristics\n   (first-fit, best-fit, FFD), distributed cron with leader leases,\n   Airflow / Nomad / Mesos / per-language job queues, fairness\n   algorithms (DRF), priority classes and quotas, exponential\n   backoff with jitter, idempotency keys, dead letter queues,\n   visibility timeouts, GPU scheduling, and cross-cluster placement\n   with workload identity. Inline SVGs for the scheduler flow and\n   the distributed job queue architecture.\n\nAll 4 posts are wired up automatically via the existing\ngenerate-routes.js + generate-sitemap.js pipelines that read from\nBLOG_POSTS. The Distributed Systems Algorithms post is set as\nfeatured to surface on the home page.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0126dj1HZL7BMD66DmDm6DUa","tree":{"sha":"15b5d4fd2df4720efbff4f44624541dadf951aa9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/git/trees/15b5d4fd2df4720efbff4f44624541dadf951aa9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/git/commits/5463ff32537ec2a724f2cf3da186d32315a8ebb6","verificatio