om/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/127ffd9b6ee9b20e59f1d12ef3c6f15c86e37705/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T20:10:22Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T20:10:22Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Complete the 7 coming-soon security simulators\n\nShips every remaining cloud-native security game using the shared\nScenarioQuizComponent pattern. Each is a fully-playable scenario quiz\nwith 6 production-grade scenarios, 4 plausible choices per scenario\nwith per-choice feedback, a production-grounded explanation, and a\ncross-link to the relevant course module:\n\n1. Incident Response Simulator (red) — Falco \"shell in container\"\n   triage, lateral movement via stolen SA tokens, crypto-miner\n   indicators, Tetragon-detected container drift, audit-log\n   compromise chains, eBPF detection of memfd-based fileless attacks.\n\n2. Supply Chain Defense Simulator (green) — cosign verify without\n   certificate-identity, syft SBOMs missing Go modules under\n   ldflags strip, SLSA L2 vs L3 provenance, dependency confusion\n   via --extra-index-url, GitHub Actions pull_request_target with\n   secrets exposed to fork checkouts, Kyverno verifyImages namespace\n   scope gaps.\n\n3. Service Mesh Routing Game (violet) — mesh-wide STRICT mTLS\n   without PERMISSIVE migration, AuthorizationPolicy ALLOW with\n   empty rules, RequestAuthentication that does not require JWTs,\n   VirtualService route ordering and broken canaries, retry-storm\n   amplification, istioctl proxy-config diagnostics.\n\n4. Threat Modeling Challenge (pink) — STRIDE classification of\n   token-enumeration as spoofing, identifying API-to-database as\n   the highest-stakes trust boundary, GDPR PII classification of\n   hashed device fingerprints, attack-tree reality (CI/CD over RCE\n   per Verizon DBIR), severity = impact × likelihood, mitigation\n   ranking by blast-radius reduction.\n\n5. Secure Architecture Builder (blue) — three-tier VPC layout\n   (public/private/isolated), WAF at edge AND origin with\n   CloudFront-to-ALB header verification, AWS SSM + IAM database\n   auth replacing SSH bastions, Secrets Manager + Secrets Store CSI\n   as the right baseline, Origin Access Control + custom-header\n   gating, active-active multi-region split-brain on payment\n   workloads.\n\n6. Kubernetes Escape Room (fuchsia) — adversarial walk-through of\n   real cluster compromise chains: SA token recon (closed by\n   automountServiceAccountToken: false), docker.sock host-mount\n   escapes (PodSecurity restricted), hostPID/hostNetwork process\n   traversal, etcd snapshot leaks (KMS encryption-at-rest),\n   pods/exec → cluster-admin via stolen privileged SAs,\n   defence-in-depth posture against container-runtime CVEs.\n\n7. AI Infrastructure Security Game (teal) — indirect prompt\n   injection in support agents and tool-layer capability scoping,\n   model extraction via high-volume diverse queries, multi-tenant\n   vector DB isolation in shared indexes, agent tool over-scoping\n   and capability-based decomposition, free-tier inference API\n   abuse with disposable email farming, MCP server identity\n   propagation via SPIFFE workload identity.\n\nEach new game is ~250 lines (theme + intro + scenarios data); the\nshared ScenarioQuizComponent (introduced in the API Attack & Defense\ncommit) handles all the state, choice rendering, scoring, and\nresult-screen logic.\n\nWires routes for all 7 in app.routes.ts, sitemap entries\n(priority 0.8), pre-rendered HTML stubs via generate-routes.js,\nand flips the hub status from \"Coming Soon\" to \"Available\" with\nhrefs.\n\nAfter this commit, all 10 cloud-native security simulators on the\nhub are playable: Kubernetes Security, Zero Trust Network Builder,\nAPI Attack & Defense, Incident Response, Supply Chain Defense,\nService Mesh Routing, Threat Modeling, Secure Architecture,\nKubernetes Escape Room, AI Infrastructure Security.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0126dj1HZL7BMD66DmDm6DUa","tree":{"sha":"569e28322af5758028a84c1cba71b5924d377380","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/git/trees/569e28322af5758028a84c1cba71b5924d377380"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/git/commits/127ffd9b6ee9b20e59f1d12ef3c6f15c86e37705","verification":{"payload":"tree 569e28322af5758028a84c1cba71b5924d377380\nparent dde515b67ffe78168e070983ce24e7e19d01233f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1777666222 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1777666222 +0000\n\nComplete the 7 coming-soon security simulators\n\nShips every remaining cloud-native security game using the shared\nScenarioQuizComponent pattern. Each is a fully-playable scenario quiz\nwith 6 production-grade scenarios, 4 plausible choices per scenario\nwith per-choice feedback, a production-grounded explanation, and a\ncross-link to the relevant course module:\n\n1. Incident Response Simulator (red) — Falco \"shell in container\"\n   triage, lateral movement via stolen SA tokens, crypto-miner\n   indicators, Tetragon-detected container drift, audit-log\n   compromise chains, eBPF detection of memfd-based fileless attacks.\n\n2. Supply Chain Defense Simulator (green) — cosign verify without\n   certificate-identity, syft SBOMs missing Go modules