nt tool over-scoping\n   and capability-based decomposition, free-tier inference API\n   abuse with disposable email farming, MCP server identity\n   propagation via SPIFFE workload identity.\n\nEach new game is ~250 lines (theme + intro + scenarios data); the\nshared ScenarioQuizComponent (introduced in the API Attack & Defense\ncommit) handles all the state, choice rendering, scoring, and\nresult-screen logic.\n\nWires routes for all 7 in app.routes.ts, sitemap entries\n(priority 0.8), pre-rendered HTML stubs via generate-routes.js,\nand flips the hub status from \"Coming Soon\" to \"Available\" with\nhrefs.\n\nAfter this commit, all 10 cloud-native security simulators on the\nhub are playable: Kubernetes Security, Zero Trust Network Builder,\nAPI Attack & Defense, Incident Response, Supply Chain Defense,\nService Mesh Routing, Threat Modeling, Secure Architecture,\nKubernetes Escape Room, AI Infrastructure Security.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0126dj1HZL7BMD66DmDm6DUa\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDh2Hm9/\n5HjIyILExU1jlF72uJHHXTEmQGQtYk3a8ndL9PLIcyhEvm4yiUjVwP99Nhhwd/ogFEVs+3Al//O1\nqQ4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-01T20:10:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commit/127ffd9b6ee9b20e59f1d12ef3c6f15c86e37705","node_id":"C_kwDOR5J1D9oAKDEyN2ZmZDliNmVlOWIyMGU1OWYxZDEyZWYzYzZmMTVjODZlMzc3MDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commit/dde515b67ffe78168e070983ce24e7e19d01233f","sha":"dde515b67ffe78168e070983ce24e7e19d01233f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/dde515b67ffe78168e070983ce24e7e19d01233f"}],"sha":"127ffd9b6ee9b20e59f1d12ef3c6f15c86e37705","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/127ffd9b6ee9b20e59f1d12ef3c6f15c86e37705"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/dde515b67ffe78168e070983ce24e7e19d01233f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T19:46:21Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T19:46:21Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Complete the 7 coming-soon cheatsheets\n\nShips all seven previously-stubbed reference sheets with the same\nproduction-reference depth as the Kubernetes Security cheatsheet:\n\n1. SPIFFE & SPIRE — SPIFFE IDs, X.509/JWT SVIDs, registration entries,\n   Kubernetes attestor selectors, federation bundle endpoints,\n   workload-not-getting-an-SVID diagnostics.\n2. OPA & Rego — Rego language essentials, built-ins, OPA CLI\n   (eval/test/run/bench), Gatekeeper constraint workflow, bundle\n   distribution, testing patterns.\n3. API Security — JWT verification (algorithms allowlist), OAuth2/OIDC\n   patterns, security headers (HSTS/CSP/XFO/Referrer-Policy/\n   Permissions-Policy), CORS, mTLS, webhook signature verification,\n   rate-limiting that survives spoofed X-Forwarded-For.\n4. Linux Networking — ip / ss / lsof, connectivity probes,\n   tcpdump/tshark capture and analysis, openssl s_client TLS\n   diagnostics, iptables/nftables, eBPF observability (bpftrace,\n   Hubble, BCC tools).\n5. Runtime Security (Falco / eBPF) — Falco rule structure, high-signal\n   detection rules, falco/falcoctl operations, Falcosidekick routing,\n   Tetragon eBPF enforcement, the Linux syscall detection alphabet,\n   tuning out noise.\n6. Service Mesh (Istio / Envoy) — mesh-wide mTLS rollout\n   (PERMISSIVE → STRICT), AuthorizationPolicy patterns,\n   RequestAuthentication + matching AuthorizationPolicy for JWT,\n   traffic management, the istioctl proxy-config / proxy-status\n   diagnostics flow, Envoy stats and config_dump for sidecar debug.\n7. DevSecOps & Supply Chain — cosign keyless signing, SBOM generation\n   (syft, grype, trivy), SLSA provenance levels (L1–L3), image\n   admission policy with Kyverno, hardened GitHub Actions patterns\n   (workflow permissions, SHA pinning, pull_request_target risk).\n\nEach sheet has:\n- Header with topic-coloured badge and intro\n- Multiple command groups, each row optionally annotated with a \"Prod\n  tip\" or \"Warning\" callout\n- \"Common Misconfigurations\" — bad/hardened pairs with the production\n  reason they aren''t equivalent\n- \"Go Deeper\" cross-links into courses, glossary, and related games\n\nAlso extracts a reusable CheatsheetPageComponent at\nsrc/app/pages/cheatsheets/_shared/cheatsheet-page.ts so each sheet is\n~200 lines of data instead of duplicating ~330 lines of template per\nsheet. The existing Kubernetes Security and Kubernetes (kubectl)\nsheets are untouched and continue to use their own templates.\n\nWires routes for all 7 in app.routes.ts, sitemap entries (priority\n0.8), and pre-rendered HTML stubs via generate-routes.js. Hub status\nflipped from \"Coming Soon\" to \"Available\" with hrefs.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0126dj1HZL7BMD66DmDm6DUa","tree":{"sha":"00adcb8c132a4cae7f86bba40ff84d998d13ff04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/git/trees/00adcb8c132a4cae7f86bba40ff84d998d13ff04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/git/commits/dde515b67ffe78168e070983ce24e7e19d01233f","verification":{"payload":"tree 00adcb8c132a4cae7f86bba40ff84d998d13ff04\nparent 50152f769a180c705124f4a97999668dd9b6753f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1777664781 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1777664781 +0000\n\nComplete the 7 coming-soon cheatsheets\n\nShips all seven previously-stubbed reference sheets with the same\nproduction-reference depth as the Kubernetes Security cheatsheet:\n\n1. SPIFFE & SPIRE — SPIFFE IDs, X.509/JWT SVIDs, registration entries,\n   Kubernetes attestor selectors, federation bundle endpoints,\n   workload-not-getting-an-SVID diagnostics.\n2. OPA & Rego — Rego language essentials, built-ins, OPA CLI\n   (eval/test/run/bench), Gatekeeper constraint workflow, bundle\n   distribution, testing patterns.\n3. API Security — JWT verification (algorithms allowlist), OAuth2/OIDC\n   patterns, security headers (HSTS/CSP/XFO/Referrer-Policy/\n   Permissions-Policy), CORS, mTLS, webhook signature verification,\n   rate-limiting that survives spoofed X-Forwarded-For.\n4. Linux Networking — ip / ss / lsof, connectivity probes,\n   tcpdump/tshark capture and analysis, openssl s_client TLS\n   diagnostics, iptables/nftables, eBPF observability (bpftrace,\n   Hubble, BCC tools).\n5. Runtime Security (Falco / eBPF) — Falco rule structure, high-signal\n   detection rules, falco/falcoctl operations, Falcosidekick routing,\n   Tetragon eBPF enforcement, the Linux syscall detection alphabet,\n   tuning out noise.\n6. Service Mesh (Istio / Envoy) — mesh-wide mTLS rollout\n   (PERMISSIVE → STRICT), AuthorizationPolicy patterns,\n   RequestAuthentication + matching AuthorizationPolicy for JWT,\n   traffic management, the istioctl proxy-config / proxy-status\n   diagnostics flow, Envoy stats and config_dump for sidecar debug.\n7. DevSecOps & Supply Chain — cosign keyless signing, SBOM generation\n   (syft, grype, trivy), SLSA provenance levels (L1–L3), image\n   admission policy with Kyverno, hardened GitHub Actions patterns\n   (workflow permissions, SHA pinning, pull_request_target risk).\n\nEach sheet has:\n- Header with topic-coloured badge and intro\n- Multiple command groups, each row optionally annotated with a \"Prod\n  tip\" or \"Warning\" callout\n- \"Common Misconfigurations\" — bad/hardened pairs with the production\n  reason they aren''t equivalent\n- \"Go Deeper\" cross-links into courses, glossary, and related games\n\nAlso extracts a reusable CheatsheetPageComponent at\nsrc/app/pages/cheatsheets/_shared/cheatsheet-page.ts so each sheet is\n~200 lines of data instead of duplicating ~330 lines of template per\nsheet. The existing Kubernetes Security and Kubernetes (kubectl)\nsheets are untouched and continue to use their own templates.\n\nWires 