/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/commits/683dff4caf11a020fd868b3ed5743174c4a23cb0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T18:48:46Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T18:48:46Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Reposition cheatsheets as production engineering reference\n\nThe /cheatsheets section was a generic \"list of notes\" (Python,\nkubectl, Git, Docker, SQL) that diluted the cloud-native security\nbrand. This commit:\n\n1. Rebrands the hub as \"Production Engineering Reference Sheets\",\n   leading with cloud-native security & infrastructure references\n   and demoting generic syntax sheets to a clearly-labeled\n   \"Engineering Essentials\" secondary section.\n\n2. Lists 9 cloud-native security tier-1 references in the hub:\n   Kubernetes Security (NEW, available), kubectl (existing,\n   available), SPIFFE/SPIRE, OPA/Rego, API Security, Linux\n   Networking, Runtime Security, Service Mesh, DevSecOps &\n   Supply Chain — each with topic chips and a full SEO-friendly\n   description so the hub indexes for cloud-native security\n   keywords even before all 9 ship.\n\n3. Ships the first new tier-1 reference fully built: the\n   Kubernetes Security Cheatsheet at /cheatsheets/kubernetes-security.\n   Structure follows the prescribed production-reference template:\n   - H1 with intro\n   - Inline SVG diagram of the Kubernetes authorization chain\n     (Auth -> Authorization -> Admission -> etcd)\n   - 6 H2 command groups: RBAC audit, PodSecurity, NetworkPolicy,\n     Secrets, Audit/Forensics, Image Security\n   - Every command shows production tip and/or security warning\n     where the security context matters\n   - \"Try It Yourself\" section with copy-paste default-deny\n     NetworkPolicy YAML\n   - Side-by-side \"Insecure vs Hardened\" misconfiguration pairs\n     covering RBAC, securityContext, NetworkPolicy, secrets-in-env\n   - Related Tutorials & Labs cross-linking the Cloud Native\n     Security Engineering course, Kubernetes Runtime Security\n     guide, Kubernetes Security Simulator, and the glossary\n\n4. Wires up the route at /cheatsheets/kubernetes-security, adds\n   the sitemap entry, and updates the static-route generator so\n   the page ships with a real <title>, meta description, and\n   semantic HTML for crawlers.\n\n5. Existing cheatsheets (kubernetes, docker, git, sql, python)\n   keep their routes live — no SEO loss — but are repositioned\n   under \"Engineering Essentials\" with reference-style copy.\n\nBuild verified: 28.6 kB lazy chunk for the new cheatsheet.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0126dj1HZL7BMD66DmDm6DUa","tree":{"sha":"1a91a124b5522e600bec73214e81f86066618034","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/git/trees/1a91a124b5522e600bec73214e81f86066618034"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vishalanandl177/coderssecret.com/git/commits/683dff4caf11a020fd868b3ed5743174c4a23cb0","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a91a124b5522e600bec73214e81f86066618034\nparent 2fe2d0316adc971fff335901ed9d2bd164f1f93c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1777661326 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1777661326 +0000\n\nReposition cheatsheets as production engineering reference\n\nThe /cheatsheets section was a generic \"list of notes\" (Python,\nkubectl, Git, Docker, SQL) that diluted the cloud-native security\nbrand. This commit:\n\n1. Rebrands the hub as \"Production Engineering Reference Sheets\",\n   leading with cloud-native security & infrastructure references\n   and demoting generic syntax sheets to a clearly-labeled\n   \"Engineering Essentials\" secondary section.\n\n2. Lists 9 cloud-native security tier-1 references in the hub:\n   Kubernetes Security (NEW, available), kubectl (existing,\n   available), SPIFFE/SPIRE, OPA/Rego, API Security, Linux\n   Networking, Runtime Security, Service Mesh, DevSecOps &\n   Supply Chain — each with topic chips and a full SEO-friendly\n   description so the hub indexes for cloud-native security\n   keywords even before all 9 ship.\n\n3. Ships the first new tier-1 reference fully built: the\n   Kubernetes Security Cheatsheet at /cheatsheets/kubernetes-security.\n   Structure follows the prescribed production-reference template:\n   - H1 with intro\n   - Inline SVG diagram of the Kubernetes authorization chain\n     (Auth -> Authorization -> Admission -> etcd)\n   - 6 H2 command groups: RBAC audit, PodSecurity, NetworkPolicy,\n     Secrets, Audit/Forensics, Image Security\n   - Every command shows production tip and/or security warning\n     where the security context matters\n   - \"Try It Yourself\" section with copy-paste default-deny\n     NetworkPolicy YAML\n   - Side-by-side \"Insecure vs Hardened\" misconfiguration pairs\n     covering RBAC, securityContext, NetworkPolicy, secrets-in-env\n   - Related Tutorials & Labs cross-linking the Cloud Native\n     Security Engineering course, Kubernetes Runtime Security\n     guide, Kubernetes Security Simulator, and the glossary\n\n4. Wires up the route at /cheatsheets/kubernetes-security, adds\n   the sitemap entry, and updates the static-route generator so\n   the page ships with a real <title>, meta description, and\n   semantic HTML for crawlers.\n\n5. Existing cheatsheets (kubernetes, docker, git, sql, python)\n   keep their routes live — no SEO loss — but are repositioned\n   under \"Engineering Essentials\" with reference-style copy.\n\nBuild verified: 28.6 kB lazy chunk for the new cheatsheet.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0126dj1HZL7BMD66DmDm6DUa\n","reason":