canAForbes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DuncanAForbes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DuncanAForbes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DuncanAForbes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bagdock/bagdock-cli/commits/6037efa251ed09db9f7bb1b1fe64b0d04502bedc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-13T23:08:19Z","email":"daf@duncanforbes.io","name":"DuncanAForbes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-13T23:42:55Z","email":"DuncanAForbes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Duncan A Forbes"},"message":"feat: declare adapter webhooks in bagdock.json manifest [BDOK-560]\n\nPhase 1 of manifest-driven adapter install. Lets an adapter declare the\nwebhook endpoints it exposes so the operator dashboard can derive the full\nper-environment registration URL ({alias}{path}) without authors hardcoding\ndeployment hosts.\n\n- config.ts: add WebhookDeclaration { name, path, description? } and\n  optional `webhooks` array on BagdockJson.\n- validate.ts: validate the webhooks block (object shape, required name/path,\n  path must start with \"/\", unique names).\n- deploy.ts: include `webhooks` in the deploy metadata so the platform\n  mirrors the manifest into the control plane (config.webhooks), which the\n  operator-api /endpoints route reads to build per-env webhook URLs.\n\nServer side (operator-api /endpoints + dashboard Endpoints tab + Stripe\nmanifest) ships in the monorepo PR bagdock/bagdock#315.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"97ab1f9b654574f11400dd6b35363bfd59213d39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bagdock/bagdock-cli/git/trees/97ab1f9b654574f11400dd6b35363bfd59213d39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bagdock/bagdock-cli/git/commits/6037efa251ed09db9f7bb1b1fe64b0d04502bedc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verifie