t"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T18:31:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(ci): correct what the concurrency group guarantees (#300)\n\n* docs(ci): correct what the concurrency group guarantees\n\nThe comment said runs are \"queued rather than cancelled\", which reads as\na promise that every run eventually executes. GitHub''s default queue\nholds one pending run per group, so a run waiting behind another is\nreplaced when a newer one arrives — cancel-in-progress: false only\nprotects the run already in progress.\n\nThe behaviour is right either way: release-please derives the release\npull request from the commit range, so a superseded pending run would\nhave produced what the newest one produces. Only the claim was wrong.\n\n* ci: keep every release-please run in one concurrency group\n\nThe group was keyed on github.ref. The action is given no target-branch,\nso every run acts on the default branch''s release pull request — a\ndispatch launched from another branch would land in a group of its own\nand edit that pull request alongside a master run, which is the\ncollision the group exists to prevent. A constant group matches what the\nruns actually contend for.","tree":{"sha":"2ef149b4bd6cae2f10c7c597937f4b81b398a0a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/git/trees/2ef149b4bd6cae2f10c7c597937f4b81b398a0a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/git/commits/4a9648c33cc024cd67b1ae6594d12d27d4f6ff79","verification":{"payload":"tree 2ef149b4bd6cae2f10c7c597937f4b81b398a0a1\nparent 1781b3e68696dda4628da0c84badc564dddc017d\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1790015470 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790015470 +1200\n\ndocs(ci): correct what the concurrency group guarantees (#300)\n\n* docs(ci): correct what the concurrency group guarantees\n\nThe comment said runs are \"queued rather than cancelled\", which reads as\na promise that every run eventually executes. GitHub''s default queue\nholds one pending run per group, so a run waiting behind another is\nreplaced when a newer one arrives — cancel-in-progress: false only\nprotects the run already in progress.\n\nThe behaviour is right either way: release-please derives the release\npull request from the commit range, so a superseded pending run would\nhave produced what the newest one produces. Only the claim was wrong.\n\n* ci: keep every release-please run in one concurrency group\n\nThe group was keyed on github.ref. The action is given no target-branch,\nso every run acts on the default branch''s release pull request — a\ndispatch launched from another branch would land in a group of its own\nand edit that pull request alongside a master run, which is the\ncollision the group exists to prevent. A constant group matches what the\nruns actually contend for.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsXfuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtYEQAJZlh9kl6VtL7FKQgrzXnVL/\n34hSJnZ1icgSFbSxlkHE6xwqPyvuXbyKsAjQ2L6MY+WqCo4+DTsCteiPAH78q6Rl\nDCqpEeUWpyMJ56a/wb6Jssl/VtCRH/jruPXeHF9iWbPyyX7HJb8UjZNHS7eWkC7r\n+2hNhfXhvftJA52Evsqxb+VUoUemTo2pxs7TR54iObswpN7Tgks2pVaiiYlrZobd\n8frqkzCienUYzxcZGdvp4cz5RpQAWEMSF1DfZ4qKUX7ejplcX9vlLKaUvzV3LF3b\nQUmOsdjAZ055wbKWltVKRsgh91gTLVIo5KUnBNiqxfeamQc4GhwYJUbbaQabjFj3\nzQxWEzypuGd/4VaYXw8JiSmmp/Fh0kMItzKXjXtJjYUV3WLyhMjps8RE4adfLNFO\nncT7fnE32K5VvIpOa4Yn3qkTa+DtFl1trEZbk4F6C286HJLc6aKxRgocuMfeExcO\ntcUN5yxoetbUekRC/lnQVxdy7XYXhtJJG+RsID1H2xnYyj3uu33zXp1fHZ/OyhAB\nRlBTW/k+atjGX5koZx/wokWasfT5mMaLoJqhO3r2oWCckT38mFfSkcUnjRe/wg/n\ntGFNODJ3moRYOnbq12rvaqot0Lw7S1Zv0mEVFPF+vXRsk5fEO0abWTO3flQR6+Ag\n/CsuBg6rdl4OcdQvzJfS\n=wFd+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T18:31:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/we