ce61fb1db11b7c64a05efc088b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/f309a0b104f8ece61fb1db11b7c64a05efc088b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/2723be132493acc04d3567a1b87e2961cfd2d6ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T02:33:51Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T02:33:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: derive the release bump from the commit type (#298)\n\nalways-bump-patch made every release a PATCH regardless of what it\ncontained, so a feature shipped under a version that said nothing had\nbeen added. Removing the key restores release-please''s default: feat is\na minor, fix and perf a patch, and a `!` or BREAKING CHANGE footer a\nmajor.\n\nA Release-As footer still pins a specific version when the derived one\nis not what a release should carry.","tree":{"sha":"df418ff53981f731c8caefd80cbe1567130ed774","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/git/trees/df418ff53981f731c8caefd80cbe1567130ed774"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/git/commits/2723be132493acc04d3567a1b87e2961cfd2d6ec","verification":{"payload":"tree df418ff53981f731c8caefd80cbe1567130ed774\nparent 14076b6794dbc99c8d778f9cd1f7164f477660fe\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1789958031 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789958031 +1200\n\nci: derive the release bump from the commit type (#298)\n\nalways-bump-patch made every release a PATCH regardless of what it\ncontained, so a feature shipped under a version that said nothing had\nbeen added. Removing the key restores release-please''s default: feat is\na minor, fix and perf a patch, and a `!` or BREAKING CHANGE footer a\nmajor.\n\nA Release-As footer still pins a specific version when the derived one\nis not what a release should carry.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsJePCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeG4QAJ0g/WKRdY6gGkxP3KcCaWS5\nA15ZUVk5q+Y3Yl34ytCqf9ZDRLBIrcagZsntmGocyACw67h6gLtHPcFO0MfYYudx\np5wEKaeb0tUo5lo/071vc19PsMY3GtAhLZ0ms6SmI1iSj55T60tqbmuU9udK/9rb\nGMmi4UbwkJDaYqJPEJyYxUygg2CgkYU28Otcl18+MbndgOe3xcTFShX+K6+Di2C8\nu6d5R7EuNHii05yP4nKzdb3xWOEjsvJaECgcG83x0zow6gywkamx2GmotHrWoh6d\nwGC+a6paukFn1jZ+ncAOfA4x9HljVEW1RdhaV7oglOWEUDtkwrPjh8WlRoQQgFjh\nxNAFF/Cbo+lmmQxE582UiDAvSJilUfJ08FkoeFil2yZU6b5GSDcR5v4gc8+/PprL\n8+7SYff6QQGYKS68I8tG0rWblWw1ezGJV1q3OBU0y9bwZ7XM5J4b5kbBiT7Z9mzH\nqcdVxR6nNdlA0ySPIpdoZj6A1Hwsburvlxv7amoa5gameJI+oy50/h8KGDp3GA4G\ntBtYHe7GGXdmEV/CRE0pFt6sOa++34ewbxTQMtxU3Sz6FPt+ymZpbRd2UGH3JZVe\nrKvWYATag0+V138GKYN+SwKRghc9N0KpDRKJuUTXfrDK42yAn4I4cOgX1uaEMhbk\nMKMoLNN1I/RnueYtgCib\n=NjoD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T02:33:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-container/commit/2723be132493acc04d3567a1b87e2961cfd2d6ec","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yCtoAKDI3MjNiZTEzMjQ5M2FjYzA0ZDM1NjdhMWI4N2UyOTYxY2ZkMmQ2ZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-container/commit/14076b6794dbc99c8d778f9cd1f7164f477660fe","sha":"14076b6794dbc99c8d778f9cd1f7164f477660fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/14076b6794dbc99c8d778f9cd1f7164f477660fe"}],"sha":"2723be132493acc04d3567a1b87e2961cfd2d6ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/2723be132493acc04d3567a1b87e2961cfd2d6ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/14076b6794dbc99c8d778f9cd1f7164f477660fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T00:54:04Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T00:54:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: list every field that recreates a container (#297)\n\n* docs: list every field that recreates a container\n\nFive hand-maintained lists across three files named seven drift axes\nwhere the code has eleven. `devices`, `groupAdd` and `extraHosts` had\nbeen missing for some time and `capAdd` since 1.34.0, so the docs read\nas a promise that changing those fields leaves a container alone — the\nopposite of what happens.\n\nAdd a test that reads the axis names out of diffContainerConfig and\nchecks each documented list names them, scoped to the sentence that does\nthe enumerating rather than the whole file: capAdd has its own README\nsection, and a whole-file search would pass on that mention while the\ndrift list stayed wrong.\n\n* fix(test): resolve doc paths as URLs throughout\n\nfileURLToPath returns a Windows path whose drive letter the URL\nconstructor then reads as a scheme, so the test threw before asserting\nanything on the one platform it was most likely to be skipped on.\nKeeping the base as a URL avoids the round trip.\n\nAlso drop the development history from the header comment; it describes\nwhat the invariant is now.","tree":{"sha":"67b787ce52883369f5661cee1c55d71ef1986a4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/git/trees/67b787ce52883369f5661cee1c55d71ef1986a4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/git/commits/14076b6794dbc99c8d778f9cd1f7164f477660fe","verification":{"payload":"tree 67b787ce52883369f5661cee1c55d71ef1986a4d\nparent 08eb678edd3b9846805a414da8526ef7c375a230\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1789952044 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789952044 +1200\n\ndocs: list every field that recreates a container (#297)\n\n* docs: list every field that recreates a container\n\nFive hand-maintained lists across three files named seven drift axes\nwhere the code has eleven. `devices`, `groupAdd` and `extraHosts` had\nbeen missing for some time and `capAdd` since 1.34.0, so the docs read\nas a promise that changing those fields leaves a container alone — the\nopposite of what happens.\n\nAdd a test that reads the axis names out of diffContainerConfig and\nchecks each documented list names them, scoped to the sentence that does\nthe enumerating rather than the whole file: capAdd has its own README\nsection, and a whole-file search would pass on that mention while the\ndrift list stayed wrong.\n\n* fix(test): resolve doc paths as URLs throughout\n\nfileURLToPath returns a Windows path whose drive letter the URL\nconstructor then reads as a scheme, so the test threw before asserting\nanything on the one platform it was most likely to be skipped on.\nKeeping the base as a URL avoids the round trip.\n\nAlso drop the development history from the header comment; it describes\nwhat the invariant is now.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsIAsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR+MQABh8Jr28a8DiicginYg1kADb\nKxXlA2ryI/IYiru0RMgW4bIav3PgddBhopb6qBDIk2kMIyKc1VK7/m+mih6arft9\n9vv4mCCFLHCHFdFHBLv1lNn/+3srO1r5HC6KTjnfPsUYL9LWiF70rZErd6Am8/sd\nGihbaS9mZUgsYWSXuN1X+90ZjC2FPdYpT0PgsaLI6IUkqJfZ6twQMGswuBNzXUsD\n3yDm7UM97WhgRhvK7KcCny/yAF7DouOWNzXXzofO0Y3+FZLp3vc9ApFuE+wD0cSe\nGK4Kbpd/UYlkUB0yhmpCbasmWBTQou5ThNfX+FfUx+MXIhsQkXB0tMuYjnggi7+7\nDFgv5nzulvfvmpe