"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/08eb678edd3b9846805a414da8526ef7c375a230/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T00:31:54Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T00:31:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(config): add capAdd for Linux capabilities (#295)\n\n* feat(config): add capAdd for Linux capabilities\n\nSome workloads need a capability rather than a device node. Victron''s\nVenus OS container, for one, reaches its CAN interface with\n--cap-add=SYS_ADMIN and no privileged flag.\n\nNames are accepted with or without the CAP_ prefix and normalised to the\nprefixed form both runtimes report, on the requested and the live side\nalike, so drift compares capabilities rather than spelling and rewriting\none form as the other does not recreate the container.\n\nDrift is symmetric off the live container, the way groupAdd already is:\nboth runtimes report HostConfig.CapAdd and nothing else populates it, so\nremoving a capability is detected with no `prior` and survives a server\nrestart. That is the direction that matters — a container must not keep\na capability the consumer has dropped.\n\nNo `privileged` field accompanies this. That is the absence of a\nboundary rather than a capability, and if it ever proves unavoidable it\nbelongs in operator config, not in a consumer-set ContainerConfig.\n\n* test(config): cover the CapAdd inspect mapping\n\nThe create payload and the diff were covered, but not the step between\nthem. A regression in the live-side normalisation would make every\nreconciliation see drift and recreate the container, or miss a dropped\ncapability entirely.","tree":{"sha":"53a27946656e402c6947fcb2258d4870d85491ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/git/trees/53a27946656e402c6947fcb2258d4870d85491ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/git/commits/08eb678edd3b9846805a414da8526ef7c375a230","verification":{"payload":"tree 53a27946656e402c6947fcb2258d4870d85491ac\nparent 99865aeb75067e3b5905cc5b21e6fea3c7c3c3fd\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1789950714 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789950714 +1200\n\nfeat(config): add capAdd for Linux capabilities (#295)\n\n* feat(config): add capAdd for Linux capabilities\n\nSome workloads need a capability rather than a device node. Victron''s\nVenus OS container, for one, reaches its CAN interface with\n--cap-add=SYS_ADMIN and no privileged flag.\n\nNames are accepted with or without the CAP_ prefix and normalised to the\nprefixed form both runtimes report, on the requested and the live side\nalike, so drift compares capabilities rather than spelling and rewriting\none form as the other does not recreate the container.\n\nDrift is symmetric off the live container, the way groupAdd already is:\nboth runtimes report HostConfig.CapAdd and nothing else populates it, so\nremoving a capability is detected with no `prior` and survives a server\nrestart. That is the direction that matters — a container must not keep\na capability the consumer has dropped.\n\nNo `privileged` field accompanies this. That is the absence of a\nboundary rather than a capability, and if it ever proves unavoidable it\nbelongs in operator config, not in a consumer-set ContainerConfig.\n\n* test(config): cover the CapAdd inspect mapping\n\nThe create payload and the diff were covered, but not the step between\nthem. A regression in the live-side normalisation would make every\nreconciliation see drift and recreate the container, or miss a dropped\ncapability entirely.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsHr6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2Z8QABljoUE/J0H81vySuy1K7+r2\nxUMLPIKSirX0ehZTg+YjMudgS1gZ9eSyVMubrMAWJIu7ImrLpu7ekO5MXOpSzbD0\nJxopGkfkV4y5P93B7OzbqVBhy1C3NoPompT9j8LuuS2crZWyWvqcszoMmnCVw5hT\nmwJLn3/9S4zYX4rEpn39Oz7MfzU5KILOSYkI8czdjLlx04cv1DqWT1M/0LUwAD6n\nWYmRps9HlYvGAqUBJcHAS5JoSTvAJscoVw5xBmJdoWZbJgZ0fhG56WVx7CcGBMBr\nfiHCBilWxIHoAyLQ+pGFxSU773V0C9oN+ajTK18m8dFBR53lH/aQ0DHD07udqYir\nsa6zrrx9tvjYvhhYGYu+FK5HLnbz4ZHrjjc4/7qyZBZPHSLKfQgRFY/wgHqnLozI\nDeFQtdQvc/JZxDfcpfKvuGGtzwr43ok0oPfCzIl2i9zNYuKhsKn5THj0cJ2LExvj\nyDTsgTsDThSFeaFTYwuJAJURxVwtPaUbdrbmZPYqN9azkv2dvjs/wigSMU4Iw2DW\nYgnBtZ4iQmKGTFS6Oxzy4DvE1RnTS9U0lXgSUyrrC8BMW99xGhXJru/m26RJY6f8\nv/cyKv3YzCOXj95rW3f0EB3MiGN8kLmZnDNpEo1cXRqXBd+rMlVjW1Hp/d01S35A\nZ5F21wVEpBtNqM954t1v\n=5Ukh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T00:31:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-container/commit/08eb678edd3b9846805a414da8526ef7c375a230","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yCtoAKDA4ZWI2NzhlZGQzYjk4NDY4MDVhNDE0ZGE4NTI2ZWY3YzM3NWEyMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-container/commit/99865aeb75067e3b5905cc5b21e6fea3c7c3c3fd","sha":"99865aeb75067e3b5905cc5b21e6fea3c7c3c3fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/99865aeb75067e3b5905cc5b21e6fea3c7c3c3fd"}],"sha":"08eb678edd3b9846805a414da8526ef7c375a230","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/08eb678edd3b9846805a414da8526ef7c375a230"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/99865aeb75067e3b5905cc5b21e6fea3c7c3c3fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T00:30:24Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T00:30:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(notifications): alert on a crash-looping container (#293)\n\n* feat(notifications): alert on a crash-looping container\n\nA container that dies and is restarted by the runtime was\nindistinguishable from one the operator stopped: both reported a bare\n\"stopped\", and no notification fired. The consumer health-check poll\ncannot cover this case at all, since a container dying during startup\nnever reaches the state where a health check could run.\n\nRaise `notifications.container.<name>.crashLooping` from the RATE of\nchange of the restart count rather than its value. The runtime reports\nonly a lifetime total, which is legitimately non-zero on a healthy\ncontainer under `--restart=unless-stopped` that has survived a host\nreboot; a threshold on the raw number would alert on uptime instead of\nfailure. `observeRestarts` keeps a per-container baseline and raises\nonly on three restarts inside five minutes, so the first observation of\na container never alerts, a decreasing count re-baselines after a\nrecreate, and a raise advances the window so the alert cannot outlive\nthe loop.\n\nOne shared sweep over the managed set drives it, not a per-container\ntimer: each sample is a single inspect, and the condition applies to\nevery managed container whether or not a consumer supplied a health\ncheck.\n\n* fix(notifications): slide the crash-loop window\n\nThe tumbling window split a burst that straddled its boundary: one\nrestart before the reset and two after it are three restarts inside two\nminutes, and produced no alert at all — the exact failure the feature\nexists to catch. Hold timestamped samples and measure against the oldest\none still inside the window instead, so any five-minute span counts.\n\nPruning deliberately keeps the newest sample that has already aged out.\nIt is the only record of what the count was when the window opened, and\ndropping it would understate the delta across a stalled poll.\n\nRetire an in-flight sweep whose generation no longer matches. An inspect\ncan resolve after stop() has reset the emitter, and recording against\nthe dropped history would seed the next start with counts from before\nthe restart.\n\nThe clear contract in the README described a rule the code never\nimplemented: the alert clears when the rate falls back below the\nthreshold, which can happen while restarts are still occurring.\n\n* fix(notifications): re-anchor when the crash-loop poll stalls\n\nTwo observations six minutes apart with three restarts between them were\nreported as a five-minute crash loop. The restarts are real but\nundatable — they may have been evenly spread — so charging them to the\nlast five minutes alerts on a rate that was never observed, which is the\nerror reading a raw lifetime count makes and the reason this is\nrate-derived at all. When nothing was sampled inside the window, take a\nfresh anchor and wait for evidence from a window actually watched.\n\nA container removed directly through the runtime never reaches\nafterContainerRemoved, so its alert and restart history outlived it.\nDrop both from the poll. The new forgetRestarts does only that, unlike\nforgetContainer, which also resets health and device-issue tracking that\na polling path has no business touching.\n\nExtract the sweep as sweepRestartsOnce with injected dependencies, the\nway SelfHealthOwnership was extracted, so failure isolation,\nretire-on-stop, vanished containers and set snapshotting are covered at\nthe function boundary rather than only through a live plugin.\n\n* fix(notifications): keep a retired sweep from freeing the poll guard\n\nstop() clears the in-flight flag, so a sweep still awaiting an inspect\ncould clear it a second time after a new lifecycle had armed its own\nsweep and set it — letting the next tick run two sweeps concurrently\nagainst the same sample history. Release the guard only from the\ngeneration that took it.\n\nAlso document when the device notification clears, and cut the\ncrash-loop section back to its invariants: the pruning and polling steps\nit spelled out duplicate the source and would drift from it.\n\n* fix(notifications): treat a gap of exactly the window as observed\n\nA sample landing precisely on the window''s edge is an observation of\nthat window, not a gap past it, so the re-anchor test takes the gap as\nstrictly greater than the window rather than equal to it.\n\n* fix(notifications): discard a sweep result for a removed container\n\nA container removed while its inspect was in flight had the old\ncontainer''s lifetime count written back into a history that removal had\njust dropped. A replacement taking the same name then inherited it, and\nthe next sample compared two different container identities — a jump\nlarge enough to raise a crash loop that never happened.\n\nStamp each observation with the container''s restart epoch, bumped\nwherever its history is dropped, and ignore one that arrives against a\nsuperseded epoch. Keeping the check in the emitter means every path that\ndrops history invalidates in-flight observations, not only the poll.\n\nAlso drop the README''s \"visual only, no audible alarm\" claim: the\nemitter deliberately omits `method`, so presentation is the\nNotificationManager''s to decide, not ours to promise.\n\n* fix(notifications): epoch-guard the missing branch too\n\nThe epoch check sat on the observe path only, so a stale `missing` that\narrived after the container had been replaced under the same name still\ndeleted the replacement''s restart history and cleared its alert. Check\nthe epoch once before branching, so a result for a container that no\nlonger exists is dropped whatever it says.","tree":{"sha":"e25aa14be8af33572febb3cd241b19b60ef63b98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/git/trees/e25aa14be8af33572febb3cd241b19b60ef63b98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/git/commits/99865aeb75067e3b5905cc5b21e6fea3c7c3c3fd","verification":{"payload":"tree e25aa14be8af33572febb3cd241b19b60ef63b98\nparent e6ecee93c8ad474c832ca7e10e8d895356e009e8\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1789950624 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789950624 +1200\n\nfeat(notifications): alert on a crash-looping container (#293)\n\n* feat(notifications): alert on a crash-looping container\n\nA container that dies and is restarted by the runtime was\nindistinguishable from one the operator stopped: both reported a bare\n\"stopped\", and no notification fired. The consumer health-check poll\ncannot cover this case at all, since a container dying during startup\nnever reaches the state where a health check could run.\n\nRaise `notifications.container.<name>.crashLooping` from the RATE of\nchange of the restart count rather than its value. The runtime reports\nonly a lifetime total, which is legitimately non-zero on a healthy\ncontainer under `--restart=unless-stopped` that has survived a host\nreboot; a threshold on the raw number would alert on uptime instead of\nfailure. `observeRestarts` keeps a per-container baseline and raises\nonly on three restarts inside five minutes, so the first observation of\na container never alerts, a decreasing count re-baselines after a\nrecreate, and a raise advances the window so the alert cannot outlive\nthe loop.\n\nOne shared sweep over the managed set drives it, not a per-container\ntimer: each sample is a single inspect, and the condition applies to\nevery managed container whether or not a consumer supplied a health\ncheck.\n\n* fix(notifications): slide the crash-loop window\n\nThe tumbling window split a burst that straddled its boundary: one\nrestart before the reset and two after it are three restarts inside two\nminutes, and produced no alert at all — the exact failure the feature\nexists to catch. Hold timestamped samples and measure against the oldest\none still inside the window instead, so any five-minute span counts.\n\nPruning deliberately keeps the newest sample that has already aged out.\nIt is the only record of what the count was when the window opened, and\ndropping it would understate the delta across a stalled poll.\n\nRetire an in-flight sweep whose generation no longer matches. An inspect\ncan resolve after stop() has reset the emitter, and recording against\nthe dropped history would seed the next start with counts from before\nthe restart.\n\nThe clear contract in the README described a rule the code never\nimplemented: the alert clears when the rate falls back below the\nthreshold, which can happen while restarts are still occurring.\n\n* fix(notifications): re-anchor when the crash-loop poll stalls\n\nTwo observations six minutes apart with three restarts between them were\nreported as a five-minute crash loop. The restarts are real but\nundatable — they may have been evenly spread — so charging them to the\nlast five minutes alerts on a rate that was never observed, which is the\nerror reading a raw lifetime count makes and the reason this is\nrate-derived at all. When nothing was sampled inside the window, take a\nfresh anchor and wait for evidence from a window actually watched.\n\nA container removed directly through the runtime never reaches\nafterContainerRemoved, so its alert and restart history outlived it.\nDrop both from the poll. The new forgetRestarts does only that, unlike\nforgetContainer, which also resets health and device-issue tracking that\na polling path has no business touching.\n\nExtract the sweep as sweepRestartsOnce with injected dependencies, the\nway SelfHealthOwnership was extracted, so failure isolation,\nretire-on-stop, vanished containers and set snapshotting are covered at\nthe function boundary rather than only through a live plugin.\n\n* fix(notifications): keep a retired sweep from freeing the poll guard\n\nstop() clears the in-flight flag, so a sweep still awaiting an inspect\ncould clear it a second time after a new lifecycle had armed its own\nsweep and set it — letting the next tick run two sweeps concurrently\nagainst the same sample history. Release the guard only from the\ngeneration that took it.\n\nAlso document when the device notification clears, and cut the\ncrash-loop section back to its invariants: the pruning and polling steps\nit spelled out duplicate the source and would drift from it.\n\n* fix(notifications): treat a gap of exactly the window as observed\n\nA sample landing precisely on the window''s edge is an observation of\nthat window, not a gap past it, so the re-anchor test takes the gap as\nstrictly greater than the window rather than equal to it.\n\n* fix(notifications): discard a sweep result for a removed container\n\nA container removed while its inspect was in flight had the old\ncontainer''s lifetime count written back into a history that removal had\njust dropped. A replacement taking the same name then inherited it, and\nthe next sample compared two different container identities — a jump\nlarge enough to raise a crash loop that never happened.\n\nStamp each observation with the container''s restart epoch, bumped\nwherever its history is dropped, and ignore one that arrives against a\nsuperseded epoch. Keeping the check in the emitter means every path that\ndrops history invalidates in-flight observations, not only the poll.\n\nAlso drop the README''s \"visual only, no audible alarm\" claim: the\nemitter deliberately omits `method`, so presentation is the\nNotificationManager''s to decide, not ours to promise.\n\n* fix(notifications): epoch-guard the missing branch too\n\nThe epoch check sat on the observe path only, so a stale `missing` that\narrived after the container had been replaced under the same name still\ndeleted the replacement''s restart history and cleared its alert. Check\nthe epoch once before branching, so a result for a container that no\nlonger exists is dropped whatever it says.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsHqgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7kYQAIEyoIKt9J7ZrQ+XG3WikEmk\nA54rQ7B3ycBxucmHK7bd0TNFjVqsj47J1cboKejvapgH1kSOL9ineRoswkYH1v5i\nmXZJRNjNH3hAh3J8dMOLhr1t1YtByMWMvmfmLj4MsTO7/EUiop23fIe2ydsrQuom\n3F/U7AcPq6qbXGA6AZpnSM87ADdvd3oRJGqmVvWSj3IQOicwOzsovyvO+TRdb9t5\nn616bSjA+ouNmEfXhP+6c5gPlBW2dZdpJ+3ZjSZnWqNxkCRv8zn6EqqvThcRe6Pl\n5E9eUxBDVawmGWkPklPDWW8Kdl56+MHNcWvX5ku6MRKPzyT6KD+vFupf2eq7KIko\nfY+SXdwLOEFS0ukg0eEvIt+N+3sfVbHjiOWgSIkSV0qI7giJ/BqifOmvL2aKHVyW\nHsrQ1fMyI2Z/f2jytU1t2KnuQ5dsP1Lbh4ji9C3mM1Q3FHqmZhSKtvY8V/BtdxGr\nXwjKZc1t3BsY4/+AGy5pGquQLjjCFO9K71Vp2Qc5UdBCrMT0v+faH3FpHFhDEAh5\njcFya8XtZt9mkCcIcYLUVbdyfqLvJAorfQW43zj+6SgbL+ju1lP+XuEB5iI2PG7b\nXOxQNtRZVadsIvy67E3JYPDue2nBStdE4qPe8fvDqsVdSbPoAEwbes1T8O0DpD8S\n9GEoCEmuUT6vrmb1ACUO\n=eoFO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T00:30:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-container/commit/99865aeb75067e3b5905cc5b21e6fea3c7c3c3fd","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yCtoAKDk5ODY1YWViNzUwNjdlM2I1OTA1Y2M1YjIxZTZmZWEzYzdjM2MzZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-container/commit/e6ecee93c8ad474c832ca7e10e8d895356e009e8","sha":"e6ecee93c8ad474c832ca7e10e8d895356e009e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/e6ecee93c8ad474c832ca7e10e8d895356e009e8"}],"sha":"99865aeb75067e3b5905cc5b21e6fea3c7c3c3fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/99865aeb75067e3b5905cc5b21e6fea3c7c3c3fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/e6ecee93c8ad474c832ca7e10e8d895356e009e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T00:28:08Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T00:28:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(configpanel): type the host React shims (#294)\n\nhost-shim/types.d.ts declares the federation globals by augmenting\n`interface Window`, but the four shims read them off `globalThis`. Those\nare different types — a Window augmentation does not reach\n`globalThis.X` — so the declaration never applied and each `host` was\nimplicitly `any`. The `const r: typeof ReactNS = host` annotation then\naccepted it silently, leaving the typed contract the .d.ts exists to\nenforce unenforced.\n\nThe shims now read `window`, which is what signalk-server''s\nbootstrap.tsx assigns and what the declaration and the error messages\nalready described. In a browser `globalThis` is the same object, so the\nemitted bundle behaves identically — it reads window.__SK_REACT__ either\nway.\n\nThe root tsconfig excludes src/configpanel so `tsc` does not emit a\nstale dist/configpanel/, and vite transpiles without typechecking, so\nnothing checked these files and the mismatch accumulated unseen. A\ntsconfig for the panel now carries the DOM and JSX settings that must\nnot leak into the server compile, and `npm run typecheck:panel` runs it\nbetween the server build and the vite build. Reverting one shim to\n`globalThis` makes it fail with the TS7017 it should.","tree":{"sha":"fe383a23485a8653f9319e5ee97710f9316fe735","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/git/trees/fe383a23485a8653f9319e5ee97710f9316fe735"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/git/commits/e6ecee93c8ad474c832ca7e10e8d895356e009e8","verification":{"payload":"tree fe383a23485a8653f9319e5ee97710f9316fe735\nparent d0d5ae040edc229b18f416a1b1661b1d78d85902\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1789950488 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789950488 +1200\n\nfix(configpanel): type the host React shims (#294)\n\nhost-shim/types.d.ts declares the federation globals by augmenting\n`interface Window`, but the four shims read them off `globalThis`. Those\nare different types — a Window augmentation does not reach\n`globalThis.X` — so the declaration never applied and each `host` was\nimplicitly `any`. The `const r: typeof ReactNS = host` annotation then\naccepted it silently, leaving the typed contract the .d.ts exists to\nenforce unenforced.\n\nThe shims now read `window`, which is what signalk-server''s\nbootstrap.tsx assigns and what the declaration and the error messages\nalready described. In a browser `globalThis` is the same object, so the\nemitted bundle behaves identically — it reads window.__SK_REACT__ either\nway.\n\nThe root tsconfig excludes src/configpanel so `tsc` does not emit a\nstale dist/configpanel/, and vite transpiles without typechecking, so\nnothing checked these files and the mismatch accumulated unseen. A\ntsconfig for the panel now carries the DOM and JSX settings that must\nnot leak into the server compile, and `npm run typecheck:panel` runs it\nbetween the server build and the vite build. Reverting one shim to\n`globalThis` makes it fail with the TS7017 it should.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsHoYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADBwQAFvWTQr4qqvFFplIoUmYLyGS\nnHjTVrEzPpiPIzFY51d1hRuOt5Q0qlGfZR1HmLjznujYv0lbwlbC7Re0ODMzCSYz\n5W49FbxNmJmhbDxEub8aIMi8Alid9lnS9WQlvFnNndn0itKgyWRQM1UPlhOvOP8H\nbC6LkdG4lwFOmox4+xE4t7aAtfSvpcXTDgblYneYfzcj1d06qnHdVMjY5XqkOV4R\n+FrCOtXZIR9cG0HHinPTBczR+XSiUzj3vWGK8LQ9lFFtHR8gQzIUP+FNq+BkJaxW\npebePXDoJzB8WeFbiRNiMB5OGkDFhSZK4xT6WIqU7MjinURnQfiV5elaM7f28rRl\nvdUqnanQ53/qFkUCpWqcJhtjkykdxxah4u5B58RD0Wl+WWRbh18W403MQFlsCLa4\n8Edl0Tk4/7oL1UL8P9SexFN2NJfd5aGnSuQwzPvUflb4pHJtn1mDf/TjSyXeXsiZ\nJgLoW873sDL4yj/Dyugask8GBJG2kGxfDTLeWWR7wpFPRWyKXCoOc074jKZZbUt2\noQ31Mrmq4z19yjsrUeTzgaOXnQjFdCsviaWy7fwQWZ2c6ulfSG14Aj25Tc8WUjlu\nCJOj8iTHSlXnHujaioOueYAJkqBItwrfzEnusYGUpchoxirHYDk2WQgkOODbrebg\nSpTorMEzDgtIcmtpuOQi\n=ShMF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T00:28:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-container/commit/e6ecee93c8ad474c832ca7e10e8d895356e009e8","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yCtoAKGU2ZWNlZTkzYzhhZDQ3NGM4MzJjYTdlMTBlOGQ4OTUzNTZlMDA5ZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-container/commit/d0d5ae040edc229b18f416a1b1661b1d78d85902","sha":"d0d5ae040edc229b18f416a1b1661b1d78d85902","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/d0d5ae040edc229b18f416a1b1661b1d78d85902"}],"sha":"e6ecee93c8ad474c832ca7e10e8d895356e009e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/e6ecee93c8ad474c832ca7e10e8d895356e009e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/commits/d0d5ae040edc229b18f416a1b1661b1d78d85902/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T23:32:53Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T23:32:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: adopt release-please with label-driven notes (#292)\n\nPorts the signalk-questdb release setup, as merged in signalk-updater\n#71 and signalk-doctor #58. Merging to master opens a \"chore: release\nX.Y.Z\" PR; merging that creates the tag and the GitHub release, then\ndispatches publish.yml on the tag to publish to npm.\n\nversioning is always-bump-patch, so every release is a PATCH bump\nregardless of commit type; anything else goes through a Release-As\nfooter. changelog-type is github, which is what produces the\n\"by @author\" lines — include-commit-authors is a no-op upstream. No\nCHANGELOG.md is kept (skip-changelog): prettier fails on the generated\none and CI does not run on the release PR to show it.\n\nA gate job fronts release-please. GitHub''s generated notes are never\nempty, so release-please''s \"no user-facing commits\" skip never fires and\na lone docs or ci merge would otherwise propose a release. The gate lets\na push through only when it carries a commit users get.\n\nlabel-by-title.yml labels each PR from its conventional-commit type and\nrelease.yml, which already sorted by label, gains the two autorelease\nexcludes so the release PR does not list itself. dependabot now emits\nbuild(deps) for runtime bumps and ci(deps) for actions, which is the\ndistinction the gate reads.\n\npublish.yml already had workflow_dispatch, which is how release-please\nreaches it: a tag pushed with GITHUB_TOKEN starts no workflow, and npm\ntrusted publishing is bound to this filename. Its release job is now\npre-release-only, since release-please creates the GitHub release for a\nreal version and a second attempt would collide with it, and publish\ndrops needs: release so a real release still publishes when that job is\nskipped.\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md is new, matching the other plugins. The AGENTS.md\nrelease flow described tagging by hand, which release-please replaces,\nand its semver table implied the bump follows the commit type, which\nalways-bump-patch overrides.","tree":{"sha":"b010985745cb4baa2a5db0c345f78c2f73fbe22a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/git/trees/b010985745cb4baa2a5db0c345f78c2f73fbe22a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-container/git/commits/d0d5ae040edc229b18f416a1b1661b1d78d85902","verification":{"payload":"tree b010985745cb4baa2a5db0c345f78c2f73fbe22a\nparent 9fdbb27f972edd36b4a18ee1766c81c12d1739f0\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1789947173 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789947173 +1200\n\nci: adopt release-please with label-driven notes (#292)\n\nPorts the signalk-questdb release setup, as merged in signalk-updater\n#71 and signalk-doctor #58. Merging to master opens a \"chore: release\nX.Y.Z\" PR; merging that creates the tag and the GitHub release, then\ndispatches publish.yml on the tag to publish to npm.\n\nversioning is always-bump-patch, so every release is a PATCH bump\nregardless of commit type; anything else goes through a Release-As\nfooter. changelog-type is github, which is what produces the\n\"by @author\" lines — include-commit-authors is a no-op upstream. No\nCHANGELOG.md is kept (skip-changelog): prettier fails on the generated\none and CI does not run on the release PR to show it.\n\nA gate job fronts release-please. GitHub''s generated notes are never\nempty, so release-please''s \"no user-facing commits\" skip never fires and\na lone docs or ci merge would otherwise propose a release. The gate lets\na push through only when it carries a commit users get.\n\nlabel-by-title.yml labels each PR from its conventional-commit type and\nrelease.yml, which already sorted by label, gains the two autorelease\nexcludes so the release PR does not list itself. dependabot now emits\nbuild(deps) for runtime bumps and ci(deps) for actions, which is the\ndistinction the gate reads.\n\npublish.yml already had workflow_dispatch, which is how release-please\nreaches it: a tag pushed with GITHUB_TOKEN starts no workflow, and npm\ntrusted publishing is bound to this filename. Its release job is now\npre-release-only, since release-please creates the GitHub release for a\nreal version and a second attempt would collide with it, and publish\ndrops needs: release so a real release still publishes when that job is\nskipped.\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md is new, matching the other plugins. The AGENTS.md\nrelease flow described tagging by hand, which release-please replaces,\nand its semver table implied the bump follows the commit type, which\nalways-bump-patch overrides.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsG0lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWMIQAFUCshc6QVS1IwjrcEX2ekxN\nQyQkKk51Rc63uXLWpxF72hVhgPB2BUw6YdndBzD6x3VgX/xrNkp8o0KpZjBbNkBY\nWChucYcYQM1ZkP8447vYaug0AO55Xkv3B1QgNJidirN1hEBp7dkDP+Ax8IVnC1XB\nY9c1jkI4WWZpYzfAkFTzuFZvt/SaISvcm8NCzDwTBWHHBu91I8m1yQzJh157RnoH\n9RpW3HFUzuzvJonS32LzGbazhkU3aodHjX7jtzscAlMDruXgPCvRic9VWctwh3Tn\nTyDPxDuU/TMO6zJRfWq7pnoTKmBaYu97Q9OPistvA1I0uDgea9WKggWzzGGrYc1Z\nm1P9E1l0FvzpOEX47ttnBZzOPavCZAX/enzAhl2zS02AlItjz2CNHhME460oPkzk\nqgGfiJ881H7UYIRGXSZA5