rred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/9405a980b34f20cd2f554e2c65c019b29f92cffc","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKDk0MDVhOTgwYjM0ZjIwY2QyZjU1NGUyYzY1YzAxOWIyOWY5MmNmZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/78735fcceef71bb21819815444282f326bb3ae8f","sha":"78735fcceef71bb21819815444282f326bb3ae8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/78735fcceef71bb21819815444282f326bb3ae8f"}],"sha":"9405a980b34f20cd2f554e2c65c019b29f92cffc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/9405a980b34f20cd2f554e2c65c019b29f92cffc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/78735fcceef71bb21819815444282f326bb3ae8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:43:02Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:43:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(recording): write an unchanged value only once per heartbeat (#207)\n\n* feat(history): hold an unchanged value across empty buckets\n\nA bucket with no row is filled with the last sample before it, for up\nto holdMs, in every aggregate: every aggregate of a steady value is that\nvalue. The first buckets of a range are held from the last row just\nbefore it, fetched only when the range opens on an empty bucket. Past\nholdMs a bucket stays null, so a sensor gone stale or a stopped\nrecorder still shows as a gap. holdMs defaults to 0, which changes\nnothing.\n\nEvery SAMPLE BY now runs FROM the range start TO its end. Without it,\nFILL(NULL) only fills between the first and last bucket that has a row,\nso leading and trailing empty buckets were missing from the response —\nverified against QuestDB 9.4.3. Buckets align to the range start\nrather than the calendar, and middle_index floors from the same start.\nThat syntax needs QuestDB 8.1, now listed as a requirement.\n\n* feat(recording): write an unchanged value only once per heartbeat\n\nMost paths hold one value from sample to sample, and the throttle wrote\neach of them at the sampling rate forever. A value equal to the last\none written for its path, context and source is now skipped until the\nunchanged-value heartbeat (default 300 s) is due. A change is written\nas it arrives, subject to the sampling rate; the gate runs before the\nthrottle so a repeat never takes a change''s throttle slot.\n\nA stale path arrives as null: the gate forgets it and its leaves, so\nthe first reading after the gap is written even when it equals the one\nbefore it. Dropped writer lines clear the gate. navigation.position is\nnever gated. The history provider holds values for twice the heartbeat.\n0 turns it off; a config saved before the option gets the default.\n\n* docs: explain change-only recording and held buckets\n\nThe heartbeat setting, what readers see between rows — the History\nAPI''s hold, stale data, direct SQL with FILL(PREV), row-weighted\naverages, startup restore — the History API''s bucket grid, and the\nQuestDB 8.1 requirement.\n\n* fix(history): measure the hold from the sample, and never past now\n\nThe hold was measured from the start of the bucket the last sample fell\nin. At a resolution near the hold, a sample late in its bucket counted\nas a whole bucket older than it was: with 10-minute buckets and a\n10-minute hold, a value one second old showed as a gap. Every bucket\nread now also selects last(ts), and the seed carries its own ts, so\nthe hold runs from when the sample was taken.\n\nA held value says the value had not changed, which nothing can say about\na time still to come, so a bucket starting after now is left empty.","tree":{"sha":"6d593fa9fe5ffeaf24992686e5c1fe0d932d74bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/6d593fa9fe5ffeaf24992686e5c1fe0d932d74bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/78735fcceef71bb21819815444282f326bb3ae8f","verification":{"payload":"tree 6d593fa9fe5ffeaf24992686e5c1fe0d932d74bd\nparent 68916575a60cd611444e086bc694d589ac26cf46\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1790275382 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790275382 +1200\n\nfeat(recording): write an unchanged value only once per heartbeat (#207)\n\n* feat(history): hold an unchanged value across empty buckets\n\nA bucket with no row is filled with the last sample before it, for up\nto holdMs, in every aggregate: every aggregate of a steady value is that\nvalue. The first buckets of a range are held from the last row just\nbefore it, fetched only when the range opens on an empty bucket. Past\nholdMs a bucket stays null, so a sensor gone stale or a stopped\nrecorder still shows as a gap. holdMs defaults to 0, which changes\nnothing.\n\nEvery SAMPLE BY now runs FROM the range start TO its end. Without it,\nFILL(NULL) only fills between the first and last bucket that has a row,\nso leading and trailing empty buckets were missing from the response —\nverified against QuestDB 9.4.3. Buckets align to the range start\nrather than the calendar, and middle_index floors from the same start.\nThat syntax needs QuestDB 8.1, now listed as a requirement.\n\n* feat(recording): write an unchanged value only once per heartbeat\n\nMost paths hold one value from sample to sample, and the throttle wrote\neach of them at the sampling rate forever. A value equal to the last\none written for its path, context and source is now skipped until the\nunchanged-value heartbeat (default 300 s) is due. A change is written\nas it arrives, subject to the sampling rate; the gate runs before the\nthrottle so a repeat never takes a change''s throttle slot.\n\nA stale path arrives as null: the gate forgets it and its leaves, so\nthe first reading after the gap is written even when it equals the one\nbefore it. Dropped writer lines clear the gate. navigation.position is\nnever gated. The history provider holds values for twice the heartbeat.\n0 turns it off; a config saved before the option gets the default.\n\n* docs: explain change-only recording and held buckets\n\nThe heartbeat setting, what readers see between rows — the History\nAPI''s hold, stale data, direct SQL with FILL(PREV), row-weighted\naverages, startup restore — the History API''s bucket grid, and the\nQuestDB 8.1 requirement.\n\n* fix(history): measure the hold from the sample, and never past now\n\nThe hold was measured from the start of the bucket the last sample fell\nin. At a resolution near the hold, a sample late in its bucket counted\nas a whole bucket older than it was: with 10-minute buckets and a\n10-minute hold, a value one second old showed as a gap. Every bucket\nread now also selects last(ts), and the seed carries its own ts, so\nthe hold runs from when the sample was taken.\n\nA held value says the value had not changed, which nothing can say about\na time still to come, so a bucket starting after now is left empty.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtW82CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMWMQAEvPwxsWTYsR0fMwzpsCjmlE\n0YdqBpIdQvjguVbQ20x5YT8JfwEifUXK5JN+P9lJvJZFAfnCEVCn8IO3AdYete1Z\n1IWTTMPWXGr2QBeiAE+dpuZYv53ApJcMVsz3WuHIx1Hg9GOyy/NaTp3ba+jw4l9l\n+ANey4tU9iLTLD1VcrERSdPtYpIZMipeUxN0YqMuMXBqZQah37ccGm62Mq9hwuSa\nE1xxCyvQByIqfKuy6SQcKWlRK4Rt1QWkY2LEE+N0jiATKoJrUBZoBK0LoF2u0CuS\nITmYmGFgIqdfhwA2T+jejMx1ASdSWKL651YMDBepitDXQDI8BglhMR6RuJEG4kjx\nCc8nB9w59+dYCW82moDjGwVQ6bQVzTg2KdXHN2e9RxvZ8ZIDWtTkThqa0G9e/grU\n8VBPAXUyacUbtMDguLXnT1k+7FR5YIQcCFKvE80k6Z4F7R+8WT+2gZ0O4tj/h4t8\nj/Fj2sWCwAcWYnYvFoqv0Qxg1rCgPSs9g//6LmEoZD3XXBptIjR8EFVSJhhK2pL8\nB/9QxiKDgyeWZTZsYqkV54uFb5fvSIT/sWQxM3GbT5XZqlJGg7meYOriZClPsPd0\nOSjZWjHrWTbVP5FDDyVjEGQJkxH1h5kNn5VLn7e+kjeuVQMa4/z0KvF3E1o0YD06\n1GB2C9a4qFydq55aFkBo\n=Z45h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T18:43:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/78735fcceef71bb21819815444282f326bb3ae8f","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKDc4NzM1ZmNjZWVmNzFiYjIxODE5ODE1NDQ0MjgyZjMyNmJiM2FlOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/68916575a60cd611444e086bc694d589ac26cf46","sha":"68916575a60cd611444e086bc694d589ac26cf46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/68916575a60cd611444e086bc694d589ac26cf46"}],"sha":"78735fcceef71bb21819815444282f326bb3ae8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/78735fcceef71bb21819815444282f326bb3ae8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/68916575a60cd611444e086bc694d589ac26cf46/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:22:16Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:22:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: derive the release bump from the commit type (#202)\n\nalways-bump-patch made every release a PATCH regardless of what it\ncontained, so a feature shipped under a version that said nothing had\nbeen added. Removing the key restores release-please''s default: feat is\na minor, fix and perf a patch, and a `!` or BREAKING CHANGE footer a\nmajor.\n\nA Release-As footer still pins a specific version when the derived one\nis not what a release should carry.","tree":{"sha":"2f3318cbb16323e4ae4a5d391492da52b05a3958","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/2f3318cbb16323e4ae4a5d391492da52b05a3958"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/68916575a60cd611444e086bc694d589ac26cf46","verification":{"payload":"tree 2f3318cbb16323e4ae4a5d391492da52b05a3958\nparent 2ad9e9306629dbd793b103b334d4910970eb9839\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1790274136 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790274136 +1200\n\nci: derive the release bump from the commit type (#202)\n\nalways-bump-patch made every release a PATCH regardless of what it\ncontained, so a feature shipped under a version that said nothing had\nbeen added. Removing the key restores release-please''s default: feat is\na minor, fix and perf a patch, and a `!` or BREAKING CHANGE footer a\nmajor.\n\nA Release-As footer still pins a specific version when the derived one\nis not what a release should carry.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtWpYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+dwQACTqT56pSs/8ygJEVbi/Cedf\nKnwN7iN2i1M9yocEKj5GYDysWSKhDdfVa5sx1HyfZghbIffuxvkMJXyiitI2EAxI\nYRA/Jk00HqgNspgPks8IS3fO8YDV72mGEoAIgcW4WQHWZ1AaNo1CNXPyBefGk8WY\n0Sbstj1xwX7o5SBkC02Ny0cro/ZvuDoox91AJVdLOXLFYmvWjNWLg+jSez+jwkn5\nlRikCDtWlKAxRaCnjIXOeL00FRX1bz8vFoqV7bw5ZleyCEYrW4XD5xhxi1rImtR3\nCWAVt96rtZk/RadKGySk2jJocuE0dwR2mIyfCf058GontsNQR3dj1WN/Gc8PIoir\nA7IYo8xW+j9MRnVfdh9VaTLECkPkfy74lLpN8uheQlAFDvG9kl3umMRAPsZ7lp0m\nxHw1YxTt8rWwWl4h7Y8AkkDBwbQA+jyeZkqZzeE0PCTRPsCRLOJM+ZOa5iyV/KOD\nyXvtPd6a4ESL59WG/NbotNSLMZU3TbcNnMADPMg6yKa+6WDJ989VkBQEIbRGyLuY\nccbZ4cMtg/nWdewjY0DHeTIj3DqK5RuKssZ2DRVqGTcDiZPFkaaMUgk1sep9drR/\nx2xmvLUjg98XFG0Q+hhSAnaGt9G0sWb//Di67xfZUhNjgOqnDdfng5vqcb129ex/\nTyg2AUU0I2VT1zahWocG\n=8wQn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T18:22:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/68916575a60cd611444e086bc694d589ac26cf46","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKDY4OTE2NTc1YTYwY2Q2MTE0NDRlMDg2YmM2OTRkNTg5YWMyNmNmNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/2ad9e9306629dbd793b103b334d4910970eb9839","sha":"2ad9e9306629dbd793b103b334d4910970eb9839","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/2ad9e9306629dbd793b103b334d4910970eb9839"}],"sha":"68916575a60cd611444e086bc694d589ac26cf46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/68916575a60cd611444e086bc694d589ac26cf46"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/2ad9e9306629dbd793b103b334d4910970eb9839/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T17:27:01Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T17:27:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(recording): drop the NMEA 2000 AC power no-data marker (#205)\n\nThe AC power fields of PGNs 65007–65029 carry a -2e9 W offset, and\ncanboat marks them signed. canboatjs reads a device''s \"no data\"\n(0xFFFFFFFF) as -1, misses the signed no-data check, and adds the\noffset, so the stream carries -2000000001 W. n2k-signalk then scales\napparent power by the power factor. A few of these on device start-up\ndominate every min and average over the path.\n\nReal and reactive power below the -2e9 floor cannot have been encoded\nand are dropped; negative exported power is untouched. Apparent power\nis a magnitude, so any negative value is the marker, however it was\nscaled — a floor test would miss it for a power factor below 1.\nDropped values are skipped and reported like NaN.","tree":{"sha":"eba90e9559e443659250467d62e646b324b7c3ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/eba90e9559e443659250467d62e646b324b7c3ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/2ad9e9306629dbd793b103b334d4910970eb9839","verification":{"payload":"tree eba90e9559e443659250467d62e646b324b7c3ae\nparent c02517ae6e93d2aff738fa7e5f7245212363a7ec\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1790270821 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790270821 +1200\n\nfix(recording): drop the NMEA 2000 AC power no-data marker (#205)\n\nThe AC power fields of PGNs 65007–65029 carry a -2e9 W offset, and\ncanboat marks them signed. canboatjs reads a device''s \"no data\"\n(0xFFFFFFFF) as -1, misses the signed no-data check, and adds the\noffset, so the stream carries -2000000001 W. n2k-signalk then scales\napparent power by the power factor. A few of these on device start-up\ndominate every min and average over the path.\n\nReal and reactive power below the -2e9 floor cannot have been encoded\nand are dropped; negative exported power is untouched. Apparent power\nis a magnitude, so any negative value is the marker, however it was\nscaled — a floor test would miss it for a power factor below 1.\nDropped values are skipped and reported like NaN.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtV1lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyjIQAK7ibRK0U8BCYPb9tp+Wm113\nn3GTK6AFYw5LpxXHeuYszFEHYlgvo/FCabHanxw0JPXUl5HuHlamDVxdAmhZEkjO\n9N4i1l6+LMDmgOS9l5C/W3jCluw54qqcjhfq9v6pxqB1PM4S0OkEw1vtBI5ZUO1g\nUoq5noru2t39AdEZgr8/NQJkYXAti70q5OjWYolID2G7wWJ3V2am7vy5LZtWxP0A\nYhXC6UWXSNzxJoLdyp+8FZIn/VZNC9LBOPCGq+e3sLQWS3FpFZBc5R65yJqUZfWs\nBZ2ExpPtVkBK9k5rVHHmg4wlKEh3/cbEUPqz4UwjzDBO5vWKBpHVc+0A2iqnAsn7\npVeOZmSh8gAS/WcY5Mo7Jba0tZNwM+YpxuipM3VrRGGU04u+QsarwTS91lkR1UE0\n1oxIjEZS1Z67/v1JAO61epoIJyJ8F90LI+713drYOh/PF9wgrIG3gp16onltrqgk\nOVgAvkh64HT7JX3XDA6f5yHD+YvUA09bs+kbNGhKCFiXDM5feV3APn0cn56WwOQr\nXAwZLo72NNPpmyo+5mrPzXHcNadQF6BYDSBlTbNKZ6pvdgkYyQbZsnKib90fjazR\nEmoW7WhoTy3P51EtibIN16okNdUNMZVtcBIVnIUITeerLIHx1UvMMOEYul/rneig\n2B+55p/dI/NHecMe8HvI\n=mCkU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T17:27:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/2ad9e9306629dbd793b103b334d4910970eb9839","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKDJhZDllOTMwNjYyOWRiZDc5M2IxMDNiMzM0ZDQ5MTA5NzBlYjk4Mzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/c02517ae6e93d2aff738fa7e5f7245212363a7ec","sha":"c02517ae6e93d2aff738fa7e5f7245212363a7ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/c02517ae6e93d2aff738fa7e5f7245212363a7ec"}],"sha":"2ad9e9306629dbd793b103b334d4910970eb9839","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/2ad9e9306629dbd793b103b334d4910970eb9839"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/c02517ae6e93d2aff738fa7e5f7245212363a7ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T18:31:45Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T18:31:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(ci): correct what the concurrency group guarantees (#204)\n\n* docs(ci): correct what the concurrency group guarantees\n\nThe comment said runs are \"queued rather than cancelled\", which reads as\na promise that every run eventually executes. GitHub''s default queue\nholds one pending run per group, so a run waiting behind another is\nreplaced when a newer one arrives — cancel-in-progress: false only\nprotects the run already in progress.\n\nThe behaviour is right either way: release-please derives the release\npull request from the commit range, so a superseded pending run would\nhave produced what the newest one produces. Only the claim was wrong.\n\n* ci: keep every release-please run in one concurrency group\n\nThe group was keyed on github.ref. The action is given no target-branch,\nso every run acts on the default branch''s release pull request — a\ndispatch launched from another branch would land in a group of its own\nand edit that pull request alongside a master run, which is the\ncollision the group exists to prevent. A constant group matches what the\nruns actually contend for.","tree":{"sha":"bfd044eeedcbf97875ade4af2a52dea0da526bd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/bfd044eeedcbf97875ade4af2a52dea0da526bd9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/c02517ae6e93d2aff738fa7e5f7245212363a7ec","verification":{"payload":"tree bfd044eeedcbf97875ade4af2a52dea0da526bd9\nparent 0b363c05f1b453a98ff3726684b241fe560d4c92\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1790015505 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790015505 +1200\n\ndocs(ci): correct what the concurrency group guarantees (#204)\n\n* docs(ci): correct what the concurrency group guarantees\n\nThe comment said runs are \"queued rather than cancelled\", which reads as\na promise that every run eventually executes. GitHub''s default queue\nholds one pending run per group, so a run waiting behind another is\nreplaced when a newer one arrives — cancel-in-progress: false only\nprotects the run already in progress.\n\nThe behaviour is right either way: release-please derives the release\npull request from the commit range, so a superseded pending run would\nhave produced what the newest one produces. Only the claim was wrong.\n\n* ci: keep every release-please run in one concurrency group\n\nThe group was keyed on github.ref. The action is given no target-branch,\nso every run acts on the default branch''s release pull request — a\ndispatch launched from another branch would land in a group of its own\nand edit that pull request alongside a master run, which is the\ncollision the group exists to prevent. A constant group matches what the\nruns actually contend for.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsXgRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWasQACJGyQW70kdMaW5kJXmu74lr\nTL0LsRnsmEgEIrgqZ1E36P0QJdPwgTqjIO8RBTl4yHsOHvsUD6ioerO1DHWy81nn\nY+DXUxcmpAB44aTc+ZZMClgPW4Pf4t+XGrqlHuyBOCiF7eodDNu