5767d6","sha":"c46db15b75a7338dfab1d5e464bffaf7fe5767d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/c46db15b75a7338dfab1d5e464bffaf7fe5767d6"}],"sha":"52f36a3dbbc918f4a129f9c15782be5a690bb9ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/52f36a3dbbc918f4a129f9c15782be5a690bb9ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/c46db15b75a7338dfab1d5e464bffaf7fe5767d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:02:16Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:02:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: restructure the README around how the plugin is used (#198)\n\n* docs: restructure the README around how the plugin is used\n\nThe README grew by accretion: two console sections, the History API\nsplit across two places 600 lines apart, Grafana contradicting\nConnectivity on loopback ports, a migration walkthrough without the\nvessel step or what to do afterwards, and no mention of the WAL\nsuspension monitor at all — not even its endpoints.\n\nIt now runs from getting started (requirements, install, first start,\ndefault provider) through configuration, recording, the History API,\nthe console, restore, migration, export, endpoints, deployment and\ntroubleshooting. Every statement was checked against the code: the\nimport keeps timestamps to the microsecond, not the nanosecond; the\nwrite buffer caps at 100000 lines and drops the oldest, it does not\ncommit early; a Grafana on the host reaches loopback without binding;\nsignalk-container 1.29.0 is what the whole feature set needs; the\nHistory API''s caps are numbers; per-path sampling rates were missing\nfrom the settings table. The web-console guide opens from the webapp\nand shows the source column.\n\n* docs: say which rows keep their own timestamps, and what value_kind is\n\nThe guide said ts is when the server received the sample; rows imported\nfrom InfluxDB keep the timestamps they had there. And it listed\nvalue_kind without saying it marks a boolean recorded as text.\n\n* docs: name the identity value kind\n\nA vessel''s name is stored in signalk_str under the path \"name\" with\nvalue_kind identity, which the v1 playback and the restore read back by\nthat tag; neither document said so.\n\n* docs: say the published-port address is probed, not assumed\n\nConnectivity said a containerized Signal K reaches the published ports\nvia host.containers.internal; the plugin probes its own loopback first\nand the gateway second, and uses the one QuestDB answers on.\n\n* docs: keep network attachment apart from port publication in Connectivity\n\nThe Bind-on bullet said the ports are published \"on the shared Container\nnetwork\"; QuestDB is attached to that network either way, and the\nsetting publishes the ports on the host''s interfaces.","tree":{"sha":"c5aab8f2027b7e4440e4d516c7b3677bedd3d776","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/c5aab8f2027b7e4440e4d516c7b3677bedd3d776"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/c46db15b75a7338dfab1d5e464bffaf7fe5767d6","verification":{"payload":"tree c5aab8f2027b7e4440e4d516c7b3677bedd3d776\nparent 962b175f53001b1f9c6388752020958a885aa4a8\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1789894936 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789894936 +1200\n\ndocs: restructure the README around how the plugin is used (#198)\n\n* docs: restructure the README around how the plugin is used\n\nThe README grew by accretion: two console sections, the History API\nsplit across two places 600 lines apart, Grafana contradicting\nConnectivity on loopback ports, a migration walkthrough without the\nvessel step or what to do afterwards, and no mention of the WAL\nsuspension monitor at all — not even its endpoints.\n\nIt now runs from getting started (requirements, install, first start,\ndefault provider) through configuration, recording, the History API,\nthe console, restore, migration, export, endpoints, deployment and\ntroubleshooting. Every statement was checked against the code: the\nimport keeps timestamps to the microsecond, not the nanosecond; the\nwrite buffer caps at 100000 lines and drops the oldest, it does not\ncommit early; a Grafana on the host reaches loopback without binding;\nsignalk-container 1.29.0 is what the whole feature set needs; the\nHistory API''s caps are numbers; per-path sampling rates were missing\nfrom the settings table. The web-console guide opens from the webapp\nand shows the source column.\n\n* docs: say which rows keep their own timestamps, and what value_kind is\n\nThe guide said ts is when the server received the sample; rows imported\nfrom InfluxDB keep the timestamps they had there. And it listed\nvalue_kind without saying it marks a boolean recorded as text.\n\n* docs: name the identity value kind\n\nA vessel''s name is stored in signalk_str under the path \"name\" with\nvalue_kind identity, which the v1 playback and the restore read back by\nthat tag; neither document said so.\n\n* docs: say the published-port address is probed, not assumed\n\nConnectivity said a containerized Signal K reaches the published ports\nvia host.containers.internal; the plugin probes its own loopback first\nand the gateway second, and uses the one QuestDB answers on.\n\n* docs: keep network attachment apart from port publication in Connectivity\n\nThe Bind-on bullet said the ports are published \"on the shared Container\nnetwork\"; QuestDB is attached to that network either way, and the\nsetting publishes the ports on the host''s interfaces.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqr6EYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5SsQAKeqAgA4gyUKNSYSVERNEZa6\nn0LIG7IZgu3PU++Fy/qavHd8Vu6kyixhDRd0T4ZysAJnbLznRR4NERWMNqS1T2g/\ni7tlWGoapBTks0KDFZsUmtSknUGWeVX51iSzxRuY+RA+7fzidN670HaCVtR1Svqw\nWOLSV/g+wRgYPM5TwjwE3YjdbANKWGhYe6avh4gQjutYez2yVChD7+uDPgz+/7Yn\n/l1D9PH8ev1KkqLhVxZJj6SLVpRudAbyE7w4ZrYZgCL2MYEFgTPNH7vJt7thYibB\nTgsepRILQ+MPC7o/0FHddQfyJZkuvBEHaW0buGnLswo3LoDhJUuYuzGriGAsoQDO\nqigLYHj+XXF3v7k1kxQPOXhJAQWaRjh1EHCn9XfYCm3yqssnOzzAA3ZRXSucUOwQ\nnT2C9Lvs0s8tftIPYANYqoJHEGDZEBOIz+V4eps0ETB1MHm5IAnB81/LyGCwmqXS\nVQhoQbzv95JDH29d6aShp+WGoTNbMGwSzd5atPouac7LimusRvgxuBfpUqeykwOy\nxJjNLVKBiy9/tPtP/0xjw8C0h0cy09yQWa7WUqcO8CeQYlM2byfYmOFht90Mc4t9\n1M2zoyVZ4sbK54g369I7Y0SBqsON64LKCjiOpBKFJDX5crXXXBk3Yg1sTX3CfCIs\nfiimKPmYyUN4tkQoA1gD\n=injl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T09:02:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/c46db15b75a7338dfab1d5e464bffaf7fe5767d6","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKGM0NmRiMTViNzVhNzMzOGRmYWIxZDVlNDY0YmZmYWY3ZmU1NzY3ZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/962b175f53001b1f9c6388752020958a885aa4a8","sha":"962b175f53001b1f9c6388752020958a885aa4a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/962b175f53001b1f9c6388752020958a885aa4a8"}],"sha":"c46db15b75a7338dfab1d5e464bffaf7fe5767d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/c46db15b75a7338dfab1d5e464bffaf7fe5767d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/962b175f53001b1f9c6388752020958a885aa4a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:42:59Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:42:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(history): type the provider against the published contract (#197)\n\nhistory-v2.ts carried its own copies of the History API''s request and\nresponse types, and the registration took the provider as unknown, so\nnothing checked the wire shape at build time: a renamed response key,\nlike sourceRef becoming $source, would go through unnoticed. The\nprovider is now a HistoryProvider from @signalk/server-api — PathSpec,\nValuesRequest, ValueList, ValuesResponse and AggregateMethod are the\npublished ones, the one flag of this provider''s own extends PathSpec,\nand the branded Path, Context, SourceRef and Timestamp are cast where\nrows leave the database. The typed test fixtures pass Temporal\ninstants, which is what the server passes; the as-any casts on the\ntime range go.","tree":{"sha":"f7cef8abf0ab0ccbcdc5e6a3800374eea844de6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/f7cef8abf0ab0ccbcdc5e6a3800374eea844de6e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/962b175f53001b1f9c6388752020958a885aa4a8","verification":{"payload":"tree f7cef8abf0ab0ccbcdc5e6a3800374eea844de6e\nparent 5505dbc429e5376ec4b6b3d96f6442dd58eb18d5\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1789864979 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789864979 +1200\n\nrefactor(history): type the provider against the published contract (#197)\n\nhistory-v2.ts carried its own copies of the History API''s request and\nresponse types, and the registration took the provider as unknown, so\nnothing checked the wire shape at build time: a renamed response key,\nlike sourceRef becoming $source, would go through unnoticed. The\nprovider is now a HistoryProvider from @signalk/server-api — PathSpec,\nValuesRequest, ValueList, ValuesResponse and AggregateMethod are the\npublished ones, the one flag of this provider''s own extends PathSpec,\nand the branded Path, Context, SourceRef and Timestamp are cast where\nrows leave the database. The typed test fixtures pass Temporal\ninstants, which is what the server passes; the as-any casts on the\ntime range go.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrywTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADsYQACIZjTSdw3SDnNRyGmAFYyq3\nD2M/mQ2Z8CeAHZ5dP9HPo2WHqhD0fuEke2SgMzvl7lL+wwiCd/joljYCiIcjuByV\nTirDtyTEYCsI/y1eW95AcHK9rOQ536K/NrYfVKLP6KK3XxNyWZmMA0UEzQY0xo+A\nJH2zxlQXTlwoN1/9QittF5rZM1wZPnetCnR/HAzkq0Q/jk3Z9UijX68QLI7AsqYH\n00a+SKTIYNUdI/poCdQYjCrev9vk9yY9+BPY01NiRh27eaeh/iMGNiPPFFOjWu2o\nhn7ZsWi9DzPalaV+kjPcAPL9oZ8GT2hZehrk5vnY85sqBth5F6HDJKiLk8eUzc4Q\n2lfkmsTZKKkniLUsiNUHGr/7SpjaRcz50GJKFsPcrgoW5zZpk/cFtY5R4rmcbCnP\n/CtquVzf+03jLEz7LBkdYjnvPW6fi1hNtJXYZR5XYA4KXKNhfjmYXMSXNEyX2GWJ\n3icC7fBJwUOTBpcRL2hlUOCyB835vJ/KFCBIvEaxjChagUW26Hi40GDe6ur0Y1bJ\nkzaCiJN9HWaPUOi4BinsSostXZh6LEaJViRCdVRUXsRKoDWX/6nr6+jBcPInmO03\n497brcvkK2697f1j8ATd2OPbQW5qN7kHThKjjCq6T5nFoCN8O6F5hYRErDjcQKog\n+N6AuHECerWLKDx6V04n\n=UPsR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T00:42:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/962b175f53001b1f9c6388752020958a885aa4a8","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKDk2MmIxNzVmNTMwMDFiMWY5YzYzODg3NTIwMjA5NThhODg1YWE0YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/5505dbc429e5376ec4b6b3d96f6442dd58eb18d5","sha":"5505dbc429e5376ec4b6b3d96f6442dd58eb18d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/5505dbc429e5376ec4b6b3d96f6442dd58eb18d5"}],"sha":"962b175f53001b1f9c6388752020958a885aa4a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/962b175f53001b1f9c6388752020958a885aa4a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/5505dbc429e5376ec4b6b3d96f6442dd58eb18d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:31:23Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:31:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(history): run middle_index per bucket and say what position ran (#195)\n\n* fix(history): run middle_index per bucket and say what position ran\n\nmiddle_index read every raw row in range under a LIMIT and returned one\nvalue, the middle row of the whole range, whatever resolution the\nrequest named — on raw timestamps no other column shared. It now picks\nthe middle row of each resolution bucket, by time, in one query\n(row_number and count over the bucket) and the middle row of the whole\nrange when no resolution is given; it counts against the sample-bucket\ncap like every other column and reads the numeric table only.\n\nnavigation.position ran first for any method but last and reported the\nmethod asked for. It now also answers middle_index, a point the vessel\nwas at, and when it does run first for something else the column says\nfirst — as the string fallback already did with last.\n\n* test(history): type the middle_index and position fixtures\n\nThe two new suites cast their client and request to any; the file\nalready has a typed pattern for both (QueryClientArg through unknown,\nthe request type derived from getValues), and they now use it.\n\n* fix(history): bound the whole-range middle row like every raw read\n\nWithout a resolution middleRowSql staged every raw row in range for one\nanswer; it now reads the range under the LIMIT the other raw reads use,\nso the answer is the middle of the first 50000 rows, as it was.","tree":{"sha":"12a0034f4c5f37e3dbd8197aeca2bec4fb3da253","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/12a0034f4c5f37e3dbd8197aeca2bec4fb3da253"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/5505dbc429e5376ec4b6b3d96f6442dd58eb18d5","verification":{"payload":"tree 12a0034f4c5f37e3dbd8197aeca2bec4fb3da253\nparent 9760cf6a040be65ffbcfa3879d3ccc85d5a9a9ad\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1789864283 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789864283 +1200\n\nfix(history): run middle_index per bucket and say what position ran (#195)\n\n* fix(history): run middle_index per bucket and say what position ran\n\nmiddle_index read every raw row in range under a LIMIT and returned one\nvalue, the middle row of the whole range, whatever resolution the\nrequest named — on raw timestamps no other column shared. It now picks\nthe middle row of each resolution bucket, by time, in one query\n(row_number and count over the bucket) and the middle row of the whole\nrange when no resolution is given; it counts against the sample-bucket\ncap like every other column and reads the numeric table only.\n\nnavigation.position ran first for any method but last and reported the\nmethod asked for. It now also answers middle_index, a point the vessel\nwas at, and when it does run first for something else the column says\nfirst — as the string fallback already did with last.\n\n* test(history): type the middle_index and position fixtures\n\nThe two new suites cast their client and request to any; the file\nalready has a typed pattern for both (QueryClientArg through unknown,\nthe request type derived from getValues), and they now use it.\n\n* fix(history): bound the whole-range middle row like every raw read\n\nWithout a resolution middleRowSql staged every raw row in range for one\nanswer; it now reads the range under the LIMIT the other raw reads use,\nso the answer is the middle of the first 50000 rows, as it was.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrylbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIFwQAHHYHG9c+7kxjucePPd02C2f\nPKT24wzbu6Sj+puw71Puxs4JwrNWp1spUz6reqx17cS7//Cyq7JOurZe9ni7shgR\nsIk/Kz0yBz6ZYjK6SXZZwt3p8YsnUquSDavzZslcV/dOwDPxQfXeo1BEespRS