ode_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKDYwNmY0ODg4MWRmM2RmMzBkNTg1YzE3MzU5NjVjZTQ4NmNmZWI4Zjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/eef2668730c5ae8b9170017490f887f588f5e299","sha":"eef2668730c5ae8b9170017490f887f588f5e299","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/eef2668730c5ae8b9170017490f887f588f5e299"}],"sha":"606f48881df3df30d585c1735965ce486cfeb8f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/606f48881df3df30d585c1735965ce486cfeb8f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/eef2668730c5ae8b9170017490f887f588f5e299/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T22:38:51Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T22:38:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(history): run sma and ema over resolution buckets (#191)\n\n* fix(history): run sma and ema over resolution buckets\n\nA moving average read every raw row in range under a LIMIT and ran its\nwindow over those, whatever resolution the request named: sma:5 at\n180s was a ten-second average, returned on raw timestamps that no other\ncolumn of the response shared, and a long range was cut at 50000 rows.\n\nThe window now runs over the series at the requested resolution — one\naveraged bucket per sample, the grid every other column is on — and over\nraw rows only when no resolution is given, as every method does. An\nempty bucket keeps its place in the sma window, so a value leaves it N\nbuckets after it arrived and a gap no longer stretches the window back\nin time. The two count against the sample-bucket cap like average,\nnever fall back to the string table, and a window that is not a whole\nnumber of samples of at least 1 (sma) or an alpha outside (0, 1] (ema)\nis refused before any query runs. middle_index keeps its raw-row read.\n\n* docs(history): say why middle_index reads raw rows; name the average bucket\n\nThe sma and ema rows of the aggregate table repeated the average row''s\nSQL; they now say the series they run over is the average bucket. The\ncomment on readsRawRows restated its name instead of saying why\nmiddle_index is the one method that ignores the resolution, and the\nmoving-average tests'' comment narrated the old behaviour. The text-path\ntest fed null buckets that SAMPLE BY over no rows never produces; it\nnow feeds none and expects an empty column.","tree":{"sha":"9f37298f3ce2f25955785bfa5cea8898efc2f1bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/9f37298f3ce2f25955785bfa5cea8898efc2f1bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/eef2668730c5ae8b9170017490f887f588f5e299","verification":{"payload":"tree 9f37298f3ce2f25955785bfa5cea8898efc2f1bc\nparent c20a856e90d3c5e31995d855715a7057431d0d17\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1789857531 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789857531 +1200\n\nfix(history): run sma and ema over resolution buckets (#191)\n\n* fix(history): run sma and ema over resolution buckets\n\nA moving average read every raw row in range under a LIMIT and ran its\nwindow over those, whatever resolution the request named: sma:5 at\n180s was a ten-second average, returned on raw timestamps that no other\ncolumn of the response shared, and a long range was cut at 50000 rows.\n\nThe window now runs over the series at the requested resolution — one\naveraged bucket per sample, the grid every other column is on — and over\nraw rows only when no resolution is given, as every method does. An\nempty bucket keeps its place in the sma window, so a value leaves it N\nbuckets after it arrived and a gap no longer stretches the window back\nin time. The two count against the sample-bucket cap like average,\nnever fall back to the string table, and a window that is not a whole\nnumber of samples of at least 1 (sma) or an alpha outside (0, 1] (ema)\nis refused before any query runs. middle_index keeps its raw-row read.\n\n* docs(history): say why middle_index reads raw rows; name the average bucket\n\nThe sma and ema rows of the aggregate table repeated the average row''s\nSQL; they now say the series they run over is the average bucket. The\ncomment on readsRawRows restated its name instead of saying why\nmiddle_index is the one method that ignores the resolution, and the\nmoving-average tests'' comment narrated the old behaviour. The text-path\ntest fed null buckets that SAMPLE BY over no rows never produces; it\nnow feeds none and expects an empty column.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrw77CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1ZwQACuxlGiw8pxSz+pDjqIDs48u\nc7iYFGHEmTxIj5l0qP2cetsEs4mWOr9DgVKUdx+Z+ybRn7Js3/RwcZK76/FengA4\nyr0/odvE1z/kCD/uCmrbf3aiZqYoJTLm3SU4HoggwoNhf9y5bld6U8W4XVeKxzZi\n1xc/nBbDsf5UgcLhenR33hu9mgvavvrJzgQ3c1eJ/wiOalmga4wSV1/hD7rHNWKW\ne+Ev6NODE5OwHpD4fPdsLvUBY78d5yr0JAYo5xaiXipfP6G3Q+SDsa7J/rav6PT0\noSvDUyN62JIvm2VqVaFFTwmiYVbhj77tCljrG1pZBBCew7t1kZyEzDWt