irs — every time, though the data said. The vessel the source\nrecorded as its own is now read from that tag and chosen; the question\nremains for a source that says nothing (signalk-to-influxdb 1.x, data\nolder than the tag) or names more than one, with this server''s identity\nstill preselected when it is among the vessels.\n\n* docs: say when a 1.x source still leaves the vessel choice to the user","tree":{"sha":"224afd08e6c9d672d80f9bb33bd52db6324afb66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/224afd08e6c9d672d80f9bb33bd52db6324afb66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/1c04e25783f6e950d5e66a85a4c7b087dc725c6e","verification":{"payload":"tree 224afd08e6c9d672d80f9bb33bd52db6324afb66\nparent 6a7bf841666b1aa030f6f990da47cf4420d25cff\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1789847955 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789847955 +1200\n\nfeat(migration): read the own vessel from the source''s self tag (#188)\n\n* feat(migration): read the own vessel from the source''s self tag\n\nsignalk-to-influxdb2 tags every point of the recording server''s own\nvessel with self=true, and its own History API answers vessels.self by\nthat tag rather than by identity. The importer read only the context\ntag, so with several vessels in the source it asked the user which was\ntheirs — every time, though the data said. The vessel the source\nrecorded as its own is now read from that tag and chosen; the question\nremains for a source that says nothing (signalk-to-influxdb 1.x, data\nolder than the tag) or names more than one, with this server''s identity\nstill preselected when it is among the vessels.\n\n* docs: say when a 1.x source still leaves the vessel choice to the user","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrumTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ5YQAGIMLv3Uh08zOiqPNPxkDXn7\ntveRuyTiMOiSM78TLUZBjFMzO4UrKyuphNJ1jQ1YzZLvJcxGAQh4MHj3DydaOUQj\nRWnYFvOSu0kXGtOf14