rl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/fd76db557c7417168a7d843110eee2f35839cdc5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T18:45:52Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T18:45:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(history): return a position as a [longitude, latitude] pair (#184)\n\n* fix(history): return a position as a [longitude, latitude] pair\n\nThe History API''s OpenAPI schema allows a number array in a data cell,\nwith [-120.5, 59.2] in its example, and signalk-to-influxdb2 and\nsignalk-parquet both return navigation.position as that pair, GeoJSON\norder. This provider returned the data model''s {latitude, longitude}\nobject, so a client written to the schema — a track viewer reading\n[lon, lat] — got nothing to draw. The v1 playback API is unchanged: it\nreplays deltas, which carry the object.\n\n* test(history): a zero coordinate is a position, not a gap","tree":{"sha":"64ac5984ba4006e046b3c29c4be349b24cea7057","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/64ac5984ba4006e046b3c29c4be349b24cea7057"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/fd76db557c7417168a7d843110eee2f35839cdc5","verification":{"payload":"tree 64ac5984ba4006e046b3c29c4be349b24cea7057\nparent 4ce77caf74b7b7eaf8c750fd878341185f5cad77\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1789843552 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789843552 +1200\n\nfix(history): return a position as a [longitude, latitude] pair (#184)\n\n* fix(history): return a position as a [longitude, latitude] pair\n\nThe History API''s OpenAPI schema allows a number array in a data cell,\nwith [-120.5, 59.2] in its example, and signalk-to-influxdb2 and\nsignalk-parquet both return navigation.position as that pair, GeoJSON\norder. This provider returned the data model''s {latitude, longitude}\nobject, so a client written to the schema — a track viewer reading\n[lon, lat] — got nothing to draw. The v1 playback API is unchanged: it\nreplays deltas, which carry the object.\n\n* test(history): a zero coordinate is a position, not a gap","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrthgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApQsQAGrwYMIuFcXrPUrHUWkId3CE\nMWhC7Pe9aZUl+gm3ZDC/jow+CCoBxcNuZBi4DqBkjo65z0PxNhKKR+dpUOfJr1wW\nQ9eccguwHXemplsjmhYvK9wuPAd14X7q3UmOAUsJQg5m2yvXxeiQGAl5OII1iDmC\nJlueIpAC5PANW6oOIj1ufkTVh1ouKebCh3RajLOtv48b+0eHtvyMbu74vHoK1Vmb\nuNBtI/KchBTf267hXB0Ik0VFxt+HyDQ6Rj3dm7+kAD3hORqwqdAwUCefJJUi6uez\nNREnl3gpski/HdpfIhMPEIFnI55HhEsElBiPA9yuFlEnzLTPK8qQtfZXmwxV7jRN\nGUt+f2Gc36MktCXyDVSbh7QjfooMrOqTST62pN3TcIlciy7ZYad6zjYXGzuBH5Yu\nLwkvjrTvzqe53PQeDsRscZN1f3fPM0eK5/GsGbU/dH0OiW1VbRGTBwtA+hpVQsqi\nisTNt7pkWjM/CIwJPdjDrUr9vtmltzXX9OEBwZR32axZe4Yl41XbIik1fIT4IHxF\nPtb/3qHoCCOu9FEI/7xCFrFr46Bfd/UZJAHkaDLL2LkunNRec4Zb2Oakhj2Z2+Nm\nGT/xHmQpRxg3x6v11+pksZktODsqo3JvXol9lJHroeTJn+2fnYyjWj5WUi/kEJP/\n4RdaFLVrvSZ6sXeFx2Dw\n=yQRV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",