ar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/20f6137cfa3c15adf9907afdd85dc478c7c897ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T16:37:25Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T16:37:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(restore): replay an object identity as the object, not its leaves (#181)\n\n* fix(restore): replay an object identity as the object, not its leaves\n\ndesign.aisShipType and design.length are objects in Signal K, recorded\nas their flattened leaves. The restore replayed the leaves under their\nown paths, which land in the data model as design.aisShipType.id.value\n— read by nothing: Freeboard takes a target''s type from\ndesign.aisShipType.value and looks for the bare path in a delta. So a\nrestored target had its type in the database, found by the restore,\nand still drew in the default colour until its next live static report\n(#170, after #148 and #163 fixed which rows are read).\n\nThe leaves go back together under the bare path before replay, at the\ntime of the newest leaf. A bare-path row from before flattening stands\nonly when no leaf does.\n\n* fix(restore): restore the hull length leaf too\n\nThe recorder writes every scalar leaf of design.length, so a hull length\nis on disk whenever a source sent one; the identity list named only\noverall, and the hull was left behind on restore.","tree":{"sha":"172aa1743e4d1ef9d43fbb9146ffcf54df68f485","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/172aa1743e4d1ef9d43fbb9146ffcf54df68f485"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/20f6137cfa3c15adf9907afdd85dc478c7c897ff","verification":{"payload":"tree 172aa1743e4d1ef9d43fbb9146ffcf54df68f485\nparent d48273b23353c4405b5b6d6c30446b2e399ef921\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1789749445 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789749445 +1200\n\nfix(restore): replay an object identity as the object, not its leaves (#181)\n\n* fix(restore): replay an object identity as the object, not its leaves\n\ndesign.aisShipType and design.length are objects in Signal K, recorded\nas their flattened leaves. The restore replayed the leaves under their\nown paths, which land in the data model as design.aisShipType.id.value\n— read by nothing: Freeboard takes a target''s type from\ndesign.aisShipType.value and looks for the bare path in a delta. So a\nrestored target had its type in the database, found by the restore,\nand still drew in the default colour until its next live static report\n(#170, after #148 and #163 fixed which rows are read).\n\nThe leaves go back together under the bare path before replay, at the\ntime of the newest leaf. A bare-path row from before flattening stands\nonly when no leaf does.\n\n* fix(restore): restore the hull length leaf too\n\nThe recorder writes every scalar leaf of design.length, so a hull length\nis on disk whenever a source sent one; the identity list named only\noverall, and the hull was left behind on restore.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrWjFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAag0QAFnE3MsvqLHInuaFIxU+Pp32\n0wGZYrIu1wCp1vbBmf0RLKuQtnwyVYp+ErUAY01EtZrgjlontOW1T/aIjnbF40/B\nVx2FwMO4dkOeJDS4jzlFKeKuIXmHb7qP+mSNNK3gEoVTUmLnAm6ysbp9dDIhsw+p\nz9nmfe93H1JN31Pp1l3bIW4aqIgjdoJYAg2rC6BhNKu5M/7Pa5854IiBuX87J44w\nz2Uoxv6WS8faf/UQi/VyUBlrghuAbzPBu68DJSV7HkGT/0747qactVMVWt3g3F3+\njzaFy8ynUO723FdiaOhGYAKN7qytc6MQboqZVs45l+78durFRqVRiDbel4EFDxCr\ndyWzrBemxRyUggl21psNbXtCfKq12Qx5hmMbBBekgsvekOfLEaekmseLny9oaabT\nwgdS0VYBwdRy8ESVz76YSUfIofyOD2emmmsIEpwIH3ZVTOr51dYT2E+B+DaCmRD/\n+wpGo7I1lL5f3tSQlbkRHIiEKiF49DZH7t13b7CeIfikNAjzqS0T35NB1FBCHHTO\nZfAILpISxfd6qgArLWPviiwSQRZCxG2X9AlvxTLVps5TlI/hyx4FbSiGw/bru+xg\n1xCxI/ru/HgmehdM8oe0oLtRNiF0oeM0PV8mKlJJfEdaGuylsFITs4fLExyVFLiS\n8VHswn9shOBq/XLdGP3+\n=nZqx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T16:37:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/20f6137cfa3c15adf9907afdd85dc478c7c897ff