":{"date":"2026-08-28T19:38:04Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T19:38:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(restore): widen the identity window to 7 days (#167)\n\nIssue #163: AIS targets still drew default purple after #148 added the\nship-type leaves to IDENTITY_PATHS. The leaves were right; the window was\ntoo short.\n\nA vessel moored nearby broadcasts position every few seconds but its STATIC\nreport — the one carrying ship type — only occasionally. A target seen daily\ncan easily have a type older than 24 hours, so it came back drawn but\nuncoloured. Reproduced against a real QuestDB: a vessel with a 30-second-old\nposition and a 3-day-old ship type restores with no type at all.\n\nMeasured on a live 155M-row install: of 415 vessels holding a ship type, 24h\nreached 190 and 7d reached 312. 30d would reach all 415.\n\n7d rather than 30d because the cost is NOT flat, which the old comment\nclaimed. LATEST ON does collapse the row count (547 at 24h, 899 at 7d, 1250\nat 30d), but the scan grows: this query warms to ~100ms at 24h, ~3s at 7d and\n~6-9s at 30d, and it runs at every plugin start. 7d buys most of the coverage\nfor a few seconds; 30d pays several times over for the last quarter.\n\nThe two tests that pinned the literal 24h are updated rather than relaxed —\nthey exist so the two windows cannot silently collapse into one.","tree":{"sha":"f530cc59e8e90844fc3fd66d54eb83be96d2d287","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/f530cc59e8e90844fc3fd66d54eb83be96d2d287"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/b03ff74da6ba92393155c3eba9835ccf3e1324f4","verification":{"payload":"tree f530cc59e8e90844fc3fd66d54eb83be96d2d287\nparent ea5edea2c2a91dc13272570f937d38ffa7417b24\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1787945884 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787945884 +1200\n\nfix(restore): widen the identity window to 7 days (#167)\n\nIssue #163: AIS targets still drew default purple after #148 added the\nship-type leaves to IDENTITY_PATHS. The leaves were right; the window was\ntoo short.\n\nA vessel moored nearby broadcasts position every few seconds but its STATIC\nreport — the one carrying ship type — only occasionally. A target seen daily\ncan easily have a type older than 24 hours, so it came back drawn but\nuncoloured. Reproduced against a real QuestDB: a vessel with a 30-second-old\nposition and a 3-day-old ship type restores with no type at all.\n\nMeasured on a live 155M-row install: of 415 vessels holding a ship type, 24h\nreached 190 and 7d reached 312. 30d would reach all 415.\n\n7d rather than 30d because the cost is NOT flat, which the old comment\nclaimed. LATEST ON does collapse the row count (547 at 24h, 899 at 7d, 1250\nat 30d), but the scan grows: this query warms to ~100ms at 24h, ~3s at 7d and\n~6-9s at 30d, and it runs at every plugin start. 7d buys most of the coverage\nfor a few seconds; 30d pays several times over for the last quarter.\n\nThe two tests that pinned the literal 24h are updated rather than relaxed —\nthey exist so the two windows cannot silently collapse into one.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkeOcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6B0QACxIpfd7IhVKGE6zvmZH6G3k\nVPLT5VMYGmxgm4WVD1ouSb7HsjMKpht4A6yAiPrcRsXy74qLrHTYh2TMkz1lOw/S\nXZGyIrnhlLADFOXaPzsXo7uiB6mPjl8iMPu6YVZTCoMnfFyjddYI/UZqMw9McEC6\nMNpENJF755/ebDzk46IcMYGlYjermPHFdig9lCwrveNDKQ8HM92WS57ogaoZEQ6V\n5jT/8zS92ePhh3WB5g61ZIqPtWeRX0+rhwlzVUoLcHo7DySWHjfNiXoHhWmbcVfF\nDPBG8hN/wKv7ECc2KcSTdHzmBXPowLBR5llGqVm8btsd01Tl+n6O08Z/2jlXyxav\nwwCwURw3WOUG/lwX21ReVefIK5nJb0i+v5TpsSkhSDYlI3qUxpUFKYbW2CwQK0kJ\nH/8ZBoWBDdH7IwswNLgKf9X6a2NczHd2gYOxeNBASR7pLXTTimnFl0ZEvsnqVcDe\n8PhWcnAnNoIsfdR25rdKxIJ/hHFHWG/ENRUKN7xLWc6yT6ya4kgqoE1KVJuwvFEk\nvseEkBAHhZso6E7MDY3lqxyXVPBRITVe74Z1aQ606L3+KyB4CgZxPwmkZXVV18ol\n