url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/830d17b87950568737a30fd251b6487d91239681","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKDgzMGQxN2I4Nzk1MDU2ODczN2EzMGZkMjUxYjY0ODdkOTEyMzk2ODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/2f9b3c40236da9e497a9fde46d16b5c283db89bf","sha":"2f9b3c40236da9e497a9fde46d16b5c283db89bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/2f9b3c40236da9e497a9fde46d16b5c283db89bf"}],"sha":"830d17b87950568737a30fd251b6487d91239681","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/830d17b87950568737a30fd251b6487d91239681"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/2f9b3c40236da9e497a9fde46d16b5c283db89bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T03:38:29Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T03:38:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ilp): stop stacking drain listeners while the socket is backpressured (#161)\n\nEvery flush that returns false from socket.write() registered another\n`once(\"drain\")` listener. `once` removes a listener when it FIRES, not when\nanother is added, so while the socket stays saturated they accumulate — one\nper flush, none removed until a drain finally happens.\n\nSurfaced importing a real user''s InfluxDB history: Node emitted\n\"MaxListenersExceededWarning: 11 drain listeners added to [Socket]\" partway\nthrough a 197M-row run. Reproduced in isolation at 369 listeners on one\nsocket; with the guard it stays at 1.\n\nHarmless in effect — the listeners only log — but it is a real leak, and a\nspurious MaxListeners warning trains operators to ignore the warning that\nwould otherwise flag a genuine one.\n\nThe flag is cleared on every path that drops the socket (close and\ndisconnect), or a stale `true` would suppress the listener on the next\nconnection entirely.","tree":{"sha":"b7ac72da59c832f45d45a02b3fd671c1387b20b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/b7ac72da59c832f45d45a02b3fd671c1387b20b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/2f9b3c40236da9e497a9fde46d16b5c283db89bf","verification":{"payload":"tree b7ac72da59c832f45d45a02b3fd671c1387b20b7\nparent c4c49e147f7648f1ed604a720e5713093b80c0c7\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1787283509 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787283509 +1200\n\nfix(ilp): stop stacking drain listeners while the socket is backpressured (#161)\n\nEvery flush that returns false from socket.write() registered another\n`once(\"drain\")` listener. `once` removes a listener when it FIRES, not when\nanother is added, so while the socket stays saturated they accumulate — one\nper flush, none removed until a drain finally happens.\n\nSurfaced importing a real user''s InfluxDB history: Node emitted\n\"MaxListenersExceededWarning: 11 drain listeners added to [Socket]\" partway\nthrough a 197M-row run. Reproduced in isolation at 369 listeners on one\nsocket; with the guard it stays at 1.\n\nHarmless in effect — the listeners only log — but it is a real leak, and a\nspurious MaxListeners warning trains operators to ignore the warning that\nwould otherwise flag a genuine one.\n\nThe flag is cleared on every path that drops the socket (close and\ndisconnect), or a stale `true` would suppress the listener on the next\nconnection entirely.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh8g1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAv8cQAElFgI0MiE2PsSdN3A1T3MFd\nv0BSLYx+OHNOgqa621Nu6P3CN8D6yZt1I9mLp3eKsPchsL7tgOAlL2eCnR2ME9lv\naDkvuIhsktvfw0bmeBM0UjQE+Sb37I4r45oBDscFAvkn+haMjqj6wecm9dsL9wuL\nLeWyeiZVDNDeTY4niv+MD5MqvI5ZW3m93V+SaroMTLaSI4kU2O7ZHuzeBPzqYHUQ\n0XgD8Pw4dpK6Kzw7m+CbswezrlOIYgs53x9rdMXL+oFkpkYjrO/1aYUsmpiXojQs\nY0dkdgU2Xx/La+hJQDIztOYgpj6ws3EI87aeGM7Dn6286x90WDbe5JWNGMza/uOZ\nT5hLBWXX8n1Hf1OdLYYwDi7YXeQeg/kqo2L0SxTrfcUzN+QU6BtPfzmAANNZvtfe\n7AThMkuVERZRLhfvleBtDI9AqMdKpxyGmhWcTPKwnjIbO7MY4Vvwm6tcQ2kC5DD+\ndNU9WmMceYlBFIBkio1xzRFO1EfjlsbGef91OhXw+n0tRB3HpBmWadfaBWQuf2wN\nJ/kHbYW/A/D6PePx6BK0/kfP66qLQVlmkVLN5xlimgluIt0Ga8YAwXhhPD5oMnF6\n4hwgIW