ollowing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/b11db9ca689bbe6a510fb6a9ba973b407d80940c","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKGIxMWRiOWNhNjg5YmJlNmE1MTBmYjZhOWJhOTczYjQwN2Q4MDk0MGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/a8ecc8794ac1e7f7b681dd9b565844fa21664781","sha":"a8ecc8794ac1e7f7b681dd9b565844fa21664781","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/a8ecc8794ac1e7f7b681dd9b565844fa21664781"}],"sha":"b11db9ca689bbe6a510fb6a9ba973b407d80940c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/b11db9ca689bbe6a510fb6a9ba973b407d80940c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/a8ecc8794ac1e7f7b681dd9b565844fa21664781/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T18:40:52Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T18:40:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(migration): discover measurements from the schema, not the data (#159)\n\nA user importing ~1 year of InfluxDB 2.x history on a Pi 5 (~40 GB) got\n\"The operation was aborted due to a timeout\" with \"0 written, 0 skipped,\n0/0 measurements\" — the import died during discovery, having read nothing.\n\nlistMeasurements() derived measurement names with\n\n    from(bucket) |> range(start: 0) |> keep([_measurement, _field]) |> distinct\n\nwhich reads EVERY POINT IN THE BUCKET before collapsing. The old comment\nclaimed `keep` avoided that; it does not — `keep` and `distinct` shrink the\nRESULT, not the scan. Measured against a live 2.9.1: 0.15s at 1.2M points,\n0.50s at 4.8M (linear in point count), while schema.measurements() answered\nin ~8ms at both sizes. On a year of boat data the scan simply outran the\nquery timeout.\n\nDiscovery now asks InfluxDB for its schema. Same names, cost proportional\nto the schema rather than the history: 40 measurements in 68ms against\n4.8M points.\n\nField keys are no longer fetched. Nothing consumed them — the import maps\nthis to `.name` and the panel renders only names — and pairing fields to\nmeasurements needs either the scan above or one request per measurement.\n`fields` stays in the response contract as an empty array rather than\nbreaking a shape consumers may destructure.\n\nThe 1.x path is unchanged and was never affected: SHOW FIELD KEYS is\nmetadata in InfluxQL, measured at 0.024s over 800k points.\n\nVerified end to end on a fresh 2.9.1 holding 4.8M points across 40\nmeasurements over two years: 4,800,000 read, 4,800,000 written, 0 skipped,\n271s, all 40 paths and the full time span present in QuestDB.","tree":{"sha":"a79cd9ce49ad311d163007eeaeef36854a2044c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/a79cd9ce49ad311d163007eeaeef36854a2044c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/a8ecc8794ac1e7f7b681dd9b565844fa21664781","verification":{"payload":"tree a79cd9ce49ad311d163007eeaeef36854a2044c7\nparent 11904c6846405afdf8e8406c8b800dfbf267c08c\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1787251252 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787251252 +1200\n\nfix(migration): discover measurements from the schema, not the data (#159)\n\nA user importing ~1 year of InfluxDB 2.x history on a Pi 5 (~40 GB) got\n\"The operation was aborted due to a timeout\" with \"0 written, 0 skipped,\n0/0 measurements\" — the import died during discovery, having read nothing.\n\nlistMeasurements() derived measurement names with\n\n    from(bucket) |> range(start: 0) |> keep([_measurement, _field]) |> distinct\n\nwhich reads EVERY POINT IN THE BUCKET before collapsing. The old comment\nclaimed `keep` avoided that; it does not — `keep` and `distinct` shrink the\nRESULT, not the scan. Measured against a live 2.9.1: 0.15s at 1.2M points,\n0.50s at 4.8M (linear in point count), while schema.measurements() answered\nin ~8ms at both sizes. On a year of boat data the scan simply outran the\nquery timeout.\n\nDiscovery now asks InfluxDB for its schema. Same names, cost proportional\nto the schema rather than the history: 40 measurements in 68ms against\n4.8M points.\n\nField keys are no longer fetched. Nothing consumed them — the import maps\nthis to `.name` and the panel renders only names — and pairing fields to\nmeasurements needs either the scan above or one request per measurement.\n`fields` stays in the response contract as an empty array rather than\nbreaking a shape consumers may destructure.\n\nThe 1.x path is unchanged and was never affected: SHOW FIELD KEYS is\nmetadata in InfluxQL, measured at 0.024s over 800k points.\n\nVerified end to end on a fresh 2.9.1 holding 4.8M points across 40\nmeasurements over two years: 4,800,000 read, 4,800,000 written, 0 skipped,\n271s, all 40 paths and the full time span present in QuestDB.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh0o0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKFsQAEXHi5qlkgAzMAsZCJMAsvjm\n7mGkosNg/DWkghC29+YAcQ47kgYWhlYXYEa9ZnfXC13MifvOOOSX/6GRyy8vKHou\n1cWh3y7Tx3sTOdz/i1ZgB05x+ZuHBJ3yDoqS3tCjkvLAePaRwrPDbtzkEB4tuqRw\nhZZFJvRvIGjGctHerqMHu7hJGASmZ6O86UxWgBHL9YXFxdlOUDvxynf8Hh+rt/xX\nbx6PidKG0ZUO49nyP9/dsCixQkynW3QNIA+e/UPLRKB6RPRBxKlDCzZuYrTWZkrB\nC6uld8pAGm2tIbT0jIfBUSX9P1scILlUgG9O4II2098MqXdDgB82mO5sJOtmpPJb\nZMh8suxPNZRL6fpX5ork/Sqg0U14q6tcgCH8GmFMAtObLuSwiAGG38Ovqyo86bkB\n/sWbtFyBwNQTrvOTLhCZ9gPA38DloNu4+0MQmPrkHqpHP+tslo9GTbGxt0O9InXc\nBWnS+/uNXlABokh/zsEo31Xc5UzXeGZZgYkJY6UR7l1IN5799WPH5wBkeLdxQifH\n6xWIdkmEH2ggzIKw6RW12b5rQ3n6QOIUi/u3s2OuPf38oK1+Fm9NDsK043Ruyczw\ntO7vHSmc97f0/lXziGOMW9l2FU3iFTWxBM59c2IfzHYlFDfxiymlnHA7m/9e3WcI\nTr+TbvYemVsJXYtsfQPn\n=k4QW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T18:40:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/a8ecc8794ac1e7f7b681dd9b565844fa21664781","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKGE4ZWNjODc5NGFjMWU3ZjdiNjgxZGQ5YjU2NTg0NGZhMjE2NjQ3ODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/11904c6846405afdf8e8406c8b800dfbf267c08c","sha":"11904c6846405afdf8e8406c8b800dfbf267c08c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/11904c6846405afdf8e8406c8b800dfbf267c08c"}],"sha":"a8ecc8794ac1e7f7b681dd9b565844fa21664781","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/a8ecc8794ac1e7f7b681dd9b565844fa21664781"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/11904c6846405afdf8e8406c8b800dfbf267c08c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T01:02:24Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T01:02:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(package): assert compiled tests stay out of the tarball (#158)\n\n* chore: stop publishing compiled tests in the npm tarball\n\n`dist/test/` shipped to npm: 57 files and 593 KB of the 1995 KB unpacked\nsize, close to a third of the package, in every release at least back to\n2.0.1. Nothing imports it — `main` is `dist/index.js`, and the only\nreference anywhere is the `test` script.\n\nThat script keeps working. `.npmignore` governs what goes into the tarball,\nnot what exists locally, so `npm test` still runs the suite from the built\nworking tree exactly as before — verified, 469 tests still pass.\n\nVerified against a real `npm pack` that the exclusion removes those 57\nfiles and nothing else: `dist/index.js`, `public/remoteEntry.js`, all 43\nfederation chunks, LICENSE.md and the icon are all still present. Also\nextracted the trimmed tarball, installed its runtime deps and loaded it as\na plugin — it registers and exposes the current config schema.\n\nThe federation chunks are the reason to check rather than assume: they are\nimported by name from `remoteEntry.js`, so excluding one publishes a config\npanel that 404s on load, with nothing in CI to catch it.\n\n* test(package): assert compiled tests stay out of the tarball\n\n#157 excluded dist/test/ from the published package. Nothing pinned that,\nso the next well-meant ignore-file edit could undo it silently — the same\nfailure mode the neighbouring .mf/ and src/ assertions guard against, and\nthe same one that shipped .mf/ once already.\n\nUses the existing publishedFiles() helper, which reads npm''s own manifest\nrather than the working tree: .npmignore excludes by exact filename, so a\nfile can be present on disk and absent from the tarball.\n\nVerified as a real guard — reverting the .npmignore line fails this test.","tree":{"sha":"e2427479eda076912fac3f31f792b4cd05d81c91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/e2427479eda076912fac3f31f792b4cd05d81c91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/11904c6846405afdf8e8406c8b800dfbf267c08c","verification":{"payload":"tree e2427479eda076912fac3f31f792b4cd05d81c91\nparent d0cbd8fe2887201d8a488717f9426be94d746290\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1787187744 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787187744 +1200\n\ntest(package): assert compiled tests stay out of the tarball (#158)\n\n* chore: stop publishing compiled tests in the npm tarball\n\n`dist/test/` shipped to npm: 57 files and 593 KB of the 1995 KB unpacked\nsize, close to a third of the package, in every release at least back to\n2.0.1. Nothing imports it — `main` is `dist/index.js`, and the only\nreference anywhere is the `test` script.\n\nThat script keeps working. `.npmignore` governs what goes into the tarball,\nnot what exists locally, so `npm test` still runs the suite from the built\nworking tree exactly as before — verified, 469 tests still pass.\n\nVerified against a real `npm pack` that the exclusion removes those 57\nfiles and nothing else: `dist/index.js`, `public/remoteEntry.js`, all 43\nfederation chunks, LICENSE.md and the icon are all still present. Also\nextracted the trimmed tarball, installed its runtime deps and loaded it as\na plugin — it registers and exposes the current config schema.\n\nThe federation chunks are the reason to check rather than assume: they are\nimported by name from `remoteEntry.js`, so excluding one publishes a config\npanel that 404s on load, with nothing in CI to catch it.\n\n* test(package): assert compiled tests stay out of the tarball\n\n#157 excluded dist/test/ from the published package. Nothing pinned that,\nso the next well-meant ignore-file edit could undo it silently — the same\nfailure mode the neighbouring .mf/ and src/ assertions guard against, and\nthe same one that shipped .mf/ once already.\n\nUses the existing publishedFiles() helper, which reads npm''s own manifest\nrather than the working tree: .npmignore excludes by exact filename, so a\nfile can be present on disk and absent from the tarball.\n\nVerified as a real guard — reverting the .npmignore line fails this test.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhlIgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArIwQAFqfAZKKpw8vANAQgM5Sl6WL\ns/ClGIcgMzDhkCvEUJh/yynWxypEEmsvizeZnwxr9IP8mj5INtCiIOemETd8O7G0\n9lV3Vrh0tVuHBxjUmbafVWRAvXcyrnN9JGNpwyW37TvmqS3KAgt91RKhJKeB/8xl\nKjA5IMnS0aJWyS7d2SDeRzuWGf6vNOloxwpS2AtvCuzgUdt9ob+ixnOKw5+N1qUh\nQQPxCRzAoPvxxqkMOfkyc641aF33R7pDH8Igpd2Q/q27OGAW8R6dZxKtHBGV37S0\n+ypWSrpNIW6xjsZnykq/zwgY/Nr2XP0pmbZ8w/0ekKwKfsNjstnDUZBw2SNe0wqo\nY++8I/NVUz2CqWARI7Ba82obkhC5U9MtWK6yUCa+mRj65bLc3nCxh9tCXOuQR7a1\n9gfZAsoRu4HxUOu6IqQummBgl9W4Aiq3lQbzDsM3gg4GDIO3Ji3rNXdNPObfBSBa\nW6Ntz4aTZyFX3BxbQRYUpuCCll7YcDJc/Ue+IsodLZp8E1nE+ao5em2Yo+G1jYve\napnaRvp3h5KDUO0z04YlxhzEY+M8qrtQBnIUa+OVa2gYWdmOOzJJFvBuqmfiN8KP\nb+oKBY/WlyOwxlGYiCPmvCOuYijk2ceeymXyx28m6AXK81EcdE2Rje8P8QW1ZUGc\nHoelooL5UUGot1PpD3TD\n=kRKB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T01:02:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/receive