{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:07:09Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:07:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: stop publishing compiled tests in the npm tarball (#157)\n\n`dist/test/` shipped to npm: 57 files and 593 KB of the 1995 KB unpacked\nsize, close to a third of the package, in every release at least back to\n2.0.1. Nothing imports it — `main` is `dist/index.js`, and the only\nreference anywhere is the `test` script.\n\nThat script keeps working. `.npmignore` governs what goes into the tarball,\nnot what exists locally, so `npm test` still runs the suite from the built\nworking tree exactly as before — verified, 469 tests still pass.\n\nVerified against a real `npm pack` that the exclusion removes those 57\nfiles and nothing else: `dist/index.js`, `public/remoteEntry.js`, all 43\nfederation chunks, LICENSE.md and the icon are all still present. Also\nextracted the trimmed tarball, installed its runtime deps and loaded it as\na plugin — it registers and exposes the current config schema.\n\nThe federation chunks are the reason to check rather than assume: they are\nimported by name from `remoteEntry.js`, so excluding one publishes a config\npanel that 404s on load, with nothing in CI to catch it.","tree":{"sha":"4412d6db9f520992b3d666d18b024e4b0e2f59e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/4412d6db9f520992b3d666d18b024e4b0e2f59e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/d0cbd8fe2887201d8a488717f9426be94d746290","verification":{"payload":"tree 4412d6db9f520992b3d666d18b024e4b0e2f59e6\nparent 58b06379f5914d14d97911b4fc40b84699a3a3f1\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1787180829 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787180829 +1200\n\nchore: stop publishing compiled tests in the npm tarball (#157)\n\n`dist/test/` shipped to npm: 57 files and 593 KB of the 1995 KB unpacked\nsize, close to a third of the package, in every release at least back to\n2.0.1. Nothing imports it — `main` is `dist/index.js`, and the only\nreference anywhere is the `test` script.\n\nThat script keeps working. `.npmignore` governs what goes into the tarball,\nnot what exists locally, so `npm test` still runs the suite from the built\nworking tree exactly as before — verified, 469 tests still pass.\n\nVerified against a real `npm pack` that the exclusion removes those 57\nfiles and nothing else: `dist/index.js`, `public/remoteEntry.js`, all 43\nfederation chunks, LICENSE.md and the icon are all still present. Also\nextracted the trimmed tarball, installed its runtime deps and loaded it as\na plugin — it registers and exposes the current config schema.\n\nThe federation chunks are the reason to check rather than assume: they are\nimported by name from `remoteEntry.js`, so excluding one publishes a config\npanel that 404s on load, with nothing in CI to catch it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhjcdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMYgQABYcyKWTHskj1t02viJ5RpUc\nNwEokzakPOnOv+xWmhYB9xdYhOPveME78Q70hPtISmIPk8+2qGT2cOT7SGnVSnZD\nqNWKqW1jNpd8P3NZn3jGZHAmb8Qz7SrDin2KornFpFi25e2BLZsY3t+MgY/QLv1f\n9PHWDPpPnZtudSA6MVdodhdVxs66Zk5OcCUu8Vo9e4bxuPsCr87DnhDDIQsW4oZc\n1sSQg7fawQrCpNM61VbXF9+sGEKyIIi9/qo8+KawfV1Xv1A6auoP2hMmwvaaYLYx\n7na6mtGOsn5LOBDZ4XSCLrymfWalW57KIo3beC4F2iIEH9KuBS39LGBciFj/wU5n\n5mpC496ZV6mr5Ht1+gbL8hlojylcRNgyxNyd7dOOjWAhrmGKwxdbQklidajqrZKk\n+6VJHEU3/EijzGqPdJUR9SDjJvnR0jLmfvth1TIoflwBLNMyrf1PULv7gJf/cWHR\nPu7GgKc+NvizOsVZMVRz/xHJb9u+HUwNFrdshWqKaq9TYelR1pWYIFEA0NxrHTpv\nzuY2WZHLUqJAxHRemzkQwcLo3/pmrgDundL+gMA2J4aEAk2G5hY9AW/RjPIjVLWQ\nwYHRG1uyiR/GQGgZp3Zq6PYwHrUyJCBjnAKMgMqfxyqnyvEJJsYg/2eTAKXjJ55q\nc7UkFWoIVH//iAbRsXRy\n=DNEB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T23:07:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v