followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/a49ba47cfdc15e5e641bffd08a23746ba41be5ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T22:15:47Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T22:15:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: cover source-aware history and the wedged-container error (#155)\n\nThree gaps found auditing the docs ahead of a release.\n\nThe `sourcePolicy=all` opt-in was explained under History API but missing\nfrom the two places an operator actually looks for settings: the feature\nlist and the configuration table. Someone reading either would not learn\nthe capability exists, let alone that it is off by default.\n\nThe wedged-container error (#151) was undocumented entirely. It is the one\nnew error string this release can put in front of an operator, and without\nan entry the admin UI shows a message with no matching section to search\nfor. The entry says what the state actually is — deferred, not abandoned;\nQuestDB still recording on its previous configuration — and gives the\nrecovery, using the real container name `sk-signalk-questdb` as the rest\nof the README already does. It also warns against masking podman.service,\nwhich is the intuitive workaround and makes the situation worse.\n\nNo behaviour change.","tree":{"sha":"7aa3f6de0a60b305540bb0bef22aa36f8be1f466","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/7aa3f6de0a60b305540bb0bef22aa36f8be1f466"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/a49ba47cfdc15e5e641bffd08a23746ba41be5ed","verification":{"payload":"tree 7aa3f6de0a60b305540bb0bef22aa36f8be1f466\nparent fab300fb23f9d3c06121718eb0d4bbf8f0a8de41\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1787177747 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787177747 +1200\n\ndocs: cover source-aware history and the wedged-container error (#155)\n\nThree gaps found auditing the docs ahead of a release.\n\nThe `sourcePolicy=all` opt-in was explained under History API but missing\nfrom the two places an operator actually looks for settings: the feature\nlist and the configuration table. Someone reading either would not learn\nthe capability exists, let alone that it is off by default.\n\nThe wedged-container error (#151) was undocumented entirely. It is the one\nnew error string this release can put in front of an operator, and without\nan entry the admin UI shows a message with no matching section to search\nfor. The entry says what the state actually is — deferred, not abandoned;\nQuestDB still recording on its previous configuration — and gives the\nrecovery, using the real container name `sk-signalk-questdb` as the rest\nof the README already does. It also warns against masking podman.service,\nwhich is the intuitive workaround and makes the situation worse.\n\nNo behaviour change.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhisTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfq4QACJi61azUlgnPrQCPlfny9xA\nR7KxZx9aOgK9CjKyfuZS4pGltpMki9y9or5iWdJ2EF9bQEwYrEb7zP5XDQOtHqcH\nDPbldJDrbSam6rijMXxyJ0Y1k+t/SQOXYjzJ8iAcA9XzEepXTKn7oI6una34