estdb/commits/1dde272bda190ffc3aed310f82531de240095dd0"}],"sha":"e5ec4d081e3f1311d63d58b019ffb3e8e6d64202","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/e5ec4d081e3f1311d63d58b019ffb3e8e6d64202"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/1dde272bda190ffc3aed310f82531de240095dd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T18:51:05Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T18:51:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: record each delta''s source and honor History API sourceRef filtering (#136)\n\n* feat: record each delta''s source and honor History API sourceRef filtering\n\nMulti-source streams (two GPS receivers) interleaved indistinguishably:\nno table stored the delta''s sourceRef, so a track drawn from history\nzigzagged between receivers with no way to separate them afterwards.\n\nStore the sourceRef as a source SYMBOL column on all three tables\n(idempotent migration, dedup keys grown to match), filter v2 queries by\nthe PathSpec.sourceRef the server delivers for path|sourceRef requests\n(signalk-server #2737), and label v1 playback updates with $source.\nColumns in the v2 response are keyed by spec index instead of path, so\nthe same path filtered by two sources yields two distinct series.\n\n* fix: survive dedup migration failures and probe degraded columns once per playback\n\nA wrong-schema (ILP auto-created) table rejects the new DEDUP ALTER,\nwhich would abort startup before healSchema() gets to rebuild exactly\nthat table; a non-WAL external table rejects it too but looks healthy\nto the mismatch probe, so that case is reported via app.error and left\nun-deduplicated instead of failing a setup that worked before the\nmigration existed.\n\nv1 playback now holds the degraded-column flags per session instead of\nre-probing missing columns on every 60s chunk.\n\n* fix: state the migration condition in the dedup warning, not a guessed mode\n\nThe failure mode depends on prior state: a non-WAL table has no dedup\nat all, while an old-version table whose ALTER timed out keeps dedup ON\nwith the stale keys. Claiming ''stays off'' was wrong for the latter.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"998dcf8905901302e5a12e83f3f4d948f5db0bf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/998dcf8905901302e5a12e83f3f4d948f5db0bf6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/1dde272bda190ffc3aed310f82531de240095dd0","verification":{"payload":"tree 998dcf8905901302e5a12e83f3f4d948f5db0bf6\nparent ad9ba0c1d035216396066b71a5587f4ee8323a92\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786647065 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786647065 +1200\n\nfeat: record each delta''s source and honor History API sourceRef filtering (#136)\n\n* feat: record each delta''s source and honor History API sourceRef filtering\n\nMulti-source streams (two GPS receivers) interleaved indistinguishably:\nno table stored the delta''s sourceRef, so a track drawn from history\nzigzagged between receivers with no way to separate them afterwards.\n\nStore the sourceRef as a source SYMBOL column on all three tables\n(idempotent migration, dedup keys grown to match), filter v2 queries by\nthe PathSpec.sourceRef the server delivers for path|sourceRef requests\n(signalk-server #2737), and label v1 playback updates with $source.\nColumns in the v2 response are keyed by spec index instead of path, so\nthe same path filtered by two sources yields two distinct series.\n\n* fix: survive dedup migration failures and probe degraded columns once per playback\n\nA wrong-schema (ILP auto-created) table rejects the new DEDUP ALTER,\nwhich would abort startup before healSchema() gets to rebuild exactly\nthat table; a non-WAL external table rejects it too but looks healthy\nto the mismatch probe, so that case is reported via app.error and left\nun-deduplicated instead of failing a setup that worked before the\nmigration existed.\n\nv1 playback now holds the degraded-column flags per session instead of\nre-probing missing columns on every 60s chunk.\n\n* fix: state the migration condition in the dedup warning, not a guessed mode\n\nThe failure mode depends on prior state: a non-WAL table has no dedup\nat all, while an old-version table whose ALTER timed out keeps dedup ON\nwith the stale keys. Claiming ''stays off'' was wrong for the latter.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfhIZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqr8QAAEedsaVq0PW9bdE69ioJeWm\n4qVVF7rbvxVtw/CfqvD6S+4LLAt/ILtzPvPSRpI002NLv0+wv77NMRdo02ZfNhTA\nCN9MQAlYRoJjEB/ofe9xaU5hN+2zTfIpbRGQbsy7glhOrTOanedj4SouVThOhLMb\nG2NSQSdbu6R7vHZ/WwDwzXqz1D5q5ZZgm1NDZo9/SzzC6CrGd7szjHpVylbCSfnj\njbg3RG37ZZnCE+2GV6cF9IQM9bj0if//qbu7dU3NCzEj3dXj7eL99CSdvdYtm5tZ\nq72eEpvESUEdJH3i5Bufoes2IowTa0jKPi6K1RsyFiKDS8ukH9eg3IBO4