rl":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/b718e0319fbe9139ba655777f7731c359d85d08a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T17:01:03Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T17:01:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: describe path filtering like every other panel section (#126)\n\nThe ''Config Panel'' list inventories what the panel shows; its other eight\nbullets describe UI and state no defaults. Path filtering was the only one\ncarrying a default value, which also made it the longest entry by some\nmargin.\n\nTrim it to match. The default is not lost: it stays in the configuration\ntable below, where every other default is documented, and in the panel\nitself -- which is where the user in #123 actually was when they drew the\nwrong conclusion. What that issue needed was for the panel to stop\nimplying position was excluded, and that copy is unchanged.\n\nRaised by CodeRabbit against #124. Its premise was right and its proposed\nfix was not: it also wanted the empty-by-default statement dropped from\nthe configuration table, which is the documentation half of the #123 fix.\n\nRefs #123\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"61b4114beb28f554fa68a3e1e44ae6ed33c7868f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/61b4114beb28f554fa68a3e1e44ae6ed33c7868f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/b718e0319fbe9139ba655777f7731c359d85d08a","verification":{"payload":"tree 61b4114beb28f554fa68a3e1e44ae6ed33c7868f\nparent 35e67a9fa26799878ca8ff4eeea101bd72552cd0\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786208463 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786208463 +1200\n\ndocs: describe path filtering like every other panel section (#126)\n\nThe ''Config Panel'' list inventories what the panel shows; its other eight\nbullets describe UI and state no defaults. Path filtering was the only one\ncarrying a default value, which also made it the longest entry by some\nmargin.\n\nTrim it to match. The default is not lost: it stays in the configuration\ntable below, where every other default is documented, and in the panel\nitself -- which is where the user in #123 actually was when they drew the\nwrong conclusion. What that issue needed was for the panel to stop\nimplying position was excluded, and that copy is unchanged.\n\nRaised by CodeRabbit against #124. Its premise was right and its proposed\nfix was not: it also wanted the empty-by-default statement dropped from\nthe configuration table, which is the documentation half of the #123 fix.\n\nRefs #123\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqd2DPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+rAQAIc1DPSeJ+BYFwd+klD1gDum\ns9Lkn2skAxlROdXb5rqYKyTmX2fosvJ0n95fGq3g1e+BRuD+cswjFIIaijwAz0sI\nzI7Hx6viLHUqNsPyWAVbCqmny74fSXEoPqk8imP83wGUG9qyuUd8cENLU4hxDScD\nquf7tugjR0Scsl5ulRklMNjBXKtEkvjGUTRvM70dPg3xPfENNW02Lmck8iTbGBi0\nckSfVSrotyVonfOdtgwZfmfEmnm2N31UGyF1a/t+1uh6L8j4ZsUZCAN527hux0KK\nr6grzsqccYjfcRoT47N0AUMx4yTMoh0TAVPUT