by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqd18OCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnXYQAH87/awLRsN1LsPA2xFl0siY\nTIwyGrY219j6aGGomZRq57yyHxOUsxgki6RFN4NBPA+GnSKbZY1WDRv0ZLgLorci\nA824/bmokJq1CAuYVwMVzi9LNXBVEiDMqXvnFbLai95FxcyUgR5rYs2AZzXddgoh\nJPUrk5AT2EwLgtRs4TNDLyhz+ty09Rd6gavbN1pvKl0iOpS8RgBZRuPnANcpNemQ\nl3Cg4dtSvfewkVLuUCgAkVGcVZbUao+u0msPTNdKhvz5vN2S7NtsI8xjr/GSss3o\n2Doyxmz2bO0Mhg7IsM6ZLSK3hQ1eysWuCHcyB2GK/SSarp0Q7iO6c0gV8IR3lma6\nWYcyS+Y8GwbEq9pyL/rD/2fcejv7zgpFIg/fekG/oV+zRL448V6oII/cMBjshsXo\nJQ11fbZPnob6xA5WxwxFpxqkcd9wBEy9qlo/Vknu3/YIXS3IVSAMAeytQxBHsmC5\nArljlwEYXzwrwJfyA7UuoZqF/bVTK+JUwz5GejuahVCC/LKLhKVtiibqxIhoYAA5\nB2ybLtzrTJO7fvhljIEHXlahBXf1SZ8IeO7iDK1FpA0DxoTfDaVzq+EDKwyRkV08\nC11s9cXyB6JBq7SP+Sm1XXR8Yj19JEvdYgpDqoajX9fFnorOG9XjrABST2vQhx0w\nw1+aNd3rEEblWX/BFAVd\n=Hr4a\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-08T16:53:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/35e67a9fa26799878ca8ff4eeea101bd72552cd0","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKDM1ZTY3YTlmYTI2Nzk5ODc4Y2E4ZmY0ZWVlYTEwMWJkNzI1NTJjZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/ed93b56bb6898f1ee69df4b101a1abbb76dd1680","sha":"ed93b56bb6898f1ee69df4b101a1abbb76dd1680","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/ed93b56bb6898f1ee69df4b101a1abbb76dd1680"}],"sha":"35e67a9fa26799878ca8ff4eeea101bd72552cd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/35e67a9fa26799878ca8ff4eeea101bd72552cd0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/ed93b56bb6898f1ee69df4b101a1abbb76dd1680/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T16:10:51Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T16:10:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(panel): make collapsible sections read as controls (#124)\n\n* fix(panel): make collapsible sections read as controls\n\nThe path-filter textarea was reported as uneditable on 1.8.3. It is a\ncorrect controlled input in both source and the published bundle; the\nproblem is that it sits inside a collapsed CollapsibleSection whose\nheader inherits sectionTitle (#888, uppercase, letter-spaced) and a 10px\ngrey marker. It reads as a caption, so there is no reason to click it and\nthe settings inside look absent rather than collapsed.\n\nDarken the header to #555 -- the same tone as label, i.e. the panel''s\n\"this is a control\" colour -- and enlarge the disclosure triangle. The\nchrome moves from an inline object to S.sectionToggle/S.sectionMarker so\nall five sections change together, rather than leaving Compression,\nMigration, Export and Danger zone to draw the same report later.\n\nPath filtering also gains defaultOpen, keyed on whether patterns are\nalready configured, so a user who has set filtering sees it on mount.\nSeeded once via useState, with no syncing effect: the section must not\nsnap shut when the field is cleared mid-edit.\n\nThe same issue reported the defaults as excluding boat position. They do\nnot -- mode is exclude with an empty pattern list, so nothing is filtered.\nThat misreading came from our own copy: navigation.position was the\ntextarea''s placeholder, and grey placeholder text inside an empty box\nreads as a value. Use the schema''s own examples instead, and promote\n\"empty = record everything\" out of the faint hint style into readable\nhelp text. README carried the same example twice; fixed there too.\n\nRefs #123\n\n* test(panel): cover collapsible section open-state behaviour\n\nThe panel had no behavioural test coverage at all: src/configpanel is\nexcluded from the root tsconfig (DOM and JSX types must not reach the\nNode compile) and its own tsconfig is noEmit, so nothing it contains ever\nreached dist/ for the test runner to import. Every panel regression so\nfar has been caught by a user in a browser.\n\nAdd a third narrow build target -- src/test/panel/tsconfig.json emitting\nto dist-panel-test/ -- rather than loosening either existing config. The\nroot tsconfig stays DOM-free and the panel''s stays noEmit; src/test/panel\nis excluded from the root compile for the same reason src/configpanel is.\n\nRendering uses react-dom/server, so no jsdom and no DOM: initial render\nis a pure function of props, and \"does the section start open\" is a\nquestion about initial render. Clicking the toggle is deliberately not\ncovered -- that needs a real DOM, and stock useState is not where the\nrisk in this change lives.\n\nVerified the tests fail against the pre-fix code: 3 of 10 fail on master\n(auto-open, the all-sections state matrix, and the empty-means-everything\ncopy) and all 10 pass with the fix. The other 7 are guard rails for\nbehaviour that already worked -- collapsed-when-empty, a corrupted\npathFilter, and every header being a real button with aria-expanded.\n\nreact-dom is a devDependency only; the runtime tree is unchanged and\ndist-panel-test/ is excluded from git, npm and prettier.\n\nRefs #123\n\n* test(panel): match section headers by tag, not backwards search\n\nsectionMarkup found a header by searching backwards from the title with\nlastIndexOf(\"<button\"). The panel renders two non-section buttons -- a\nrefresh control and Save -- and today both sit outside the section block,\nso that worked. It worked by coincidence of layout: a button added inside\na section body would put itself between the search start and the real\nheader, and every assertion would then silently target the wrong element\nwhile still passing.\n\nWalk the button tags and keep the one whose text is the title instead.\nRe-verified the fail-on-master property survives the change: the same 3\nof 10 fail against the pre-fix panel, all 10 pass with the fix.\n\nRefs #123\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"06ececeaedcfc1b17aac8cb683e06ff1d61edae4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/06ececeaedcfc1b17aac8cb683e06ff1d61edae4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/ed93b56bb6898f1ee69df4b101a1abbb76dd1680","verification":{"payload":"tree 06ececeaedcfc1b17aac8cb683e06ff1d61edae4\nparent 9012f783ae06456740e365a55350616ecdc42915\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786205451 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786205451 +1200\n\nfix(panel): make collapsible sections read as controls (#124)\n\n* fix(panel): make collapsible sections read as controls\n\nThe path-filter textarea was reported as uneditable on 1.8.3. It is a\ncorrect controlled input in both source and the published bundle; the\nproblem is that it sits inside a collapsed CollapsibleSection whose\nheader inherits sectionTitle (#888, uppercase, letter-spaced) and a 10px\ngrey marker. It reads as a caption, so there is no reason to click it and\nthe settings inside look absent rather than collapsed.\n\nDarken the header to #555 -- the same tone as label, i.e. the panel''s\n\"this is a control\" colour -- and enlarge the disclosure triangle. The\nchrome moves from an inline object to S.sectionToggle/S.sectionMarker so\nall five sections change together, rather than leaving Compression,\nMigration, Export and Danger zone to draw the same report later.\n\nPath filtering also gains defaultOpen, keyed on whether patterns are\nalready configured, so a user who has set filtering sees it on mount.\nSeeded once via useState, with no syncing effect: the section must not\nsnap shut when the field is cleared mid-edit.\n\nThe same issue reported the defaults as excluding boat position. They do\nnot -- mode is exclude with an empty pattern list, so nothing is filtered.\nThat misreading came from our own copy: navigation.position was the\ntextarea''s placeholder, and grey placeholder text inside an empty box\nreads as a value. Use the schema''s own examples instead, and promote\n\"empty = record everything\" out of the faint hint style into readable\nhelp text. README carried the same example twice; fixed there too.\n\nRefs #123\n\n* test(panel): cover collapsible section open-state behaviour\n\nThe panel had no behavioural test coverage at all: src/configpanel is\nexcluded from the root tsconfig (DOM and JSX types must not reach the\nNode compile) and its own tsconfig is noEmit, so nothing it contains ever\nreached dist/ for the test runner to import. Every panel regression so\nfar has been caught by a user in a browser.\n\nAdd a third narrow build target -- src/test/panel/tsconfig.json emitting\nto dist-panel-test/ -- rather than loosening either existing config. The\nroot tsconfig stays DOM-free and the panel''s stays noEmit; src/test/panel\nis excluded from the root compile for the same reason src/configpanel is.\n\nRendering uses react-dom/server, so no jsdom and no DOM: initial render\nis a pure function of props, and \"does the section start open\" is a\nquestion about initial render. Clicking the toggle is deliberately not\ncovered -- that needs a real DOM, and stock useState is not where the\nrisk in this change lives.\n\nVerified the tests fail against the pre-fix code: 3 of 10 fail on master\n(auto-open, the all-sections state matrix, and the empty-means-everything\ncopy) and all 10 pass with the fix. The other 7 are guard rails for\nbehaviour that already worked -- collapsed-when-empty, a corrupted\npathFilter, and every header being a real button with aria-expanded.\n\nreact-dom is a devDependency only; the runtime tree is unchanged and\ndist-panel-test/ is excluded from git, npm and prettier.\n\nRefs #123\n\n* test(panel): match section headers by tag, not backwards search\n\nsectionMarkup found a header by searching backwards from the title with\nlastIndexOf(\"<button\"). The panel renders two non-section buttons -- a\nrefresh control and Save -- and today both sit outside the section block,\nso that worked. It worked by coincidence of layout: a button added inside\na section body would put itself between the search start and the real\nheader, and every assertion would then silently target the wrong element\nwhile still passing.\n\nWalk the button tags and keep the one whose text is the title instead.\nRe-verified the fail-on-master property survives the change: the same 3\nof 10 fail against the pre-fix panel, all 10 pass with the fix.\n\nRefs #123\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqd1ULCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoAsQAAi+EFd3XMdkboAnFPVu//Lf\nL9/f4xUhHfQuEZReiSN5JBJxmwCcs/UMYz6Rgi4Fs76nQ3mUYuUOJCdHfpi2CM9x\nauh51fq634ZaPOZ07osJyqXxphqLeRvDeWSUu49BzAilQYZhlZPsSogC/yXdiOwq\nQQtEUhO1TaZZhDDYR09TAan2ztyn8+NLT8QU5XzczpBMntLedw1Wa3rMexLr5In3\nVmzr2pJlkTJiIACXw7M1SE1hGckjXJ0O0hnzXMmUphb2pGWxmIXPDE3g9uH3MYnh\nNdEvX+b23YnN1PLUuhGFpBElPNy/qVROrEuteRMGfeBnGNjwqeIaBIB9cDDzHRX+\nlSJWUc75nfxqsYT7fq7DamafXmQUdsq+55a/POhvs9+xPETDQtwSAnRPmn3c48Sd\nxyZduGdGawB+ZwRmLrUbG8OckpQo1RHyY7/cQ71h+Ypt/08uQubQWRI409M5FnPi\nu4cDXCuPCXpEDIklPk9G+cxn1rCoDdSUWK92Bi8H66Q7wUZvWERKlf5ivYZwIKp+\nwBxe2VdI+yd/lvlybQGsaqMbjNzvCOTEnRlz6JnEYXaUl3RhgXnEZHzGIEKhvjjl\nKPyD/eXiXY9mtfQrgnDZkaxUILp/BFAIlEb0gm2IWDvoWBL6DUj143XjDWQ4s+mU\n1NAbnit62pLSEmGx67PD\n=utcs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-08T16:10:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,