//api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/9012f783ae06456740e365a55350616ecdc42915","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKDkwMTJmNzgzYWUwNjQ1Njc0MGUzNjVhNTUzNTA2MTZlY2RjNDI5MTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/c941205acb039ac71cc3023a3419a9cf7ee37e7c","sha":"c941205acb039ac71cc3023a3419a9cf7ee37e7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/c941205acb039ac71cc3023a3419a9cf7ee37e7c"}],"sha":"9012f783ae06456740e365a55350616ecdc42915","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/9012f783ae06456740e365a55350616ecdc42915"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/c941205acb039ac71cc3023a3419a9cf7ee37e7c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T23:32:34Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T23:32:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(console): preserve chunked redirect bodies and real HEAD lengths (#121)\n\nA local review of the audit commit — which CodeRabbit never got to, since it\nlanded after the last review pass on #120 — found two more defects of the same\nfamily I had already fixed twice.\n\n**A chunked redirect body was still dropped.** Keying \"bodyless\" on the absence\nof content-length alone misses a redirect body streamed with chunked encoding,\nwhich carries no length. Both framing headers must be absent before a 3xx can\nbe treated as empty.\n\n**HEAD reported content-length: 0 for every resource.** A HEAD response must\ncarry the headers a GET would return (RFC 9110 §9.3.2), so overwriting a stated\n`content-length: 12345` with 0 misreports the size — a client sizing a download\nfrom HEAD reads it as empty. The zero is now synthesized only when the upstream\ndeclared no framing at all, which is the single case where Node would otherwise\nguess and fall back to chunked.\n\nAlso makes the bodyless-redirect test faithful: it used `writeHead(); end()`,\nbut Node adds `chunked` for an empty body while the real QuestDB sends neither\nframing header — so the stand-in was not reproducing the case under test. It\nnow writes the raw response bytes QuestDB actually emits.\n\nAll three audit tests verified to fail against their un-fixed code. Re-verified\nagainst the real QuestDB: the 301 carries content-length 0 and follows through\nto 200.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"7d0fdca297e134c1e27c2a0836a73b47957e5b44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/7d0fdca297e134c1e27c2a0836a73b47957e5b44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/c941205acb039ac71cc3023a3419a9cf7ee37e7c","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d0fdca297e134c1e27c2a0836a73b47957e5b44\nparent 8fc9ae20fca3df0a11762939650bef481edadf1d\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786145554 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786145554 +1200\n\nfix(console): preserve chunked redirect bodies and real HEAD lengths (#121)\n\nA local review of the audit commit — which CodeRabbit never got to, since it\nlanded after the last review pass on #120 — found two more defects of the same\nfamily I had already fixed twice.\n\n**A chunked redirect body was still dropped.** Keying \"bodyless\" on the absence\nof content-length alone misses a redirect body streamed with chunked encoding,\nwhich carries no length. Both framing headers must be absent before a 3xx can\nbe treated as empty.\n\n**HEAD reported content-length: 0 for every resource.** A HEAD response must\ncarry the headers a GET would return (RFC 9110 §9.3.2), so overwriting a stated\n`content-length: 12345` with 0 misreports the size — a client sizing a download\nfrom HEAD reads it as empty. The zero is now synthesized only when the upstream\ndeclared no framing at all, which is the single case where Node would otherwise\nguess and fall back to chunked.\n\nAlso makes the bodyless-redirect test faithful: it used `writeHead(); end()`,\nbut Node adds `chunked` for an empty body while the real QuestDB sends neither\nframing header — so the stand-in was not reproducing the case under test. It\nnow writes the raw response bytes QuestDB actually emits.\n\nAll three audit tests verified to fail against their un-fixed code. Re-verified\nagainst the real QuestDB: the 301 carries content-length 0 and follows through\nto 200.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdmsSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALe0QAHaY3VVzjX5QBIJ+6tnNzhTZ\nleUYKaSNM+KC3pssR9k3DuM90ERFqWJbuoC3I9QWZBEMkAZhF/DV1STV35SO18WA\nW1vVV6knKaArkNSEFoi2WEWMJ7yGIDd/CW3ogEHFs1TzejHamEd6F55Na6UhO4wi\n3eUDRaEvENZxKcCutlH3dCtjKKAt1dfZdBUYKvyXPT3k4l3MzQgCjVtZbfb9Cxhe\n5DdocE+i/tte1juy5CHc+rAa92IqjuYw9LYdCqzr5mD2azxrmZhqfRjfGg6ExddX\nPesQYhjv2PB3Z78NPibRHxTYaq/SbqOw3xRNIGEpc0Iy8QM8GNwdMKRGWEACUe2I\nOtPqYCwapJZFWT+DIyrILLx/WluXn35riQ29iAeBBWmQxRh0LIl6UAIl5AzRCpxh\n9Coc1UrjyCWg6D6UAvRwVmV58bQgtkNn4XLlnXkPxgOwtI5zagSlROWkLVLtZrN0\nWiv4UOSaD+XFVLTxL79ryTdHtKoEfubKO7M8UUAptSSAIFz63ZzRdyuwE0jW4m6i\nDKYCgafbea3Wn3sMBeKAvpKLGV7t5dY+zdF3npiVlvOPHtu5yreUHrf2CtcAgfb1\n9FO+bU9E+EcUTJHkpFFyydgdsSWcgHpUNM4Lhs91q4LN9LsdNoG6qbzoJ4JiwFh1\nJuvyUEZsBo/e5DSL2/FI\n=D0fX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-07T23:32:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/c941205acb039ac71cc3023a3419a9cf7ee37e7c","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKGM5NDEyMDVhY2IwMzlhYzcxY2MzMDIzYTM0MTlhOWNmN2VlMzdlN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/8fc9ae20fca3df0a11762939650bef481edadf1d","sha":"8fc9ae20fca3df0a11762939650bef481edadf1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/8fc9ae20fca3df0a11762939650bef481edadf1d"}],"sha":"c941205acb039ac71cc3023a3419a9cf7ee37e7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/c941205acb039ac71cc3023a3419a9cf7ee37e7c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/8fc9ae20fca3df0a11762939650bef481edadf1d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T23:15:16Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T23:15:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(console): declare zero length on bodyless responses (#120)\n\n* fix(console): declare zero length on bodyless responses\n\n1.8.2 still showed \"console unavailable\". The Location rewrite shipped in #118\nwas correct but not sufficient — reproduced on Dirk''s boat, then locally.\n\nQuestDB''s `301` states NEITHER content-length nor transfer-encoding, so Node\ncannot know the response is complete and falls back to `Transfer-Encoding:\nchunked` — announcing a body that never arrives. The browser waits on a\nredirect that never finishes, so the probe fails and the fallback shows while\nthe console itself is serving fine.\n\nDeclaring the length explicitly is what stops Node guessing. Keyed on the\nSTATUS rather than the upstream''s framing headers: an origin that omits both\n(QuestDB) and one that sends `chunked` for an empty body (Node''s own server)\nmust be handled identically, and only the status tells us a body is absent by\ndefinition. 204/304 get no content-length at all, per RFC 9110 §6.4.1.\n\nThe regression test uses a raw http.request rather than fetch, because fetch\nnormalises framing away and hides the very header under test — which is also\nwhy every existing test passed against the broken behaviour.\n\nVerified against the real QuestDB: the redirect now carries `content-length: 0`,\nno chunked encoding, and follows through to a 200.\n\n* fix(console): preserve redirect bodies and surface upstream truncation\n\nSelf-audit of the framing fix found two defects in my own code, both of which\nwould have shipped.\n\n**A redirect with a body had it silently dropped.** The bodyless check keyed\npurely on status, but a 3xx MAY carry a body (RFC 9110 §15.4) and browsers\nrender it. That version discarded the body AND overwrote a correct\ncontent-length with 0 — trading one framing bug for a quieter, worse one. It\nnow keys on the absence of a declared content-length, which is the signal that\nactually distinguishes QuestDB''s bodyless 301 from a redirect with content.\n\n**A truncated response hung the browser.** `proxied.pipe(res)` had no error or\nabort handler, so an upstream dying after headers were sent never ended our\nresponse — the tab waited forever. Verified against a direct client, which Node\naborts to signal truncation; the proxy now does the same, so a failed console\nquery fails visibly instead of hanging.\n\nBoth have regression tests verified to fail against the un-fixed code, and both\nwere invisible to the existing suite: every other test drives the proxy through\n`fetch`, which normalises framing and hides exactly these cases.\n\nRe-verified against the real QuestDB: redirect carries content-length 0 and\nfollows through to 200, the 3MB bundle loads, /exec answers, and 304 caching\npasses through without an invented content-length.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"99de7c823c8394fccf714f0b3c34d93ab29319da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/99de7c823c8394fccf714f0b3c34d93ab29319da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/8fc9ae20fca3df0a11762939650bef481edadf1d","verification":{"payload":"tree 99de7c823c8394fccf714f0b3c34d93ab29319da\nparent b9ccb7ba866b3972eb90cc42e5368678185ca821\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786144516 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786144516 +1200\n\nfix(console): declare zero length on bodyless responses (#120)\n\n* fix(console): declare zero length on bodyless responses\n\n1.8.2 still showed \"console unavailable\". The Location rewrite shipped in #118\nwas correct but not sufficient — reproduced on Dirk''s boat, then locally.\n\nQuestDB''s `301` states NEITHER content-length nor transfer-encoding, so Node\ncannot know the response is complete and falls back to `Transfer-Encoding:\nchunked` — announcing a body that never arrives. The browser waits on a\nredirect that never finishes, so the probe fails and the fallback shows while\nthe console itself is serving fine.\n\nDeclaring the length explicitly is what stops Node guessing. Keyed on the\nSTATUS rather than the upstream''s framing headers: an origin that omits both\n(QuestDB) and one that sends `chunked` for an empty body (Node''s own server)\nmust be handled identically, and only the status tells us a body is absent by\ndefinition. 204/304 get no content-length at all, per RFC 9110 §6.4.1.\n\nThe regression test uses a raw http.request rather than fetch, because fetch\nnormalises framing away and hides the very header under test — which is also\nwhy every existing test passed against the broken behaviour.\n\nVerified against the real QuestDB: the redirect now carries `content-length: 0`,\nno chunked encoding, and follows through to a 200.\n\n* fix(console): preserve redirect bodies and surface upstream truncation\n\nSelf-audit of the framing fix found two defects in my own code, both of which\nwould have shipped.\n\n**A redirect with a body had it silently dropped.** The bodyless check keyed\npurely on status, but a 3xx MAY carry a body (RFC 9110 §15.4) and browsers\nrender it. That version discarded the body AND overwrote a correct\ncontent-length with 0 — trading one framing bug for a quieter, worse one. It\nnow keys on the absence of a declared content-length, which is the signal that\nactually distinguishes QuestDB''s bodyless 301 from a redirect with content.\n\n**A truncated response hung the browser.** `proxied.pipe(res)` had no error or\nabort handler, so an upstream dying after headers were sent never ended our\nresponse — the tab waited forever. Verified against a direct client, which Node\naborts to signal truncation; the proxy now does the same, so a failed console\nquery fails visibly instead of hanging.\n\nBoth have regression tests verified to fail against the un-fixed code, and both\nwere invisible to the existing suite: every other test drives the proxy through\n`fetch`, which normalises framing and hides exactly these cases.\n\nRe-verified against the real QuestDB: redirect carries content-length 0 and\nfollows through to 200, the 3MB bundle loads, /exec answers, and 304 caching\npasses through without an invented content-length.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdmcECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt6MQAKSNDplF16qnaJ1US1ObO0K4\nYRsrDpTKU0p00mZvjbVRpr/kc+KX/g6QIGqIgQoWc2Ge7yVRGJTH0a85+MWEdIar\naQK1+DiFdu8DPP7q8OqXzYdvz0EUDVH5HoDelB/i9aInJe8cvgTArOk8CxTTySvQ\nSQprkUIJiZWhJS6AoqUduZs7wJh7vvrYZBgVR4pKY3Z6DGVYtu4FKiRODWuVwAl4\nz4yUN4zI8e/2yTkeJcSbJGg/MPlotI9lYTewtqehwalfr1OCNEd1VnoZAMv6HrRw\nWQ/HeaFsq2hRXtxsS2hF60N/pknK7Dm+MA7WYqI851B4n8bWxroKt9pjiYOVKXey\nkY6P2jSrcFNfP4yAXRbAXEIafLgIuzSdjr6xl/oVsy6s9Gf/hmFcJISXLrLC8QIn\n8QFXHSMGAsXwt58P23oRHRHLLsfnkMCMvM6oxXqG9NIujoQ7WUkglXGHXDqe7/Qf\nuHoUnxMMJG7uih55gHarPIQQnWkkCPxapLuvDGeZabO8sBVz540EFdTp7PPCEoLf\nTW09/D6hbnNjS17zvzmAdc7rKuG3ciqdmblfpnK5EdZPIXovv9ZOKpQDdtSBXCj4\nGLgzC0fpt/TWB5Z9V/zXVYdwDmzj5F/DpQ+g7kKh2XDIHPpeYvnw1NCnsiduteNx\nM3sYkJINiQb2oLcSh1by\n=InA7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-07T23:15:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://