","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/b9ccb7ba866b3972eb90cc42e5368678185ca821","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKGI5Y2NiN2JhODY2YjM5NzJlYjkwY2M0MmU1MzY4Njc4MTg1Y2E4MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/ad19e752b8164d722707672b7c148eec6bf2660f","sha":"ad19e752b8164d722707672b7c148eec6bf2660f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/ad19e752b8164d722707672b7c148eec6bf2660f"}],"sha":"b9ccb7ba866b3972eb90cc42e5368678185ca821","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/b9ccb7ba866b3972eb90cc42e5368678185ca821"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/ad19e752b8164d722707672b7c148eec6bf2660f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T21:13:59Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T21:13:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(console): keep upstream redirects inside the mount, report restore count (#118)\n\n* fix(console): keep upstream redirects inside the mount, report restore count\n\nTwo problems found by using the plugin on a real boat.\n\n**The webapp reported \"console unavailable\" while the console worked.**\nQuestDB answers `/` with `301 Location: /index.html` — an ABSOLUTE path, so\nrelaying it unchanged sent the browser to the Signal K root, which 404s. The\nproxy now rewrites root-relative redirects to stay inside the mount. Relative\ntargets, absolute URLs to other hosts, and protocol-relative `//host/` paths\nare deliberately left alone — the last would otherwise be rewritten into a path\non this origin.\n\nMy own testing missed this because `curl -L` follows the redirect and hides the\nescape. Five tests now cover the cases.\n\n**The restore result was invisible.** It was reported only through\n`app.debug()`, so with DEBUG unset — the normal case — a user had no way to\ntell whether a feature whose whole point is \"did it repopulate?\" had run.\n\n`setPluginStatus` turns out not to fix this: Signal K writes plugin status\nunder `plugin.id` but reads it back by `plugin.name`, so every plugin with a\ndisplay name gets an empty statusMessage (verified: all 20 on a live server).\nThe status string is kept — it is correct and starts working if that is ever\nfixed upstream — but the count is now also served on `/api/status`, which the\nconfig panel already polls, and shown there as \"Vessels Restored\".\n\nVerified against a live QuestDB: 103 vessels reported, and the console entry\nreturns 200 with no redirect escape.\n\n* fix(status): do not let a late restore result hide an active error\n\nReview of #118.\n\nSignal K keeps ONE status entry per plugin, and the restore result publishes\nseconds after startup on a timer of its own — so a writer or WAL failure raised\nduring that window was overwritten by \"Recording…\", hiding the error behind a\ncheerful line. Errors now latch a flag that the recording publisher respects,\nand the writer''s onHealthy callback clears it so the recording line comes back\nonce the failure is genuinely over.\n\nAlso from the review: documents the \"Restore failed\" panel state alongside\n\"Vessels Restored\" (only the success case was written up), sets\n`Connection: close` on the two fetch-based tests so a keep-alive socket cannot\nstall server.close(), and drops two comments that restated what the code\nalready said.\n\nVerified against a live QuestDB: /api/status still reports 103 vessels\nrestored, and the console entry still returns 200.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"028f3dc58115d15dd2f8e40189b27aae17c390e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/028f3dc58115d15dd2f8e40189b27aae17c390e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/ad19e752b8164d722707672b7c148eec6bf2660f","verification":{"payload":"tree 028f3dc58115d15dd2f8e40189b27aae17c390e5\nparent 37bf1e06dd95ebf85334027bfb295ecddd55e1f4\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786137239 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786137239 +1200\n\nfix(console): keep upstream redirects inside the mount, report restore count (#118)\n\n* fix(console): keep upstream redirects inside the mount, report restore count\n\nTwo problems found by using the plugin on a real boat.\n\n**The webapp reported \"console unavailable\" while the console worked.**\nQuestDB answers `/` with `301 Location: /index.html` — an ABSOLUTE path, so\nrelaying it unchanged sent the browser to the Signal K root, which 404s. The\nproxy now rewrites root-relative redirects to stay inside the mount. Relative\ntargets, absolute URLs to other hosts, and protocol-relative `//host/` paths\nare deliberately left alone — the last would otherwise be rewritten into a path\non this origin.\n\nMy own testing missed this because `curl -L` follows the redirect and hides the\nescape. Five tests now cover the cases.\n\n**The restore result was invisible.** It was reported only through\n`app.debug()`, so with DEBUG unset — the normal case — a user had no way to\ntell whether a feature whose whole point is \"did it repopulate?\" had run.\n\n`setPluginStatus` turns out not to fix this: Signal K writes plugin status\nunder `plugin.id` but reads it back by `plugin.name`, so every plugin with a\ndisplay name gets an empty statusMessage (verified: all 20 on a live server).\nThe status string is kept — it is correct and starts working if that is ever\nfixed upstream — but the count is now also served on `/api/status`, which the\nconfig panel already polls, and shown there as \"Vessels Restored\".\n\nVerified against a live QuestDB: 103 vessels reported, and the console entry\nreturns 200 with no redirect escape.\n\n* fix(status): do not let a late restore result hide an active error\n\nReview of #118.\n\nSignal K keeps ONE status entry per plugin, and the restore result publishes\nseconds after startup on a timer of its own — so a writer or WAL failure raised\nduring that window was overwritten by \"Recording…\", hiding the error behind a\ncheerful line. Errors now latch a flag that the recording publisher respects,\nand the writer''s onHealthy callback clears it so the recording line comes back\nonce the failure is genuinely over.\n\nAlso from the review: documents the \"Restore failed\" panel state alongside\n\"Vessels Restored\" (only the success case was written up), sets\n`Connection: close` on the two fetch-based tests so a keep-alive socket cannot\nstall server.close(), and drops two comments that restated what the code\nalready said.\n\nVerified against a live QuestDB: /api/status still reports 103 vessels\nrestored, and the console entry still returns 200.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdkqXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArtgQALEUhZdA6WygBBynqR94HJd3\nwgy1/VPi50gecaVeJ5oXAGCJl0Zhq8s0SA8jdm6YWsv9rY+3r8xg6EgRlWj1TRe6\n6eyGQ04jW1Bp+6VVtRa3nVnX8K+rTDJ8IA4oCjJCV2mgGGnkRApZqEYsm3wSbkh4\nciMkL5f6boGuMQtUnwX1vKH0O+qs/fmsrD8JDSYkpl4deKoZhlCzZAxGyTeRoE8Y\n5BtGffgsk7u0duWh3Fii5vKSzT3BGXgk7XWbObcacYIBvRPFdoQUQN7DLLQ9MIXR\nCckgTW3cempC7m1SrTC9YrwGYgYRjh9R9vsMxGfmW7fUxceaX3RbAbbmtQnLgDn8\n/neb/brxCfncHry1R6TF71qTweixh5cZqL7Fr24cNb92Cs5dPBDBNDoMmiqQRPYs\nhI6qJhaSN3wNcUbUOSXyx+mhnCYR75bVZP/uccuRMbCOtDyHIWUOnbWjF2TLB3LN\nlHrPUpDgdHyNSSdATQ65GB4XMpHrfoHG8Rz8J96iNNtwi8ugqMCbnZJp2xEg9qnv\nDlTNcES2JrJ0sSAOJzgfDYLXgVzbQ0pOwNugy6CUOIe++5tJTHPLpVpDFWyMW1BX\nsAJ324yb+JpwaQw3K0D+EXpLRTzL2jMx3zxBtyEeQlTpMxTLTyoLgGDEwS3dl5H8\nca+MmY6BcaoFIUqK+mkW\n=Y25B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-07T21:14:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/ad19e752b8164d722707672b7c148eec6bf2660f","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKGFkMTllNzUyYjgxNjRkNzIyNzA3NjcyYjdjMTQ4ZWVjNmJmMjY2MGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/37bf1e06dd95ebf85334027bfb295ecddd55e1f4","sha":"37bf1e06dd95ebf85334027bfb295ecddd55e1f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/37bf1e06dd95ebf85334027bfb295ecddd55e1f4"}],"sha":"ad19e752b8164d722707672b7c148eec6bf2660f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/ad19e752b8164d722707672b7c148eec6bf2660f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/37bf1e06dd95ebf85334027bfb295ecddd55e1f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T19:57:37Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"commit