","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/37bf1e06dd95ebf85334027bfb295ecddd55e1f4","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKDM3YmYxZTA2ZGQ5NWViZjg1MzM0MDI3YmZiMjk1ZWNkZGQ1NWUxZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/2a9a7a68dcc96c42f77ad72ed8fe7882303a186d","sha":"2a9a7a68dcc96c42f77ad72ed8fe7882303a186d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/2a9a7a68dcc96c42f77ad72ed8fe7882303a186d"}],"sha":"37bf1e06dd95ebf85334027bfb295ecddd55e1f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/37bf1e06dd95ebf85334027bfb295ecddd55e1f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/2a9a7a68dcc96c42f77ad72ed8fe7882303a186d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T19:55:39Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T19:55:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(console): expose ./AppPanel so the webapp actually opens (#116)\n\n* fix(console): expose ./AppPanel so the webapp actually opens\n\nThe webapp shipped in 1.8.0 could not be opened. Signal K''s Embedded route\nresolves a Module Federation module named `./AppPanel` and renders it as a\nReact component; the plugin exposed only `./PluginConfigurationPanel`, so the\nadmin UI failed with \"Module ./AppPanel does not exist in container\".\n\nThe static `public/index.html` was the wrong shape entirely — an embeddable\nwebapp is never served as a page, so that file was dead weight that also made\nthe mistake look deliberate. Removed, and replaced by an AppPanel component\nthat hosts the same console iframe (keeping the GET probe, since QuestDB\nanswers HEAD with 405).\n\nAlso fixes the missing card logo: the Admin UI interpolates\n`/<package>/<appIcon>`, so a value written `./app-icon.svg` produced a\ndouble-slashed 404, and the file only existed at the repo root rather than in\nthe `public/` directory Signal K serves.\n\nBoth are now covered where the rest of the federation contract already is:\n`get(''./AppPanel'')` must return a factory, and the icon must be a bare filename\npresent in public/ and in the published package. Both fail against the 1.8.0\nstate.\n\nCaught by opening the webapp on a real server — the build, the tests and the\nwhole CI matrix were green with a webapp that could not load.\n\n* fix(console): sandbox the console iframe\n\nReview of #116. The iframe had no sandbox attribute at all.\n\nUses the same list Signal K''s own admin applies to the embedded server docs\n(EmbeddedDocs.tsx): `allow-scripts allow-same-origin`.\n\n`allow-same-origin` is required and is not an oversight — the console reads\nlocalStorage and calls its API relatively, and dropping it breaks both. So this\ndoes NOT isolate the frame from the Signal K origin, and the review is right\nthat only a separate origin would. A plugin cannot mint one; its routes are\nmounted under the server''s origin, which is why the console is admin-only.\n\nWhat the sandbox does buy is everything omitted from the list: no top-level\nnavigation away from the admin UI, no popups, no form submission, no downloads,\nno pointer lock. That is worth having even without isolation.\n\nVerified against a real server: both federation modules resolve, the sandbox\nreaches the served chunk, and the console still loads.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"deefd4a35b240b4802999a645ce7ab2be4a96cea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/deefd4a35b240b4802999a645ce7ab2be4a96cea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/2a9a7a68dcc96c42f77ad72ed8fe7882303a186d","verification":{"payload":"tree deefd4a35b240b4802999a645ce7ab2be4a96cea\nparent faa643a513239f6a0bb23e4ce1086e9abfdc8f88\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786132539 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786132539 +1200\n\nfix(console): expose ./AppPanel so the webapp actually opens (#116)\n\n* fix(console): expose ./AppPanel so the webapp actually opens\n\nThe webapp shipped in 1.8.0 could not be opened. Signal K''s Embedded route\nresolves a Module Federation module named `./AppPanel` and renders it as a\nReact component; the plugin exposed only `./PluginConfigurationPanel`, so the\nadmin UI failed with \"Module ./AppPanel does not exist in container\".\n\nThe static `public/index.html` was the wrong shape entirely — an embeddable\nwebapp is never served as a page, so that file was dead weight that also made\nthe mistake look deliberate. Removed, and replaced by an AppPanel component\nthat hosts the same console iframe (keeping the GET probe, since QuestDB\nanswers HEAD with 405).\n\nAlso fixes the missing card logo: the Admin UI interpolates\n`/<package>/<appIcon>`, so a value written `./app-icon.svg` produced a\ndouble-slashed 404, and the file only existed at the repo root rather than in\nthe `public/` directory Signal K serves.\n\nBoth are now covered where the rest of the federation contract already is:\n`get(''./AppPanel'')` must return a factory, and the icon must be a bare filename\npresent in public/ and in the published package. Both fail against the 1.8.0\nstate.\n\nCaught by opening the webapp on a real server — the build, the tests and the\nwhole CI matrix were green with a webapp that could not load.\n\n* fix(console): sandbox the console iframe\n\nReview of #116. The iframe had no sandbox attribute at all.\n\nUses the same list Signal K''s own admin applies to the embedded server docs\n(EmbeddedDocs.tsx): `allow-scripts allow-same-origin`.\n\n`allow-same-origin` is required and is not an oversight — the console reads\nlocalStorage and calls its API relatively, and dropping it breaks both. So this\ndoes NOT isolate the frame from the Signal K origin, and the review is right\nthat only a separate origin would. A plugin cannot mint one; its routes are\nmounted under the server''s origin, which is why the console is admin-only.\n\nWhat the sandbox does buy is everything omitted from the list: no top-level\nnavigation away from the admin UI, no popups, no form submission, no downloads,\nno pointer lock. That is worth having even without isolation.\n\nVerified against a real server: both federation modules resolve, the sandbox\nreaches the served chunk, and the console still loads.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdjg7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAefUQAALPAKcitXxCoEPYiiLepjzt\nmdd9Mf3nFt5h4PjOiSLI37/tMQyNHaBbSIqA9uExL/7v/qOU0l3ZLohsWP3HSugF\n89O+A8C8ZsrRu2Z6q6PBfoKuALmWmemwQnClS99IQvP6GtG2B4roVbNoKReEYvGY\nuOR3+PkOWzJ4OPH/i95AM5FGkCvmnwfODgKUl4Ev/f3Wt55a1qCeU4tmUOfd8S+0\nlvya3ZJxkgOktyZ830f78gXS4vu50l3JV3dVbm0vGjQV7Jtcim2pyXTgPoS6VkYz\nUYh/IRH73/t/BQlOvduc+xxPUjJgltUoVZV9T48iEkrMBrtaumgwR1yp6xtd5Web\nKDHUEPFnz2Nq53INa7w6lXCaA0667CnTxuMXGFXzZgXe6VU4EKv/WqXYg7j4QFhE\n5VSiG08rSr/StRGPRVauIc1PETKO4GjSynlBo10VA4J0XY6No4Moz402+idDlj6o\nBVwFkBhvok7fLzBDCHL4RnoY3xnx1rs3PYCxXL2v8eIQtWRYqrX6UqogAu5jOSNh\nlHWl0VWLW3tHky00TgFmm3kFj7R3E+/le7N4+Jh8JMSVqCC0hM4dsKQ93Djf45MP\nEZ2OhB70KegK68L9qD8+cx1keZ+UGa52Yldwf0nFov6pPxjXxoQREBhzzSPdTEXb\ndkwrYhUk4VyvPYXlDHHE\n=aAot\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-07T19:56:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/2a9a7a68dcc96c42f