.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/b886a9188e27587bc3b56c86528a4b0d78cf76be"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/c5a2d5e0c7b179986dcaf71bb90729ef3d3bbcf6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T15:52:11Z","email":"dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com","name":"dirkwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T15:52:11Z","email":"dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com","name":"dirkwa"},"message":"fix(history): cancel the pending playback chunk timer on stop\n\nStopping a v1 playback set a `stopped` flag but left the already-scheduled\ninter-chunk timer running. The flag only gates the NEXT scheduling decision, so\na timer armed for `CHUNK_SECONDS / playbackRate` — 60 seconds at rate 1 — kept\nfiring regardless, and kept the event loop alive until it did.\n\nThat made the history-v1 test file take 60.3s of wall clock to run 21 tests\nthat assert in under 300ms, because the process could not exit until the\norphaned timer elapsed. The plugin registry runs `npm test` under a hard\n`timeout 60s`, so the suite was killed mid-run and scored as failing —\ndropping the plugin from 100 to 70 with a `tests-failing` badge despite every\ntest passing.\n\nTimers are now tracked and cleared on stop, and unref''d so a playback stream\ncan never be the last thing holding the process open — the server owns that\nlifecycle, not this stream.\n\nhistory-v1 tests: 60268ms -> 326ms. Full suite: ~60s -> 6.6s, 294 passing.","tree":{"sha":"dab1a8ecaa7194aa6bd50f24ea39003b33249054","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/dab1a8ecaa7194aa6bd50f24ea39003b33249054"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/c5a2d5e0c7b179986dcaf71bb90729ef3d3bbcf6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/c5a2d5e0c7b179986dcaf71bb90729ef3d3bbcf6","node_id":"C_kwDO