llowing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/3d93816f090c1c86f56324b20a68d80c330e7a89","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKDNkOTM4MTZmMDkwYzFjODZmNTYzMjRiMjBhNjhkODBjMzMwZTdhODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/1e73256840a8b544d3bd16f483c9f50ee0f822b7","sha":"1e73256840a8b544d3bd16f483c9f50ee0f822b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/1e73256840a8b544d3bd16f483c9f50ee0f822b7"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/004af84639d0b94aa22a42eb04bbab7b379786fb","sha":"004af84639d0b94aa22a42eb04bbab7b379786fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/004af84639d0b94aa22a42eb04bbab7b379786fb"}],"sha":"3d93816f090c1c86f56324b20a68d80c330e7a89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/3d93816f090c1c86f56324b20a68d80c330e7a89"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/004af84639d0b94aa22a42eb04bbab7b379786fb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T05:04:20Z","email":"dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com","name":"dirkwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T15:05:27Z","email":"dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com","name":"dirkwa"},"message":"test: add end-to-end checks on the built package\n\nThe 13 existing suites all test modules in isolation, so nothing covered\nthe seams that only exist once the package is assembled — which is\nprecisely what the TypeScript, ESM and Vite migrations changed. Each of\nthese invariants broke at least once during that work, always silently:\nthe build stayed green while the plugin failed to load or the panel\nrendered blank.\n\nCovers what a consumer actually receives:\n\n- Signal K can require() the ESM entry point and get a plugin with\n  id/start/stop and a schema the Admin UI form can render\n- remoteEntry.js is imported the way the Admin UI imports it and must\n  really export get()/init(), and every chunk it references is present\n- the bundle uses classic-runtime createElement and never imports\n  react/jsx-runtime, which would give the host page a second React whose\n  dispatcher isn''t the one useState reads\n- no server-only module (typebox, fs/promises) leaked into the browser\n- package.json still declares \"type\": \"module\" and the configurator\n  keyword, without which the panel is never loaded as a module or never\n  offered at all\n\nPackage-layout assertions read npm''s publish manifest rather than the\nworking tree. The distinction is the point: .npmignore can exclude a\nfile that is sitting right there on disk, so a tree-only check passes\nwhile the tarball ships a panel that 404s.\n\nA missing panel build fails these tests rather than skipping them. A\nskip would report green for exactly the build that produced nothing,\nwhich is the failure this suite exists to catch; CI always builds first.\n\nEach assertion was mutation-tested: deleting a chunk, excluding\npublic/assets from the package, removing the panel build entirely,\nrenaming the remote''s exports, appending a jsx-runtime import, adding a\ntypebox reference, removing \"type\" and removing the keyword each fail\nthe corresponding test and nothing else.","tree":{"sha":"fe7e1ead8260727a09735c73b4bf3171c036df5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/fe7e1ead8260727a09735c73b4bf3171c036df5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/004af84639d0b94aa22a42eb04bbab7b379786fb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/004af84639d0b94aa22a42eb04bbab7b379786fb","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKDAwNGFmODQ2MzlkMGI5NGFhMjJhNDJlYjA0YmJhYjdiMzc5Nzg2ZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/644fdd84ea31d9b2bb94e2839e957cea74a4ab12","sha":"644fdd84ea31d9b2bb94e2839e957cea74a4ab12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/644fdd84ea31d9b2bb94e2839e957cea74a4ab12"}],"sha":"004af84639d0b94aa22a42eb04bbab7b379786fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/004af84639d0b94aa22a42eb04bbab7b379786fb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/644fdd84ea31d9b2bb94e2839e957cea74a4ab12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T05:04:20Z","email":"dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com","name":"dirkwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T14:52:57Z","email":"dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com","name":"dirkwa"},"message":"fix(configpanel): validate API responses instead of trusting the cast\n\nEvery fetch in the panel casts res.json() to a contract type. A cast\nasserts a shape rather than checking one — fine for the plugin''s own\nhandlers, but a reverse proxy or auth gateway can answer 200 with a\nbody of an entirely different shape.\n\nTwo of those results are dereferenced without a guard:\n\n- /api/versions feeds `versions.filter(v => !v.prerelease)`, which runs\n  during render with no error boundary above it. A non-array body — or\n  a single null element — threw mid-render and unmounted the whole\n  config panel: a blank area, no message.\n- /api/migration/detect reads `data.sources.length` directly, so a body\n  without `sources` reported \"Detection failed: Cannot read properties\n  of undefined\" instead of \"no InfluxDB found\", and left `undefined` in\n  state the type declares as an array.\n\nNormalize both in configpanel/responses.ts. Fields are validated, not\njust the container: `status` and `version` are rendered as React\nchildren, where a plain object throws \"Objects are not valid as a React\nchild\" — the same blank screen reached from the sources list. And\n`prerelease` must really be a boolean, since the version dropdown\npartitions stable from pre-release on it.\n\nBoth call sites read `res.json().catch(() => null)`, because a 200\ncarrying HTML — captive portal, auth redirect — rejects in json() before\nany shape check could run. Verified in a browser against a stubbed HTML\nresponse: the panel now says \"No InfluxDB found\" where it previously\nsaid \"Detection failed: Unexpected token ''<''\".\n\nMatches the Array.isArray guard the panel already applies to hydrated\nconfig (pathFilter.paths) for exactly this reason.\n\nBoth predate the TypeScript conversion; the casts added then made the\ncompiler assert a safety that was never checked.","tree":{"sha":"e21839fa0b4aeb026b46eb5985815f00ece30ebc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/e21839fa0b4aeb026b46eb5985815f00ece30ebc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/644fdd84ea31d9b2bb94e2839e957cea74a4ab12","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/644fdd84ea31d9b2bb94e2839e957cea74a4ab12","node_id":"C_kwDOR56yYtoAKDY0NGZkZDg0ZWEzMWQ5YjJiYjk0ZTI4MzllOTU3Y2VhNzRhNGFiMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commit/1e73256840a8b544d3bd16f483c9f50ee0f822b7","sha":"1e73256840a8b544d3bd16f483c9f50ee0f822b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/1e73256840a8b544d3bd16f483c9f50ee0f822b7"}],"sha":"644fdd84ea31d9b2bb94e2839e957cea74a4ab12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/644fdd84ea31d9b2bb94e2839e957cea74a4ab12"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/commits/1e73256840a8b544d3bd16f483c9f50ee0f822b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T14:46:52Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T14:46:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #108 from dirkwa/chore-eslint-config-typescript\n\nchore(lint): convert the eslint config to TypeScript","tree":{"sha":"e8382f18b4a0bed02bc8c2dc5a9951a6c8928e52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/trees/e8382f18b4a0bed02bc8c2dc5a9951a6c8928e52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dirkwa/signalk-questdb/git/commits/1e73256840a8b544d3bd16f483c9f50ee0f822b7","verification":{"payload":"tree e8382f18b4a0bed02bc8c2dc5a9951a6c8928e52\n