ontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/4012710ceb02d242292410a2babc453c826027ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T07:20:20Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T07:20:20Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(listening): move the Play Services work into its own process\n\nOn GrapheneOS the whole Play Services stack tears itself down nightly, and\nevery process holding gmscompat''s RpcProvider dies with it. Observed at\n00:20 five nights running, 09-18 through 09-22, each time taking the process\nthat holds Ari''s microphone.\n\nSo put everything that touches Play Services behind a process boundary.\nPlaceGeofences and GeofenceReceiver move to `:gms`, and place state comes\nback to the main process as a broadcast. A broadcast specifically: a bound\nservice would keep `:gms` alive for nothing, and a ContentProvider would\nmake the main process a dependent of `:gms` and reproduce the exact bug this\nchange exists to remove.\n\nTwo smaller leaks closed with it, neither worth a process hop. The settings\nmap centres on the platform''s last-known fix, since it is an Activity and\ncannot move. LocationProvider skips Play Services where it is sandboxed,\nwhich costs nothing: that path is cell-tower grade there, around 300m, where\nthe platform hands over 10m for free.\n\nAlso stops AriApplication.onCreate running the app in secondary processes.\nIt would have built a second engine, loaded a second STT model, scheduled\nevery worker twice and opened the DataStore concurrently with the main\nprocess, which is single-process by design.\n\nRefs #19\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"161c40c875fd8bf869bbe839642ddadfd3b9feec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/161c40c875fd8bf869bbe839642ddadfd3b9feec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/4012710ceb02d242292410a2babc453c826027ea","verification":{"payload":"tree 161c40c875fd8bf869bbe839642ddadfd3b9feec\nparent 49d38938ed97dcab6b7befc7fce32200e24ea6a8\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1790061620 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1790061620 +0100\n\nfeat(listening): move the Play Services work into its own process\n\nOn GrapheneOS the whole Play Services stack tears itself down nightly, and\nevery process holding gmscompat''s RpcProvider dies with it. Observed at\n00:20 five nights running, 09-18 through 09-22, each time taking the process\nthat holds Ari''s microphone.\n\nSo put everything that touches Play Services behind a process boundary.\nPlaceGeofences and GeofenceReceiver move to `:gms`, and place state comes\nback to the main process as a broadcast. A broadcast specifically: a bound\nservice would keep `:gms` alive for nothing, and a ContentProvider would\nmake the main process a dependent of `:gms` and reproduce the exact bug this\nchange exists to remove.\n\nTwo smaller leaks closed with it, neither worth a process hop. The settings\nmap centres on the platform''s last-known fix, since it is an Activity and\ncannot move. LocationProvider skips Play Services where it is sandboxed,\nwhich costs nothing: that path is cell-tower grade there, around 300m, where\nthe platform hands over 10m for free.\n\nAlso stops AriApplication.onCreate running the app in secondary processes.\nIt would have built a second engine, loaded a second STT model, scheduled\nevery worker twice and opened the DataStore concurrently with the main\nprocess, which is single-process by design.\n\nRefs #19\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOVtAb41trjq+TAdlnevESqHF1b803pH/8CjWE4o4FzX5pDqIPbWDsu5QXlDbjOIMr\nVmOHC5X3zA0yUGQrQjJwg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T07:20:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/4012710ceb02d242292410a2babc453c826027ea","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDQwMTI3MTBjZWIwMmQyNDIyOTI0MTBhMmJhYmM0NTNjODI2MDI3ZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/49d38938ed97dcab6b7befc7fce32200e24ea6a8","sha":"49d38938ed97dcab6b7befc7fce32200e24ea6a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/49d38938ed97dcab6b7befc7fce32200e24ea6a8"}],"sha":"4012710ceb02d242292410a2babc453c826027ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/4012710ceb02d242292410a2babc453c826027ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/49d38938ed97dcab6b7befc7fce32200e24ea6a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T15:40:02Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T15:40:02Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(listening): log Play Services crossings alongside the platform ones\n\nPlatform crossings were logged and Play Services ones were not, so under\nBOTH there was no way to tell which stack noticed a crossing or how far\napart the two were — which is the only question worth asking of a commute.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"19706eb5b4f271ca1a433c4ce9544c38d414fa94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/19706eb5b4f271ca1a433c4ce9544c38d414fa94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/49d38938ed97dcab6b7befc7fce32200e24ea6a8","verification":{"payload":"tree 19706eb5b4f271ca1a433c4ce9544c38d414fa94\nparent 086dc323beacbe5f9b745a3aa637431efc5aa639\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1790005202 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1790005202 +0100\n\nfeat(listening): log Play Services crossings alongside the platform ones\n\nPlatform crossings were logged and Play Services ones were not, so under\nBOTH there was no way to tell which stack noticed a crossing or how far\napart the two were — which is the only question worth asking of a commute.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFG+YjNfnsU/FD9LGvp7PHk7N/mDQp6cwgC0DpzcgiI1C/v68XoDHSqz+6baiSlZmD\nAWIH3Q1vrOKBm0F8fpXQw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T15:40:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/49d38938ed97dcab6b7befc7fce32200e24ea6a8","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDQ5ZDM4OTM4ZWQ5N2RjYWI2YjdiZWZjN2ZjZTMyMjAwZTI0ZWE2YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/086dc323beacbe5f9b745a3aa637431efc5aa639","sha":"086dc323beacbe5f9b745a3aa637431efc5aa639","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/086dc323beacbe5f9b745a3aa637431efc5aa639"}],"sha":"49d38938ed97dcab6b7befc7fce32200e24ea6a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/49d38938ed97dcab6b7befc7fce32200e24ea6a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/086dc323beacbe5f9b745a3aa637431efc5aa639/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:49:37Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T09:49:37Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(listening): offer platform place fences where Play Services is sandboxed\n\nPlace fences have always been Play Services alone, which on GrapheneOS is\ntwo problems at once: the fix behind sandboxed Play is vague enough that a\n100m home circle never fires reliably, and depending on gmscompat is what\ngets Ari''s process killed when it goes down (#19).\n\nSo register the platform''s own proximity alerts alongside, and act on\nwhichever stack notices first. Both go through the same seed and the same\ninsideIds set, so a second opinion agreeing later is a no-op rather than a\nflap.\n\nThe choice is a setting, but only where it is a real choice: detection is by\nthe presence of app.grapheneos.gmscompat, and on every other device the\nsection stays hidden and Play Services keeps the job on its own. Default\nthere is Both. Whether it should become platform-only depends on the walk\ntest, which is on the backlog.\n\nAlso falls back to platform fences when Play Services is absent entirely,\nrather than switching place-based listening off and saying nothing.\n\nRefs #19\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f3730b864092057602e589114955bff1ccd9102d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/f3730b864092057602e589114955bff1ccd9102d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/086dc323beacbe5f9b745a3aa637431efc5aa639","verification":{"payload":"tree f3730b864092057602e589114955bff1ccd9102d\nparent ef82df3a7c053cfa0e2a4f0e97c19bb04fdb9c3b\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789984177 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789984177 +0100\n\nfeat(listening): offer platform place fences where Play Services is sandboxed\n\nPlace fences have always been Play Services alone, which on GrapheneOS is\ntwo problems at once: the fix behind sandboxed Play is vague enough that a\n100m home circle never fires reliably, and depending on gmscompat is what\ngets Ari''s process killed when it goes down (#19).\n\nSo register the platform''s own proximity alerts alongside, and act on\nwhichever stack notices first. Both go through the same seed and the same\ninsideIds set, so a second opinion agreeing later is a no-op rather than a\nflap.\n\nThe choice is a setting, but only where it is a real choice: detection is by\nthe presence of app.grapheneos.gmscompat, and on every other device the\nsection stays hidden and Play Services keeps the job on its own. Default\nthere is Both. Whether it should become platform-only depends on the walk\ntest, which is on the backlog.\n\nAlso falls back to platform fences when Play Services is absent entirely,\nrather than switching place-based listening off and saying nothing.\n\nRefs #19\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDIIWkVVjO1lQVBXKEmCJVwFPpArmW//jzRlQZ8vIWSU5wo2FU3J6axjXAE0+hYmDi\nWsy4AiHvkopnysgNT8JgQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T09:49:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/086dc323beacbe5f9b745a3aa637431efc5aa639","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDA4NmRjMzIzYmVhY2JlNWY5Yjc0NWEzYWE2Mzc0MzFlZmM1YWE2Mzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/ef82df3a7c053cfa0e2a4f0e97c19bb04fdb9c3b","sha":"ef82df3a7c053cfa0e2a4f0e97c19bb04fdb9c3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/ef82df3a7c053cfa0e2a4f0e97c19bb04fdb9c3b"}],"sha":"086dc323beacbe5f9b745a3aa637431efc5aa639","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/086dc323beacbe5f9b745a3aa637431efc5aa639"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/ef82df3a7c053cfa0e2a4f0e97c19bb04fdb9c3b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:31:35Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:31:35Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"test(listening): probe whether platform location is throttled under the FGS\n\nPlaceGeofences depends on Play Services, and that dependency is what gets\nAri''s process killed when gmscompat goes down (#19). The stated reason for\nit is the platform''s thirty-minute background location throttle — but that\nthrottle exempts apps running a foreground service, and Ari runs one\nwhenever listening is anything but Never, standing by included.\n\nSo the reason may not apply to Ari at all. Debug-only receiver, driven by\nadb, that measures the gaps between platform location deliveries rather than\narguing about them. Second half is a proximity alert around the starting\npoint, for the transition latency that \"when I get home\" actually cares\nabout.\n\nRefs #19\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5015241f9249e1739721ca3ec7118e780a3d4da4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/5015241f9249e1739721ca3ec7118e780a3d4da4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/ef82df3a7c053cfa0e2a4f0e97c19bb04fdb9c3b","verification":{"payload":"tree 5015241f9249e1739721ca3ec7118e780a3d4da4\nparent 3703a8dc023f6938cabae7aa01fe7a20919b6873\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789975895 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789975895 +0100\n\ntest(listening): probe whether platform location is throttled under the FGS\n\nPlaceGeofences depends on Play Services, and that dependency is what gets\nAri''s process killed when gmscompat goes down (#19). The stated reason for\nit is the platform''s thirty-minute background location throttle — but that\nthrottle exempts apps running a foreground service, and Ari runs one\nwhenever listening is anything but Never, standing by included.\n\nSo the reason may not apply to Ari at all. Debug-only receiver, driven by\nadb, that measures the gaps between platform location deliveries rather than\narguing about them. Second half is a proximity alert around the starting\npoint, for the transition latency that \"when I get home\" actually cares\nabout.\n\nRefs #19\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEaR7ImftTRfzKAhgUayFG1dMIziTGc8WXP0wmO/o/ap0agILLZkxZeATrlSf57nb2\ns4VA06UK754785aaqgrgY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T07:31:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/ef82df3a7c053cfa0e2a4f0e97c19bb04fdb9c3b","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGVmODJkZjNhN2MwNTNjZmEwZTJhNGYwZTk3YzE5YmIwNGZkYjljM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/3703a8dc023f6938cabae7aa01fe7a20919b6873","sha":"3703a8dc023f6938cabae7aa01fe7a20919b6873","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/3703a8dc023f6938cabae7aa01fe7a20919b6873"}],"sha":"ef82df3a7c053cfa0e2a4f0e97c19bb04fdb9c3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/ef82df3a7c053cfa0e2a4f0e97c19bb04fdb9c3b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/3703a8dc023f6938cabae7aa01fe7a20919b6873/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:25:40Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:25:40Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(bugreport): show the real size of the log being offered\n\nThe logcat offer reported zero bytes, so the one attachment ticked by\ndefault was also the one whose size nobody was told — in the offer row and\nagain in the pre-send list. It just grew fivefold, which makes that worse.\n\nSizing it means capturing it, so offers() now does, keeps the snapshot and\nhands it to stage(). The figure shown is then the file that goes up rather\nthan a guess about it, and one report runs logcat once instead of twice.\n\nThe screenshot offer still reports zero. Same defect, left alone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ec9f18d687edded7fa0e15c09ed5baa8a98c25d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/ec9f18d687edded7fa0e15c09ed5baa8a98c25d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/3703a8dc023f6938cabae7aa01fe7a20919b6873","verification":{"payload":"tree ec9f18d687edded7fa0e15c09ed5baa8a98c25d1\nparent a684e2d9f8a98719d37f6990e7af9d699cc114eb\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789975540 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789975540 +0100\n\nfix(bugreport): show the real size of the log being offered\n\nThe logcat offer reported zero bytes, so the one attachment ticked by\ndefault was also the one whose size nobody was told — in the offer row and\nagain in the pre-send list. It just grew fivefold, which makes that worse.\n\nSizing it means capturing it, so offers() now does, keeps the snapshot and\nhands it to stage(). The figure shown is then the file that goes up rather\nthan a guess about it, and one report runs logcat once instead of twice.\n\nThe screenshot offer still reports zero. Same defect, left alone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLTip9domv1hQ+IoCJbqtrL+s9eABk5ovfIJZD3lPwfHmNcpeQuNKjESBeLmnrp5Ai\nCaJCgyfuvZfy1gy8HBNwk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T07:25:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/3703a8dc023f6938cabae7aa01fe7a20919b6873","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDM3MDNhOGRjMDIzZjY5MzhjYWJhZTdhYTAxZmU3YTIwOTE5YjY4NzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/a684e2d9f8a98719d37f6990e7af9d699cc114eb","sha":"a684e2d9f8a98719d37f6990e7af9d699cc114eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/a684e2d9f8a98719d37f6990e7af9d699cc114eb"}],"sha":"3703a8dc023f6938cabae7aa01fe7a20919b6873","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/3703a8dc023f6938cabae7aa01fe7a20919b6873"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/a684e2d9f8a98719d37f6990e7af9d699cc114eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:22:59Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:22:59Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(bugreport): raise the logcat cap to 10k lines\n\n2000 was sized for one process''s worth of trouble. The read now spans Ari''s\nprevious lives, and the incident worth catching is a restart loop — nine\nprocesses over six hours on 2026-09-21, where 2000 lines would have reached\nback about as far as the last one.\n\nAt the ~150 bytes a line runs to in practice that is roughly 1.5MB, against\na 20MB per-report ceiling that the audio attachments are what actually spend.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3c8d20a1564373797512eabd465263052929ea8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/3c8d20a1564373797512eabd465263052929ea8e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/a684e2d9f8a98719d37f6990e7af9d699cc114eb","verification":{"payload":"tree 3c8d20a1564373797512eabd465263052929ea8e\nparent 87385ccdd7c385c42b56db1a89eef51edcf94057\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789975379 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789975379 +0100\n\nfix(bugreport): raise the logcat cap to 10k lines\n\n2000 was sized for one process''s worth of trouble. The read now spans Ari''s\nprevious lives, and the incident worth catching is a restart loop — nine\nprocesses over six hours on 2026-09-21, where 2000 lines would have reached\nback about as far as the last one.\n\nAt the ~150 bytes a line runs to in practice that is roughly 1.5MB, against\na 20MB per-report ceiling that the audio attachments are what actually spend.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPy7eqFly0kXtdqo7aM7upr/jXUQnvTshHYPaHhZznwQN2cPPb1YuSFA8UkiBBBC6f\nz/ejf2gbopzCjqifVDQAc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T07:23:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/a684e2d9f8a98719d37f6990e7af9d699cc114eb","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGE2ODRlMmQ5ZjhhOTg3MTlkMzdmNjk5MGU3YWY5ZDY5OWNjMTE0ZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/87385ccdd7c385c42b56db1a89eef51edcf94057","sha":"87385ccdd7c385c42b56db1a89eef51edcf94057","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/87385ccdd7c385c42b56db1a89eef51edcf94057"}],"sha":"a684e2d9f8a98719d37f6990e7af9d699cc114eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/a684e2d9f8a98719d37f6990e7af9d699cc114eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/87385ccdd7c385c42b56db1a89eef51edcf94057/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:21:21Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:21:21Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(bugreport): stop excluding the crash from the crash report\n\nlogcat was narrowed with --pid to the current process. A crash report is\nfiled by the process that came up *after* the crash, so the one thing the\nreport existed to carry was reliably missing from it. The platform already\nrestricts a log read to the app''s own uid, so that filter never bought any\nprivacy — the scrubber is the boundary, and still is.\n\nAdds a process-exit header from ApplicationExitInfo above the log, newest\nfirst, with reasons named rather than numbered. It says what stopped a\nprocess rather than what it was doing at the time, and unlike the ring\nbuffer it survives a roll and a reboot.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d883cbdd7655ae4d0cef8787e8e79b4099939177","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/d883cbdd7655ae4d0cef8787e8e79b4099939177"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/87385ccdd7c385c42b56db1a89eef51edcf94057","verification":{"payload":"tree d883cbdd7655ae4d0cef8787e8e79b4099939177\nparent b9c41a7ec21aa140dbea708d6ecb14bce3b34b9a\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789975281 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789975281 +0100\n\nfix(bugreport): stop excluding the crash from the crash report\n\nlogcat was narrowed with --pid to the current process. A crash report is\nfiled by the process that came up *after* the crash, so the one thing the\nreport existed to carry was reliably missing from it. The platform already\nrestricts a log read to the app''s own uid, so that filter never bought any\nprivacy — the scrubber is the boundary, and still is.\n\nAdds a process-exit header from ApplicationExitInfo above the log, newest\nfirst, with reasons named rather than numbered. It says what stopped a\nprocess rather than what it was doing at the time, and unlike the ring\nbuffer it survives a roll and a reboot.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFqis664tIXgL2NAKi1K2XGTgDeIOUNvLmON8pu+2digjGMSNEctclI1xDh9BL32sD\nd04NaTJYS69NI3wib4dAs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T07:21:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/87385ccdd7c385c42b56db1a89eef51edcf94057","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDg3Mzg1Y2NkZDdjMzg1YzQyYjU2ZGIxYTg5ZWVmNTFlZGNmOTQwNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/b9c41a7ec21aa140dbea708d6ecb14bce3b34b9a","sha":"b9c41a7ec21aa140dbea708d6ecb14bce3b34b9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/b9c41a7ec21aa140dbea708d6ecb14bce3b34b9a"}],"sha":"87385ccdd7c385c42b56db1a89eef51edcf94057","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/87385ccdd7c385c42b56db1a89eef51edcf94057"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/b9c41a7ec21aa140dbea708d6ecb14bce3b34b9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:21:21Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:21:21Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(wakeword): stand down instead of crashing when the mic FGS is refused\n\nA killed process comes back through START_STICKY with a null intent and no\nforeground anything, and Android 14+ refuses a microphone-typed FGS to a\ncaller in that state. The catch only covered IllegalStateException, so every\nrestart crashed instead — nine times over one night, from 00:19 until\nsomeone happened to open the app at 07:06.\n\ncheckSelfPermission cannot see this coming. RECORD_AUDIO is while-in-use, so\nit answers GRANTED for a process nowhere near eligible to open a microphone;\nonly the catch is in a position to know. Standing down from there with\nSTART_NOT_STICKY ends the restart chain at the first failure rather than the\nninth, and leaves the same tap-to-start recovery boot already uses.\n\nAlso guards Hilt injection failing in onCreate, which happened once in the\nmiddle of the same storm: the process came up with the stock Application\nclass, so every injected field was a landmine before onStartCommand could\nread one. Android calls onStartCommand regardless of a stopSelf() in\nonCreate, hence the flag rather than a bare return.\n\nRefs #18\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f11ee538d58f9ef0db0b3c2ebf2a8cb896d45fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/4f11ee538d58f9ef0db0b3c2ebf2a8cb896d45fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/b9c41a7ec21aa140dbea708d6ecb14bce3b34b9a","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f11ee538d58f9ef0db0b3c2ebf2a8cb896d45fd\nparent a54e9802562171e370214a9092f2086b6aeabbb4\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789975281 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789975281 +0100\n\nfix(wakeword): stand down instead of crashing when the mic FGS is refused\n\nA killed process comes back through START_STICKY with a null intent and no\nforeground anything, and Android 14+ refuses a microphone-typed FGS to a\ncaller in that state. The catch only covered IllegalStateException, so every\nrestart crashed instead — nine times over one night, from 00:19 until\nsomeone happened to open the app at 07:06.\n\ncheckSelfPermission cannot see this coming. RECORD_AUDIO is while-in-use, so\nit answers GRANTED for a process nowhere near eligible to open a microphone;\nonly the catch is in a position to know. Standing down from there with\nSTART_NOT_STICKY ends the restart chain at the first failure rather than the\nninth, and leaves the same tap-to-start recovery boot already uses.\n\nAlso guards Hilt injection failing in onCreate, which happened once in the\nmiddle of the same storm: the process came up with the stock Application\nclass, so every injected field was a landmine before onStartCommand could\nread one. Android calls onStartCommand regardless of a stopSelf() in\nonCreate, hence the flag rather than a bare return.\n\nRefs #18\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPJLpG1EGe63FulXD5c2JMss5dDNxzF2fE646cXXphfSjSbD1E/EwBsAYzVa6c/R69\nu+ckyHI/7EuheJUSPj+QQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T07:21:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/b9c41a7ec21aa140dbea708d6ecb14bce3b34b9a","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGI5YzQxYTdlYzIxYWExNDBkYmVhNzA4ZDZlY2IxNGJjZTNiMzRiOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/a54e9802562171e370214a9092f2086b6aeabbb4","sha":"a54e9802562171e370214a9092f2086b6aeabbb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/a54e9802562171e370214a9092f2086b6aeabbb4"}],"sha":"b9c41a7ec21aa140dbea708d6ecb14bce3b34b9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/b9c41a7ec21aa140dbea708d6ecb14bce3b34b9a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/a54e9802562171e370214a9092f2086b6aeabbb4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:34:28Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:34:28Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat: recording contributions and false-wake advice, in progress\n\nCommitted as-is at Keith''s request so the work stops living only on the test\ndevice. Not finished and not reviewed end to end.\n\nRecordings. What Ari keeps and what it may share are now two separate questions,\nasked on their own Developer settings page and again as a final onboarding\nscreen. Sharing a category that isn''t being kept is meaningless, so the two sets\nare always compared rather than read on their own. A worker uploads opted-in\nclips over Wi-Fi under an anonymised id, capped per run so a phone that has been\noffline for a month doesn''t send 50 MB in one go.\n\nFalse wakes. A monitor watches for a wake word that keeps firing at nothing and\noffers exactly one remedy beside doing nothing — handing over three options and\na probability curve moves the decision to the person least equipped to make it.\nBehind it sits a ladder measured on this phone in this household, allowed only\never to be stricter than the one the app ships, with a review screen that asks\nwhether a step down was the right call.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8f374bff48bd8650c67b4c4c8fef95f06b8f3205","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/8f374bff48bd8650c67b4c4c8fef95f06b8f3205"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/a54e9802562171e370214a9092f2086b6aeabbb4","verification":{"payload":"tree 8f374bff48bd8650c67b4c4c8fef95f06b8f3205\nparent c9a828e16a3f5e7b70f7bd7ea1a02f68f5f542bd\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789929268 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789929268 +0100\n\nfeat: recording contributions and false-wake advice, in progress\n\nCommitted as-is at Keith''s request so the work stops living only on the test\ndevice. Not finished and not reviewed end to end.\n\nRecordings. What Ari keeps and what it may share are now two separate questions,\nasked on their own Developer settings page and again as a final onboarding\nscreen. Sharing a category that isn''t being kept is meaningless, so the two sets\nare always compared rather than read on their own. A worker uploads opted-in\nclips over Wi-Fi under an anonymised id, capped per run so a phone that has been\noffline for a month doesn''t send 50 MB in one go.\n\nFalse wakes. A monitor watches for a wake word that keeps firing at nothing and\noffers exactly one remedy beside doing nothing — handing over three options and\na probability curve moves the decision to the person least equipped to make it.\nBehind it sits a ladder measured on this phone in this household, allowed only\never to be stricter than the one the app ships, with a review screen that asks\nwhether a step down was the right call.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFtcLGB8HLEW09vljP8zRP3e6kQGiKinc8zHJCH/vU2KdiXEDEK6xx6Fxsuvg0XBHd\ncxetKISMpfuZGM1u4Qpwk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T18:34:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/a54e9802562171e370214a9092f2086b6aeabbb4","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGE1NGU5ODAyNTYyMTcxZTM3MDIxNGE5MDkyZjIwODZiNmFlYWJiYjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/c9a828e16a3f5e7b70f7bd7ea1a02f68f5f542bd","sha":"c9a828e16a3f5e7b70f7bd7ea1a02f68f5f542bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/c9a828e16a3f5e7b70f7bd7ea1a02f68f5f542bd"}],"sha":"a54e9802562171e370214a9092f2086b6aeabbb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/a54e9802562171e370214a9092f2086b6aeabbb4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/c9a828e16a3f5e7b70f7bd7ea1a02f68f5f542bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:34:20Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:34:20Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(listening): seed places from the sharpest fix, not just Play Services\n\nThe seed only ever asked FusedLocationProviderClient, and where GmsCore is\nsandboxed or cut off from Google''s own backend its fused provider drops to\ncell-tower grade. On the reporter''s GrapheneOS Pixel that is ±300m, which\nsettles nothing about a 100m circle: every fix came back too vague, the burst\nexpired undecided, and place state sat empty for good. Standing in the kitchen\nwith the microphone shut, which is what #17 describes.\n\nThe OS had the answer the whole time. Its own providers were holding a ±24m GPS\nfix fifteen metres from the centre of the place while Play Services handed us\n±300m. So sweep the platform''s last-known fixes first, drop anything over\nfifteen minutes old, and keep the sharpest. On the reported device that settles\nconfidently in 131ms without building the Play Services request at all.\n\nNot shared with LocationProvider, which sweeps the same providers: that class\npromises skills a coarse fix and checks only the coarse grant, where this one is\ngated on fine location and wants every metre of it.\n\nAlso give the burst a real deadline. It expires in silence — no callback, no\nerror — so an inconclusive seed had nothing left to end it. The backstop commits\non the sharpest fix seen, judged on centre distance, on the grounds that a guess\nthe geofencer can correct beats an answer that never arrives. When it saw\nnothing usable at all it leaves lastConfirmedAt alone deliberately, so the next\nscreen-on re-arms rather than sitting out the hour on a lie.\n\nCloses #17\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3258f1d1eca69b26ac29eb1a14457f1753bf6181","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/3258f1d1eca69b26ac29eb1a14457f1753bf6181"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/c9a828e16a3f5e7b70f7bd7ea1a02f68f5f542bd","verification":{"payload":"tree 3258f1d1eca69b26ac29eb1a14457f1753bf6181\nparent 4e441687761cd53e06f18e158642dbdb170751ea\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789929260 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789929260 +0100\n\nfix(listening): seed places from the sharpest fix, not just Play Services\n\nThe seed only ever asked FusedLocationProviderClient, and where GmsCore is\nsandboxed or cut off from Google''s own backend its fused provider drops to\ncell-tower grade. On the reporter''s GrapheneOS Pixel that is ±300m, which\nsettles nothing about a 100m circle: every fix came back too vague, the burst\nexpired undecided, and place state sat empty for good. Standing in the kitchen\nwith the microphone shut, which is what #17 describes.\n\nThe OS had the answer the whole time. Its own providers were holding a ±24m GPS\nfix fifteen metres from the centre of the place while Play Services handed us\n±300m. So sweep the platform''s last-known fixes first, drop anything over\nfifteen minutes old, and keep the sharpest. On the reported device that settles\nconfidently in 131ms without building the Play Services request at all.\n\nNot shared with LocationProvider, which sweeps the same providers: that class\npromises skills a coarse fix and checks only the coarse grant, where this one is\ngated on fine location and wants every metre of it.\n\nAlso give the burst a real deadline. It expires in silence — no callback, no\nerror — so an inconclusive seed had nothing left to end it. The backstop commits\non the sharpest fix seen, judged on centre distance, on the grounds that a guess\nthe geofencer can correct beats an answer that never arrives. When it saw\nnothing usable at all it leaves lastConfirmedAt alone deliberately, so the next\nscreen-on re-arms rather than sitting out the hour on a lie.\n\nCloses #17\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPi6OKkJSgMMhE10uY357u8y0f+n1fIpEtgAl4JXCw4TabnkLradEtyY/X5S4b4bxo\nvj9eQQvU71Xr1VEoHOrwE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T18:34:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/c9a828e16a3f5e7b70f7bd7ea1a02f68f5f542bd","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGM5YTgyOGUxNmEzZjVlN2I3MGY3YmQ3ZWExYTAyZjY4ZjVmNTQyYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/4e441687761cd53e06f18e158642dbdb170751ea","sha":"4e441687761cd53e06f18e158642dbdb170751ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/4e441687761cd53e06f18e158642dbdb170751ea"}],"sha":"c9a828e16a3f5e7b70f7bd7ea1a02f68f5f542bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/c9a828e16a3f5e7b70f7bd7ea1a02f68f5f542bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/4e441687761cd53e06f18e158642dbdb170751ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:05:15Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:05:15Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"docs: say what the Rust step actually needs, and correct the test count\n\nThree things the build docs left a newcomer to discover the hard way:\n\nANDROID_NDK has to be set explicitly. llama-cpp-sys-2''s cmake path panics\nwithout it, and Gradle cannot pass it — the Rust plugin''s task sets only\nCARGO_TARGET_DIR. The README now says so, and points at the config.toml.example\nari-engine gained in the same batch.\n\nThe Gradle daemon captures the environment it started with, so exporting the\nvariable into a shell that already has a daemon running changes nothing until\n./gradlew --stop. This cost an hour of a build failing identically for a reason\nthat had already been fixed.\n\nA stale app/build/intermediates/rust can bake an absolute cmake path into its\ngenerated Makefiles and then fail as `make: /usr/bin/cmake: No such file or\ndirectory` regardless of PATH. Deleting that directory is the fix.\n\nThe cmake note also no longer claims only release and beta builds hit it; any\nbuild that actually compiles llama.cpp does.\n\nCONTRIBUTING said 466 tests. It is 499.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d45839a8f084c8bddaf619d4f274c9f912ba0939","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/d45839a8f084c8bddaf619d4f274c9f912ba0939"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/4e441687761cd53e06f18e158642dbdb170751ea","verification":{"payload":"tree d45839a8f084c8bddaf619d4f274c9f912ba0939\nparent 5f8dbc2449ea4fb154fdfaeb9c0658e160f87c66\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789383915 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789383915 +0100\n\ndocs: say what the Rust step actually needs, and correct the test count\n\nThree things the build docs left a newcomer to discover the hard way:\n\nANDROID_NDK has to be set explicitly. llama-cpp-sys-2''s cmake path panics\nwithout it, and Gradle cannot pass it — the Rust plugin''s task sets only\nCARGO_TARGET_DIR. The README now says so, and points at the config.toml.example\nari-engine gained in the same batch.\n\nThe Gradle daemon captures the environment it started with, so exporting the\nvariable into a shell that already has a daemon running changes nothing until\n./gradlew --stop. This cost an hour of a build failing identically for a reason\nthat had already been fixed.\n\nA stale app/build/intermediates/rust can bake an absolute cmake path into its\ngenerated Makefiles and then fail as `make: /usr/bin/cmake: No such file or\ndirectory` regardless of PATH. Deleting that directory is the fix.\n\nThe cmake note also no longer claims only release and beta builds hit it; any\nbuild that actually compiles llama.cpp does.\n\nCONTRIBUTING said 466 tests. It is 499.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLktNNQZH7YZgbx5E5owp7ZtveY5zAn56Ls8Yzmxxj/XRvP9QnSV4eo4/VJTfaxsRu\nHWEdXcGo18RvhMCe7KLwc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/4e441687761cd53e06f18e158642dbdb170751ea","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDRlNDQxNjg3NzYxY2Q1M2UwNmYxOGUxNTg2NDJkYmRiMTcwNzUxZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/5f8dbc2449ea4fb154fdfaeb9c0658e160f87c66","sha":"5f8dbc2449ea4fb154fdfaeb9c0658e160f87c66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/5f8dbc2449ea4fb154fdfaeb9c0658e160f87c66"}],"sha":"4e441687761cd53e06f18e158642dbdb170751ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/4e441687761cd53e06f18e158642dbdb170751ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/5f8dbc2449ea4fb154fdfaeb9c0658e160f87c66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:05:06Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:05:06Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(skills): nudge for notification access, and seed the listener on connect\n\nA reply-capable skill needs notification access to reach the conversation, and\nnothing said so. The skill detail screen now carries the same nudge the media\nskills use, with its own copy in English and Italian.\n\nThe listener also only ever saw what arrived *after* it connected, so the first\nmessage of a session was never repliable: grant access with an unanswered\nmessage on screen and Ari still could not answer it, which reads as the feature\nbeing broken rather than as a timing detail. onListenerConnected now seeds from\nactiveNotifications, clearing first because anything held from a previous\nbinding points at a dead PendingIntent. Connection happens on grant, on boot,\nand on every rebind after the system kills the service, so this is the common\npath rather than an edge case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"99b95ecc4ae0ff4b92f30aa946a31878099b0b04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/99b95ecc4ae0ff4b92f30aa946a31878099b0b04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/5f8dbc2449ea4fb154fdfaeb9c0658e160f87c66","verification":{"payload":"tree 99b95ecc4ae0ff4b92f30aa946a31878099b0b04\nparent 69215f29887ab84cb48780597a8a0262d191e12b\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789383906 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789383906 +0100\n\nfeat(skills): nudge for notification access, and seed the listener on connect\n\nA reply-capable skill needs notification access to reach the conversation, and\nnothing said so. The skill detail screen now carries the same nudge the media\nskills use, with its own copy in English and Italian.\n\nThe listener also only ever saw what arrived *after* it connected, so the first\nmessage of a session was never repliable: grant access with an unanswered\nmessage on screen and Ari still could not answer it, which reads as the feature\nbeing broken rather than as a timing detail. onListenerConnected now seeds from\nactiveNotifications, clearing first because anything held from a previous\nbinding points at a dead PendingIntent. Connection happens on grant, on boot,\nand on every rebind after the system kills the service, so this is the common\npath rather than an edge case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJuNCHDwOpxdpprwkq0S/qYNoSlTirLVCCzMrDgyPhaDkVBbNh1OfVNT6UAi5huq+n\nSlrM2loJqkZhtv+ybaaQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/5f8dbc2449ea4fb154fdfaeb9c0658e160f87c66","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDVmOGRiYzI0NDllYTRmYjE1NGZkZmFlYjljMDY1OGUxNjBmODdjNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/69215f29887ab84cb48780597a8a0262d191e12b","sha":"69215f29887ab84cb48780597a8a0262d191e12b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/69215f29887ab84cb48780597a8a0262d191e12b"}],"sha":"5f8dbc2449ea4fb154fdfaeb9c0658e160f87c66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/5f8dbc2449ea4fb154fdfaeb9c0658e160f87c66"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/69215f29887ab84cb48780597a8a0262d191e12b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T09:44:04Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T09:44:04Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(wakeword): put the April model back, on a ladder measured against a real room\n\nThe RUN 2 model goes back out and its predecessor returns, because the\nretrain never fixed the thing that was actually broken.\n\nThe ladder did. It had been 0.95 / 0.985 / 0.99 since April, arriving in a\ncommit called \"Minor UI tweaks\", inherited from upstream and never once\nmeasured against a recording. On 92 marked takes from four speakers that\nladder hears the loudest voice in the house 13 times out of 16 and the\nquietest 18 times out of 46. Every week of \"Gail can''t wake it\" was that\ngap. The model could always hear her; the threshold was throwing the\nanswer away, and I spent a week retraining rather than checking the\nnumber the model was being judged by.\n\nMeasured on twenty minutes of household ambient (kitchen with four people\ntalking, plus a living room), the loudest mean across a window of 10 is\n0.349. Quoting each cutoff by its gap above that floor gives 0.45 / 0.55 /\n0.65 at +0.10 / +0.20 / +0.30, and 72% / 69% / 69% recall — Gail at 29 of\n46 instead of 18.\n\nIt also condemns what shipped yesterday. RUN 2 seed3''s strictest setting\nwas 0.60 against an ambient peak of 0.623: below the noise floor of an\nordinary kitchen, firing on conversation by construction rather than by\nbad luck. Held to equal headroom seed3 manages 64/53/46% where the April\nmodel manages 74/71/70% — it separates the phrase from speech worse, which\nis why it missed takes and false-fired at the same time.\n\nThe per-model operating points from 56599e1 stay. That refactor was right;\nit just measured recall and never asked what the cutoff had to clear.\n\nWakeWordSensitivityTest gains the check whose absence let a sub-floor\ncutoff ship: every hey_ari cutoff must clear measured ambient by 0.10. The\nfloor rises as we record more rooms, and cutoffs move with it.\n\nTwenty minutes cannot price a rate of one false wake an hour. Longer\nambient is the measurement still missing, and it is the one that would\nhave caught all of this.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"03807ccf57ec3619b250499449da33c605351cb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/03807ccf57ec3619b250499449da33c605351cb8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/69215f29887ab84cb48780597a8a0262d191e12b","verification":{"payload":"tree 03807ccf57ec3619b250499449da33c605351cb8\nparent 932f9f6592562fa99c5bf74d7018f57b14d11627\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789379044 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789379044 +0100\n\nfix(wakeword): put the April model back, on a ladder measured against a real room\n\nThe RUN 2 model goes back out and its predecessor returns, because the\nretrain never fixed the thing that was actually broken.\n\nThe ladder did. It had been 0.95 / 0.985 / 0.99 since April, arriving in a\ncommit called \"Minor UI tweaks\", inherited from upstream and never once\nmeasured against a recording. On 92 marked takes from four speakers that\nladder hears the loudest voice in the house 13 times out of 16 and the\nquietest 18 times out of 46. Every week of \"Gail can''t wake it\" was that\ngap. The model could always hear her; the threshold was throwing the\nanswer away, and I spent a week retraining rather than checking the\nnumber the model was being judged by.\n\nMeasured on twenty minutes of household ambient (kitchen with four people\ntalking, plus a living room), the loudest mean across a window of 10 is\n0.349. Quoting each cutoff by its gap above that floor gives 0.45 / 0.55 /\n0.65 at +0.10 / +0.20 / +0.30, and 72% / 69% / 69% recall — Gail at 29 of\n46 instead of 18.\n\nIt also condemns what shipped yesterday. RUN 2 seed3''s strictest setting\nwas 0.60 against an ambient peak of 0.623: below the noise floor of an\nordinary kitchen, firing on conversation by construction rather than by\nbad luck. Held to equal headroom seed3 manages 64/53/46% where the April\nmodel manages 74/71/70% — it separates the phrase from speech worse, which\nis why it missed takes and false-fired at the same time.\n\nThe per-model operating points from 56599e1 stay. That refactor was right;\nit just measured recall and never asked what the cutoff had to clear.\n\nWakeWordSensitivityTest gains the check whose absence let a sub-floor\ncutoff ship: every hey_ari cutoff must clear measured ambient by 0.10. The\nfloor rises as we record more rooms, and cutoffs move with it.\n\nTwenty minutes cannot price a rate of one false wake an hour. Longer\nambient is the measurement still missing, and it is the one that would\nhave caught all of this.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIG3V2+ORC9jsKjLC+7GY2/a6IK4ZTWdQ2RXYDsxU7Ry21mkflIDOrDXPpiTtRjX4Z\nETI5qt8bOZyFYpgRnfuww=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/69215f29887ab84cb48780597a8a0262d191e12b","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDY5MjE1ZjI5ODg3YWI4NGNiNDg3ODA1OTdhOGEwMjYyZDE5MWUxMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/932f9f6592562fa99c5bf74d7018f57b14d11627","sha":"932f9f6592562fa99c5bf74d7018f57b14d11627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/932f9f6592562fa99c5bf74d7018f57b14d11627"}],"sha":"69215f29887ab84cb48780597a8a0262d191e12b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/69215f29887ab84cb48780597a8a0262d191e12b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/932f9f6592562fa99c5bf74d7018f57b14d11627/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T07:56:09Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T07:56:09Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(wakeword): warm each tuning attempt on silence, not on the attempt before it\n\nEvery attempt was warmed up on the five seconds preceding it, which contains the\nprevious attempt. The engine detected that, detection resets the cool-off to\nMIN_SLICES_BEFORE_DETECTION, and the next attempt then landed inside a blind\nperiod. The cool-off is 100 frames rather than a duration, so it lasts 2 s on a\nstride-2 model and 3 s on a stride-3 one, against prompts 3.24 s apart.\n\nSo the bias tracked the model rather than the speaker: the same voice scored 5/5\non the model this was written against and 2/5 on the one that replaced it.\nReproduced exactly by porting the engine''s state machine and replaying the\nrecording — 2/5 with the old run-in, 3/5 with a speech-free one.\n\nEvery attempt is now warmed on the room recorded before the first prompt, where\nnobody has said anything, so no attempt can be suppressed by the one before it.\n\nWorth keeping in mind beyond this screen: the cool-off penalises long-stride\nmodels by the same mechanism anywhere takes come faster than three seconds\napart, which is a recording protocol rather than anything a user does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9b45340c97b3b690095a39b1130e775a4ed1c958","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/9b45340c97b3b690095a39b1130e775a4ed1c958"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/932f9f6592562fa99c5bf74d7018f57b14d11627","verification":{"payload":"tree 9b45340c97b3b690095a39b1130e775a4ed1c958\nparent ef8b464c5df88b63622366cf2838b988b58cc92d\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789372569 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789372569 +0100\n\nfix(wakeword): warm each tuning attempt on silence, not on the attempt before it\n\nEvery attempt was warmed up on the five seconds preceding it, which contains the\nprevious attempt. The engine detected that, detection resets the cool-off to\nMIN_SLICES_BEFORE_DETECTION, and the next attempt then landed inside a blind\nperiod. The cool-off is 100 frames rather than a duration, so it lasts 2 s on a\nstride-2 model and 3 s on a stride-3 one, against prompts 3.24 s apart.\n\nSo the bias tracked the model rather than the speaker: the same voice scored 5/5\non the model this was written against and 2/5 on the one that replaced it.\nReproduced exactly by porting the engine''s state machine and replaying the\nrecording — 2/5 with the old run-in, 3/5 with a speech-free one.\n\nEvery attempt is now warmed on the room recorded before the first prompt, where\nnobody has said anything, so no attempt can be suppressed by the one before it.\n\nWorth keeping in mind beyond this screen: the cool-off penalises long-stride\nmodels by the same mechanism anywhere takes come faster than three seconds\napart, which is a recording protocol rather than anything a user does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOc9b3hxj0OnaBKFlnqoWTPGsk6l0AOV9hVzBJJAguteBztR78iLZ6FWjggEwiBLNx\n9MZ2oQ2fAQE9AyQGOziA8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/932f9f6592562fa99c5bf74d7018f57b14d11627","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDkzMmY5ZjY1OTI1NjJmYTk5YzViZjc0ZDcwMThmNTdiMTRkMTE2Mjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/ef8b464c5df88b63622366cf2838b988b58cc92d","sha":"ef8b464c5df88b63622366cf2838b988b58cc92d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/ef8b464c5df88b63622366cf2838b988b58cc92d"}],"sha":"932f9f6592562fa99c5bf74d7018f57b14d11627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/932f9f6592562fa99c5bf74d7018f57b14d11627"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/ef8b464c5df88b63622366cf2838b988b58cc92d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T07:32:24Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T07:32:24Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(wakeword): give each tuning attempt the run-in the engine demands\n\nFive attempts, zero heard, from the speaker who scores 16 out of 16 offline.\nMicroWakeWordEngine reports nothing for its first MIN_SLICES_BEFORE_DETECTION\nprobabilities, which is 100 of them — two seconds on the model this feature was\nwritten against, three on the one that replaced it. The listening window is 2.5\nseconds, so a fresh engine handed one attempt on its own could not fire whoever\nwas speaking. It worked before the model swap on half a second of margin, which\nis the kind of luck that reads as a working feature.\n\nThe session is now one continuous recording, as the phone hears it, and each\nattempt is scored with the audio in front of it — verdicts from the run-in\nthrown away, so only the attempt itself counts. Five seconds of warm-up precedes\nthe first prompt, comfortably past the threshold for any plausible stride, since\nthe app cannot see a model''s stride from this side of the JNI boundary.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e7fdbefeff6ea27c8aac234a06c4b16170603b44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/e7fdbefeff6ea27c8aac234a06c4b16170603b44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/ef8b464c5df88b63622366cf2838b988b58cc92d","verification":{"payload":"tree e7fdbefeff6ea27c8aac234a06c4b16170603b44\nparent aaf1a66614f164a3885ae1e9711068b87c0c8616\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789371144 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789371144 +0100\n\nfix(wakeword): give each tuning attempt the run-in the engine demands\n\nFive attempts, zero heard, from the speaker who scores 16 out of 16 offline.\nMicroWakeWordEngine reports nothing for its first MIN_SLICES_BEFORE_DETECTION\nprobabilities, which is 100 of them — two seconds on the model this feature was\nwritten against, three on the one that replaced it. The listening window is 2.5\nseconds, so a fresh engine handed one attempt on its own could not fire whoever\nwas speaking. It worked before the model swap on half a second of margin, which\nis the kind of luck that reads as a working feature.\n\nThe session is now one continuous recording, as the phone hears it, and each\nattempt is scored with the audio in front of it — verdicts from the run-in\nthrown away, so only the attempt itself counts. Five seconds of warm-up precedes\nthe first prompt, comfortably past the threshold for any plausible stride, since\nthe app cannot see a model''s stride from this side of the JNI boundary.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMcMStqUJa09k7cIWgFPlUPDA+x450wOPfyJm/D6qk/z/sQ7Z7zVULXITt4wYzkwQw\nP+OS2oZkTyOeUBdYSLhAs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/ef8b464c5df88b63622366cf2838b988b58cc92d","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGVmOGI0NjRjNWRmODhiNjM2MjIzNjZjZjI4MzhiOTg4YjU4Y2M5MmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/aaf1a66614f164a3885ae1e9711068b87c0c8616","sha":"aaf1a66614f164a3885ae1e9711068b87c0c8616","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/aaf1a66614f164a3885ae1e9711068b87c0c8616"}],"sha":"ef8b464c5df88b63622366cf2838b988b58cc92d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/ef8b464c5df88b63622366cf2838b988b58cc92d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/aaf1a66614f164a3885ae1e9711068b87c0c8616/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T07:15:50Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T07:15:50Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(wakeword): stop backing up the household''s wake-phrase recordings\n\nBoth rule files default to backing everything up, so every store is included\nuntil somebody remembers to exclude it. The four capture buffers are excluded,\nwith comments about microphone recordings of the user''s home never leaving the\ndevice. wake-samples was added days ago and never joined them — so named\nrecordings of four people saying the wake phrase were going to Google''s servers,\nunder a settings page promising the opposite.\n\nFound by uninstalling: the reinstall restored them.\n\nThe test scans both files for every store the app writes, and checks\ndata_extraction_rules twice over, because cloud-backup and device-transfer are\nseparate blocks and an exclusion in one says nothing about the other.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"474d1a7dbad60a50f5662cc7525e98f6e19507cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/474d1a7dbad60a50f5662cc7525e98f6e19507cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/aaf1a66614f164a3885ae1e9711068b87c0c8616","verification":{"payload":"tree 474d1a7dbad60a50f5662cc7525e98f6e19507cf\nparent 56599e15c8dd7eabc9376ebcc1575fc387874bdd\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789370150 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789370150 +0100\n\nfix(wakeword): stop backing up the household''s wake-phrase recordings\n\nBoth rule files default to backing everything up, so every store is included\nuntil somebody remembers to exclude it. The four capture buffers are excluded,\nwith comments about microphone recordings of the user''s home never leaving the\ndevice. wake-samples was added days ago and never joined them — so named\nrecordings of four people saying the wake phrase were going to Google''s servers,\nunder a settings page promising the opposite.\n\nFound by uninstalling: the reinstall restored them.\n\nThe test scans both files for every store the app writes, and checks\ndata_extraction_rules twice over, because cloud-backup and device-transfer are\nseparate blocks and an exclusion in one says nothing about the other.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIW+IooCprD6eA4MiMB8wS9ZRSXl8aveWrMH9th7svA1cx01JZgQmyUfW5PjF5vsr2\nzHKvwf3YkbLS7yRH/qlAY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/aaf1a66614f164a3885ae1e9711068b87c0c8616","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGFhZjFhNjY2MTRmMTY0YTM4ODVhZTFlOTcxMTA2OGI4N2MwYzg2MTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/56599e15c8dd7eabc9376ebcc1575fc387874bdd","sha":"56599e15c8dd7eabc9376ebcc1575fc387874bdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/56599e15c8dd7eabc9376ebcc1575fc387874bdd"}],"sha":"aaf1a66614f164a3885ae1e9711068b87c0c8616","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/aaf1a66614f164a3885ae1e9711068b87c0c8616"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/56599e15c8dd7eabc9376ebcc1575fc387874bdd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T07:06:52Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T07:06:52Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(wakeword): ship the RUN 2 model, with operating points that belong to it\n\nReplaces the April model, which was never retrained and had never been measured\nagainst anyone but its owner. Scored on 92 marked takes from four speakers and\nten minutes of a kitchen with four people talking — none of which either model\nhad ever heard:\n\n                        household /76   Keith /16   blackouts /92\n  April model @ 0.7           53           14            15\n  RUN 2 seed3 @ 0.5           60           16             5\n\nThe blackout column is the point. The old model cleared its threshold on 67 of\n92 takes and cleared it comfortably on none, which is why a take either fired or\nvanished depending on how a voice happened to wobble. The new one is comfortable\non 50. Across the room, the speaker it served worst went from nothing\ncomfortable to 10 takes of 15.\n\nOperating points move onto WakeWordModel, which is the prerequisite §7 of the\ndesign doc has been asking for since the retrain was planned. A cutoff means\nnothing on its own: shipping this model on its predecessor''s ladder would have\nrun it at 0.9, scoring 24/76 — considerably worse than the model it replaces,\nwith nothing anywhere to say why. ok_ari and hey_jarvis keep the ladder they\nshipped on, because neither has a household recording to justify moving it.\n\nThe model also strides 3 rather than 2, so a sliding window of 5 now spans 150 ms\nof audio. The engine reads stride from the input tensor, so nothing needed\nchanging — but every conversion between windows and milliseconds depends on it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"12448f6cb092be2821e8ae54d9bc88f02058e825","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/12448f6cb092be2821e8ae54d9bc88f02058e825"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/56599e15c8dd7eabc9376ebcc1575fc387874bdd","verification":{"payload":"tree 12448f6cb092be2821e8ae54d9bc88f02058e825\nparent f3b7e44496b5488a07db3951aef41aa6d02463cd\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789369612 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789369612 +0100\n\nfeat(wakeword): ship the RUN 2 model, with operating points that belong to it\n\nReplaces the April model, which was never retrained and had never been measured\nagainst anyone but its owner. Scored on 92 marked takes from four speakers and\nten minutes of a kitchen with four people talking — none of which either model\nhad ever heard:\n\n                        household /76   Keith /16   blackouts /92\n  April model @ 0.7           53           14            15\n  RUN 2 seed3 @ 0.5           60           16             5\n\nThe blackout column is the point. The old model cleared its threshold on 67 of\n92 takes and cleared it comfortably on none, which is why a take either fired or\nvanished depending on how a voice happened to wobble. The new one is comfortable\non 50. Across the room, the speaker it served worst went from nothing\ncomfortable to 10 takes of 15.\n\nOperating points move onto WakeWordModel, which is the prerequisite §7 of the\ndesign doc has been asking for since the retrain was planned. A cutoff means\nnothing on its own: shipping this model on its predecessor''s ladder would have\nrun it at 0.9, scoring 24/76 — considerably worse than the model it replaces,\nwith nothing anywhere to say why. ok_ari and hey_jarvis keep the ladder they\nshipped on, because neither has a household recording to justify moving it.\n\nThe model also strides 3 rather than 2, so a sliding window of 5 now spans 150 ms\nof audio. The engine reads stride from the input tensor, so nothing needed\nchanging — but every conversion between windows and milliseconds depends on it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAxqhEo4IrjboJxQI/UxIIAxeZkmCO56590asDGxpMPWR5UDQH4iGN81C5Mpm+55Yn\nCZ/4ox/VOxTEXFxxCWzwo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/56599e15c8dd7eabc9376ebcc1575fc387874bdd","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDU2NTk5ZTE1YzhkZDdlYWJjOTM3NmViY2MxNTc1ZmMzODc4NzRiZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/f3b7e44496b5488a07db3951aef41aa6d02463cd","sha":"f3b7e44496b5488a07db3951aef41aa6d02463cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/f3b7e44496b5488a07db3951aef41aa6d02463cd"}],"sha":"56599e15c8dd7eabc9376ebcc1575fc387874bdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/56599e15c8dd7eabc9376ebcc1575fc387874bdd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/f3b7e44496b5488a07db3951aef41aa6d02463cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T19:46:34Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T19:46:34Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(wakeword): say that the tuned sensitivity is one setting for the household\n\nRun for one person it reported Low, then High once a second was added, and it\nread as a result per person rather than one shared setting being re-picked. The\nnumber was right and the story was wrong, which on this screen is the same as\nbeing wrong: the whole point is that the household shares a setting chosen for\nwhoever is hardest to hear.\n\nThe result now says so, and once there are two or more people it names the one\nholding the setting open — \"the strictest one that still hears Gail\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b1f88c0a6e73925e89ec3cdf26f756f3a0abc70a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/b1f88c0a6e73925e89ec3cdf26f756f3a0abc70a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/f3b7e44496b5488a07db3951aef41aa6d02463cd","verification":{"payload":"tree b1f88c0a6e73925e89ec3cdf26f756f3a0abc70a\nparent 63cf1221dc159b2bd0a545b2ad297ed13fb31be2\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789328794 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789328794 +0100\n\nfix(wakeword): say that the tuned sensitivity is one setting for the household\n\nRun for one person it reported Low, then High once a second was added, and it\nread as a result per person rather than one shared setting being re-picked. The\nnumber was right and the story was wrong, which on this screen is the same as\nbeing wrong: the whole point is that the household shares a setting chosen for\nwhoever is hardest to hear.\n\nThe result now says so, and once there are two or more people it names the one\nholding the setting open — \"the strictest one that still hears Gail\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLAxA2QYQPeFS8ZKLj/CXDGLHWDVLS0K/jufmd64KG347AJrPCKuXlw/1Wm0I2Bz6P\n/biGl/vx3xii8iIws41go=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/f3b7e44496b5488a07db3951aef41aa6d02463cd","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGYzYjdlNDQ0OTZiNTQ4OGEwN2RiMzk1MWFlZjQxYWE2ZDAyNDYzY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/63cf1221dc159b2bd0a545b2ad297ed13fb31be2","sha":"63cf1221dc159b2bd0a545b2ad297ed13fb31be2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/63cf1221dc159b2bd0a545b2ad297ed13fb31be2"}],"sha":"f3b7e44496b5488a07db3951aef41aa6d02463cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/f3b7e44496b5488a07db3951aef41aa6d02463cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/63cf1221dc159b2bd0a545b2ad297ed13fb31be2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T19:38:15Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T19:38:15Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(wakeword): measure the sensitivity setting instead of asking people to guess\n\nLOW, MEDIUM and HIGH have never meant anything to a user. The setting shipped\nfor months heard one member of the test household 6 times in 15 beside the phone\nand 2 in 15 across a quiet room, and there was no way to find that out except by\nliving with it for a week and concluding the assistant was rubbish.\n\nThe screen offers both routes. Measuring takes five prompted attempts, scores\neach one at all three levels, and keeps the strictest that heard the speaker at\nleast four times. Choosing by hand is still there underneath it.\n\nIt tunes for the household rather than the owner. \"Add someone else\" enrols the\nnext person and the level picked is the strictest that clears the bar for\neverybody — because the owner is the one voice that never needed tuning, and a\nwizard that measures only him picks LOW, shows a tick, and leaves his wife\ntalking to a phone that ignores her. That rule is the part with tests on it.\n\nWhen no level clears the bar it settles on HIGH and says so, rather than\nreporting success over a setting that does not work.\n\nWizard placement is skippable and skipping leaves MEDIUM. It is offered there\nbecause setup is the one moment the whole household is in the room, and reachable\nfrom Settings afterwards because rooms and households change.\n\nA fresh engine scores every attempt: reset() clears the frontend and the\ndetection window but leaves the TFLite interpreter''s variable tensors alone, so a\nreused engine scores attempt five with attempt four still inside it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b18c858be841a3d549dd9d79c66d9165d1d3c3ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/b18c858be841a3d549dd9d79c66d9165d1d3c3ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/63cf1221dc159b2bd0a545b2ad297ed13fb31be2","verification":{"payload":"tree b18c858be841a3d549dd9d79c66d9165d1d3c3ac\nparent 1ebf76f24057639ac1a74325f9671a89813b93c7\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789328295 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789328295 +0100\n\nfeat(wakeword): measure the sensitivity setting instead of asking people to guess\n\nLOW, MEDIUM and HIGH have never meant anything to a user. The setting shipped\nfor months heard one member of the test household 6 times in 15 beside the phone\nand 2 in 15 across a quiet room, and there was no way to find that out except by\nliving with it for a week and concluding the assistant was rubbish.\n\nThe screen offers both routes. Measuring takes five prompted attempts, scores\neach one at all three levels, and keeps the strictest that heard the speaker at\nleast four times. Choosing by hand is still there underneath it.\n\nIt tunes for the household rather than the owner. \"Add someone else\" enrols the\nnext person and the level picked is the strictest that clears the bar for\neverybody — because the owner is the one voice that never needed tuning, and a\nwizard that measures only him picks LOW, shows a tick, and leaves his wife\ntalking to a phone that ignores her. That rule is the part with tests on it.\n\nWhen no level clears the bar it settles on HIGH and says so, rather than\nreporting success over a setting that does not work.\n\nWizard placement is skippable and skipping leaves MEDIUM. It is offered there\nbecause setup is the one moment the whole household is in the room, and reachable\nfrom Settings afterwards because rooms and households change.\n\nA fresh engine scores every attempt: reset() clears the frontend and the\ndetection window but leaves the TFLite interpreter''s variable tensors alone, so a\nreused engine scores attempt five with attempt four still inside it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIQdzTv6AkZG45B3yeVHZQwSy45hJ9t5otUO7v3wtkm/Jik/m6or+blQOEnigNxm5L\nwSgI3Tjz5roiB9XYWCrwI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/63cf1221dc159b2bd0a545b2ad297ed13fb31be2","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDYzY2YxMjIxZGMxNTliMmJkMGE1NDViMmFkMjk3ZWQxM2ZiMzFiZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/1ebf76f24057639ac1a74325f9671a89813b93c7","sha":"1ebf76f24057639ac1a74325f9671a89813b93c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/1ebf76f24057639ac1a74325f9671a89813b93c7"}],"sha":"63cf1221dc159b2bd0a545b2ad297ed13fb31be2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/63cf1221dc159b2bd0a545b2ad297ed13fb31be2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/1ebf76f24057639ac1a74325f9671a89813b93c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T19:32:35Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T19:32:35Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"docs(wakeword): spec the sensitivity tuning screen\n\nThree words with nothing behind them, and 2026-09-13 showed the wrong choice\nexcludes people rather than merely annoying them. The screen offers the measured\nroute or a plain pick between the three levels, skips to MEDIUM in the wizard,\nand is reachable from settings afterwards because households change.\n\nRecords the two constraints that cost an hour to find: the native engine cannot\nbe reused between attempts, since reset() leaves the interpreter''s variable\ntensors alone; and free choice between the three levels is safe only for as long\nas all three detect nothing on the kitchen negative.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7da5fbd290de40579a03c287e04375b55ead1c20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/7da5fbd290de40579a03c287e04375b55ead1c20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/1ebf76f24057639ac1a74325f9671a89813b93c7","verification":{"payload":"tree 7da5fbd290de40579a03c287e04375b55ead1c20\nparent 7fc6b9bf2512b5b5d62da90d4b5420da2380fe48\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789327955 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789327955 +0100\n\ndocs(wakeword): spec the sensitivity tuning screen\n\nThree words with nothing behind them, and 2026-09-13 showed the wrong choice\nexcludes people rather than merely annoying them. The screen offers the measured\nroute or a plain pick between the three levels, skips to MEDIUM in the wizard,\nand is reachable from settings afterwards because households change.\n\nRecords the two constraints that cost an hour to find: the native engine cannot\nbe reused between attempts, since reset() leaves the interpreter''s variable\ntensors alone; and free choice between the three levels is safe only for as long\nas all three detect nothing on the kitchen negative.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLNfDBaVPZRmx/duYIV99wfPAzZ9rWG1EnB+f+Esw7uNLbW8OWfd2eyKlXJr8mIYZV\novZokkYxljGbxcQGbLTAo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/1ebf76f24057639ac1a74325f9671a89813b93c7","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDFlYmY3NmYyNDA1NzYzOWFjMWE3NDMyNWY5NjcxYTg5ODEzYjkzYzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/7fc6b9bf2512b5b5d62da90d4b5420da2380fe48","sha":"7fc6b9bf2512b5b5d62da90d4b5420da2380fe48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/7fc6b9bf2512b5b5d62da90d4b5420da2380fe48"}],"sha":"1ebf76f24057639ac1a74325f9671a89813b93c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/1ebf76f24057639ac1a74325f9671a89813b93c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/7fc6b9bf2512b5b5d62da90d4b5420da2380fe48/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T19:22:56Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T19:22:56Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"docs(wakeword): correct the sensitivity table to the segment-scored numbers\n\nThe table came from scoring clips cut out of each recording, which cold-starts a\nstreaming model at every clip boundary and flatters or punishes a setting\ndepending on where the cuts fell. Scored across the continuous recording, as the\nphone hears it, the ordering survives but the drama does not: the speaker the\nprevious note said was heard \"once in fifteen tries\" at the old default is\nheard six times in fifteen.\n\nThe ladder is unchanged — it is still the best of the four columns for every\nspeaker measured. The claim that it rescues anybody is withdrawn: at 0.9 the two\nnew speakers are still missed a third of the time standing next to the phone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"95d1234dd46979a87c60b566ae613892e9329b9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/95d1234dd46979a87c60b566ae613892e9329b9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/7fc6b9bf2512b5b5d62da90d4b5420da2380fe48","verification":{"payload":"tree 95d1234dd46979a87c60b566ae613892e9329b9e\nparent 8eade231c83e46633054691e5e037692f4a0bca3\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789327376 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789327376 +0100\n\ndocs(wakeword): correct the sensitivity table to the segment-scored numbers\n\nThe table came from scoring clips cut out of each recording, which cold-starts a\nstreaming model at every clip boundary and flatters or punishes a setting\ndepending on where the cuts fell. Scored across the continuous recording, as the\nphone hears it, the ordering survives but the drama does not: the speaker the\nprevious note said was heard \"once in fifteen tries\" at the old default is\nheard six times in fifteen.\n\nThe ladder is unchanged — it is still the best of the four columns for every\nspeaker measured. The claim that it rescues anybody is withdrawn: at 0.9 the two\nnew speakers are still missed a third of the time standing next to the phone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQISCSjyOrzYTIRUOn0NJC8TMmGv/DgIY4Y3/bfgxj8eM7D1+0veDp4+1D2RO4petCf\nsTsPbyRspV8PPMNNoRBAM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/7fc6b9bf2512b5b5d62da90d4b5420da2380fe48","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDdmYzZiOWJmMjUxMmI1YjVkNjJkYTkwZDRiNTQyMGRhMjM4MGZlNDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/8eade231c83e46633054691e5e037692f4a0bca3","sha":"8eade231c83e46633054691e5e037692f4a0bca3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/8eade231c83e46633054691e5e037692f4a0bca3"}],"sha":"7fc6b9bf2512b5b5d62da90d4b5420da2380fe48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/7fc6b9bf2512b5b5d62da90d4b5420da2380fe48"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/8eade231c83e46633054691e5e037692f4a0bca3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T18:35:39Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T18:35:39Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(wakeword): move HIGH to 0.9, now that a real negative can price it\n\nThe 16 hand-picked false accepts saturate below 0.99, so every earlier number\nwas blind in exactly the range where the second speaker''s problem gets solved.\nTwo measurements fixed that: ten minutes of four people talking round a kitchen\ntable with nobody saying the phrase, and the 162-hour span of the captured\naccepts themselves.\n\nAt 0.9 / 5, against take counts the speaker marked herself:\n\n  near        56% -> 88%\n  mid-room    33% -> 60%\n  across room 20% -> 47%\n\nThe first speaker goes 19/20 to 20/20. Of the 16 false accepts that actually\noccurred, 14 already fired at the setting shipped for months and 15 fire at 0.9;\nthe kitchen recording detects nothing at any cutoff at or above 0.7, its loudest\nmoment reaching 0.59.\n\nMEDIUM and LOW are untouched. HIGH is the end of the ladder a user has to pick\ndeliberately, and its description now says what it is actually for rather than\nwarning it belongs in very quiet rooms, which the kitchen recording disproves.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f436f6143194e89564742e9a63a7e9d86b33e272","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/f436f6143194e89564742e9a63a7e9d86b33e272"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/8eade231c83e46633054691e5e037692f4a0bca3","verification":{"payload":"tree f436f6143194e89564742e9a63a7e9d86b33e272\nparent 1a4597d0b5b274aee6161db5e0d37c4e7c423945\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789324539 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789324539 +0100\n\nfeat(wakeword): move HIGH to 0.9, now that a real negative can price it\n\nThe 16 hand-picked false accepts saturate below 0.99, so every earlier number\nwas blind in exactly the range where the second speaker''s problem gets solved.\nTwo measurements fixed that: ten minutes of four people talking round a kitchen\ntable with nobody saying the phrase, and the 162-hour span of the captured\naccepts themselves.\n\nAt 0.9 / 5, against take counts the speaker marked herself:\n\n  near        56% -> 88%\n  mid-room    33% -> 60%\n  across room 20% -> 47%\n\nThe first speaker goes 19/20 to 20/20. Of the 16 false accepts that actually\noccurred, 14 already fired at the setting shipped for months and 15 fire at 0.9;\nthe kitchen recording detects nothing at any cutoff at or above 0.7, its loudest\nmoment reaching 0.59.\n\nMEDIUM and LOW are untouched. HIGH is the end of the ladder a user has to pick\ndeliberately, and its description now says what it is actually for rather than\nwarning it belongs in very quiet rooms, which the kitchen recording disproves.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHeb8jNn7UBO5Fo8j+FxkeeLH6GZtr44nvT3ZFnQ9kCs2a57lIsrnvBPOBEEZvw7iJ\ngCcB3NfDh0iejE5t4NSQM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/8eade231c83e46633054691e5e037692f4a0bca3","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDhlYWRlMjMxYzgzZTQ2NjMzMDU0NjkxZTVlMDM3NjkyZjRhMGJjYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/1a4597d0b5b274aee6161db5e0d37c4e7c423945","sha":"1a4597d0b5b274aee6161db5e0d37c4e7c423945","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/1a4597d0b5b274aee6161db5e0d37c4e7c423945"}],"sha":"8eade231c83e46633054691e5e037692f4a0bca3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/8eade231c83e46633054691e5e037692f4a0bca3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/1a4597d0b5b274aee6161db5e0d37c4e7c423945/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T18:06:37Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T18:06:37Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(wakeword): show whether a recording is loud enough to be worth keeping\n\nTen minutes of a living room with the television on came back with 1% of its\naudio at speaking level, against 15-53% for every recording that turned out to\nbe usable. Nothing on screen said so: a level meter that never rises looks\nexactly like a level meter in a quiet moment, and the recording was only found\nto be worthless after it had been pulled off the phone and scored.\n\nThe running share is now on screen while recording, and a warning appears below\n10% once the recording is long enough for that to mean anything. Same threshold\nthe take counter already uses, so one yardstick rather than two.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"959900ccd3e03aa529a98a07914fff512b18b4e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/959900ccd3e03aa529a98a07914fff512b18b4e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/1a4597d0b5b274aee6161db5e0d37c4e7c423945","verification":{"payload":"tree 959900ccd3e03aa529a98a07914fff512b18b4e8\nparent f6424c67a96d8d5bdf711daf174845e6e6456b55\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789322797 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789322797 +0100\n\nfeat(wakeword): show whether a recording is loud enough to be worth keeping\n\nTen minutes of a living room with the television on came back with 1% of its\naudio at speaking level, against 15-53% for every recording that turned out to\nbe usable. Nothing on screen said so: a level meter that never rises looks\nexactly like a level meter in a quiet moment, and the recording was only found\nto be worthless after it had been pulled off the phone and scored.\n\nThe running share is now on screen while recording, and a warning appears below\n10% once the recording is long enough for that to mean anything. Same threshold\nthe take counter already uses, so one yardstick rather than two.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQE3u30WBMKwHVIT8AgapsdYIjyFzijdJn/33Opcjv7k9/TXFWD2CEshwIwpcW0fUHd\nUJH1TdIn9vTQhqn7dASgY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/1a4597d0b5b274aee6161db5e0d37c4e7c423945","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDFhNDU5N2QwYjViMjc0YWVlNjE2MWRiNWUwZDM3YzRlN2M0MjM5NDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/f6424c67a96d8d5bdf711daf174845e6e6456b55","sha":"f6424c67a96d8d5bdf711daf174845e6e6456b55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/f6424c67a96d8d5bdf711daf174845e6e6456b55"}],"sha":"1a4597d0b5b274aee6161db5e0d37c4e7c423945","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/1a4597d0b5b274aee6161db5e0d37c4e7c423945"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/f6424c67a96d8d5bdf711daf174845e6e6456b55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T16:27:59Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T16:27:59Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(wakeword): mark takes while recording, and make the countdown optional\n\nRecall numbers from these recordings are only as good as their denominator, and\nuntil now the denominator was an energy split guessing which bursts were the\nphrase. It counts the telly, a cough and the other person in the room, so every\npercentage computed from a segment was directional at best.\n\nThe mark button is optional and records milliseconds from the start of the\nrecording into the sidecar. Nothing changes for a speaker who ignores it: an\nunmarked segment writes no `marks:` line at all, because \"nobody tapped the\nbutton\" and \"the speaker said it zero times\" must not read the same.\n\nThe countdown is now opt-in rather than fixed at ten seconds. It exists for\nacross-the-room takes where somebody has to walk; beside the phone it is ten\nseconds of dead air in every file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4330b22a0b4af7a278701e51a1338d54ae37a89f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/4330b22a0b4af7a278701e51a1338d54ae37a89f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/f6424c67a96d8d5bdf711daf174845e6e6456b55","verification":{"payload":"tree 4330b22a0b4af7a278701e51a1338d54ae37a89f\nparent 1afd5d42d6072f9b2af81f895ffa26a0a9aee4e7\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789230479 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789230479 +0100\n\nfeat(wakeword): mark takes while recording, and make the countdown optional\n\nRecall numbers from these recordings are only as good as their denominator, and\nuntil now the denominator was an energy split guessing which bursts were the\nphrase. It counts the telly, a cough and the other person in the room, so every\npercentage computed from a segment was directional at best.\n\nThe mark button is optional and records milliseconds from the start of the\nrecording into the sidecar. Nothing changes for a speaker who ignores it: an\nunmarked segment writes no `marks:` line at all, because \"nobody tapped the\nbutton\" and \"the speaker said it zero times\" must not read the same.\n\nThe countdown is now opt-in rather than fixed at ten seconds. It exists for\nacross-the-room takes where somebody has to walk; beside the phone it is ten\nseconds of dead air in every file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLWrmtUxoKxq5He6c7ajvYZq4E0Sy05IxfHVxONcF+aTl8hPK3itV3glAZmI+k+LTM\naXQ41EgR5hG5dj86juzwQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/f6424c67a96d8d5bdf711daf174845e6e6456b55","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGY2NDI0YzY3YTk2ZDhkNWJkZjcxMWRhZjE3NDg0NWU2ZTY0NTZiNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/1afd5d42d6072f9b2af81f895ffa26a0a9aee4e7","sha":"1afd5d42d6072f9b2af81f895ffa26a0a9aee4e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/1afd5d42d6072f9b2af81f895ffa26a0a9aee4e7"}],"sha":"f6424c67a96d8d5bdf711daf174845e6e6456b55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/f6424c67a96d8d5bdf711daf174845e6e6456b55"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/1afd5d42d6072f9b2af81f895ffa26a0a9aee4e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T16:11:14Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T16:11:14Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(wakeword): let the FileProvider serve the wake-sample recordings\n\nExport built a content URI for every clip in wake-samples, but that directory\nwas never declared in capture_paths.xml, so getUriForFile threw straight out of\nthe click handler and killed the app. The recordings survived; there was just no\nway to get them off the phone, which is the one thing the recorder exists for.\n\nThe test scans both directions, because a store nobody can export and a grant\nnobody uses fail in opposite ways and neither shows up until someone taps the\nbutton.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"038545111dedf620256ce863714619b50b73a343","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/038545111dedf620256ce863714619b50b73a343"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/1afd5d42d6072f9b2af81f895ffa26a0a9aee4e7","verification":{"payload":"tree 038545111dedf620256ce863714619b50b73a343\nparent d4a737d161d79ef8cc4f9613aca651a8d10bba2f\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789229474 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789229474 +0100\n\nfix(wakeword): let the FileProvider serve the wake-sample recordings\n\nExport built a content URI for every clip in wake-samples, but that directory\nwas never declared in capture_paths.xml, so getUriForFile threw straight out of\nthe click handler and killed the app. The recordings survived; there was just no\nway to get them off the phone, which is the one thing the recorder exists for.\n\nThe test scans both directions, because a store nobody can export and a grant\nnobody uses fail in opposite ways and neither shows up until someone taps the\nbutton.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDQb2q0X3/fNZAviIOaljzoOdfdGBi+VoZcSm5pJghJm1+z/wubSKbtUjcjanuJ3sQ\npDtZpY+9Ymi+SWhCf0igg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/1afd5d42d6072f9b2af81f895ffa26a0a9aee4e7","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDFhZmQ1ZDQyZDYwNzJmOWIyYWY4MWY4OTVmZmEyNmEwYTlhZWU0ZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/d4a737d161d79ef8cc4f9613aca651a8d10bba2f","sha":"d4a737d161d79ef8cc4f9613aca651a8d10bba2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/d4a737d161d79ef8cc4f9613aca651a8d10bba2f"}],"sha":"1afd5d42d6072f9b2af81f895ffa26a0a9aee4e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/1afd5d42d6072f9b2af81f895ffa26a0a9aee4e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/d4a737d161d79ef8cc4f9613aca651a8d10bba2f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:28:11Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:28:11Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(wakeword): re-pitch the sensitivity ladder around window, not cutoff\n\nThe old shape was built to catch the wrong thing. It loosened the cutoff and\nlengthened the window together, so strictness meant \"the score must stay high\nacross a long stretch\" — which is exactly what ambient noise does. Vague but\npersistent. A real spoken word is the reverse: convincing, and brief. Asking\nfor persistence let the television through and shut out anyone who says the\nphrase a little quicker or quieter than I do.\n\nStrictness now rides on the window, with the cutoff pinned near the ceiling.\n\nMeasured on 20 recordings of speaker A, 15 of speaker B, and 16 real captured\nfalse accepts (ari-tools/wakeword/baseline/):\n\n  setting  was          speaker A      speaker B        false accepts\n  HIGH     0.95 / 5     100% -> 95%    100% -> 93.3%    15/16 -> 13/16\n  MEDIUM   0.985 / 10    95% -> 95%    66.7% -> 86.7%   14/16 -> 10/16\n  LOW      0.99 / 14     90% -> 90%    13.3% -> 40%     10/16 -> 9/16\n\nEvery level improves or holds on both axes. At the default, speaker B gains 20\npoints while false accepts drop by four. LOW stops being the setting that\nignores her almost entirely.\n\nThis came out of a sweep run while evaluating retrained models. None of those\nbeat the incumbent; the incumbent being operated badly turned out to be the\nbigger finding, and it needed no retraining at all. It is also section 7 of the\nretrain design arriving early: that noted the app overrides each model''s own\noperating point with this enum, and filed it as a blocker for shipping a new\nmodel. It was already a defect in the shipped one.\n\nTests cover the invariant rather than restating the constants: strictness must\nincrease down the ladder, and every level must survive int8 quantisation as a\ndistinct threshold — there is very little room up there, and 0.9981 and above\nall collapse onto the same byte.\n\nCaveat on the record: speaker B''s recordings are near-field, one room, one\nsession. Direction solid, magnitudes provisional.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e3c450ee74082163e9ffc4c30fb1212ba14865f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/9e3c450ee74082163e9ffc4c30fb1212ba14865f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/d4a737d161d79ef8cc4f9613aca651a8d10bba2f","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e3c450ee74082163e9ffc4c30fb1212ba14865f\nparent b6f508079dbf079f8b8b0a379fdd8d1dd71bb916\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789129691 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789129691 +0100\n\nfix(wakeword): re-pitch the sensitivity ladder around window, not cutoff\n\nThe old shape was built to catch the wrong thing. It loosened the cutoff and\nlengthened the window together, so strictness meant \"the score must stay high\nacross a long stretch\" — which is exactly what ambient noise does. Vague but\npersistent. A real spoken word is the reverse: convincing, and brief. Asking\nfor persistence let the television through and shut out anyone who says the\nphrase a little quicker or quieter than I do.\n\nStrictness now rides on the window, with the cutoff pinned near the ceiling.\n\nMeasured on 20 recordings of speaker A, 15 of speaker B, and 16 real captured\nfalse accepts (ari-tools/wakeword/baseline/):\n\n  setting  was          speaker A      speaker B        false accepts\n  HIGH     0.95 / 5     100% -> 95%    100% -> 93.3%    15/16 -> 13/16\n  MEDIUM   0.985 / 10    95% -> 95%    66.7% -> 86.7%   14/16 -> 10/16\n  LOW      0.99 / 14     90% -> 90%    13.3% -> 40%     10/16 -> 9/16\n\nEvery level improves or holds on both axes. At the default, speaker B gains 20\npoints while false accepts drop by four. LOW stops being the setting that\nignores her almost entirely.\n\nThis came out of a sweep run while evaluating retrained models. None of those\nbeat the incumbent; the incumbent being operated badly turned out to be the\nbigger finding, and it needed no retraining at all. It is also section 7 of the\nretrain design arriving early: that noted the app overrides each model''s own\noperating point with this enum, and filed it as a blocker for shipping a new\nmodel. It was already a defect in the shipped one.\n\nTests cover the invariant rather than restating the constants: strictness must\nincrease down the ladder, and every level must survive int8 quantisation as a\ndistinct threshold — there is very little room up there, and 0.9981 and above\nall collapse onto the same byte.\n\nCaveat on the record: speaker B''s recordings are near-field, one room, one\nsession. Direction solid, magnitudes provisional.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHzdAE1LmHMYpn4YTFH+bpEhqgOD0h0MpYNPk5wnu9LqjdfBxXp2SURiKsUwxQcyAh\nK5TC6MjQEPeq9J5vtdCAo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/d4a737d161d79ef8cc4f9613aca651a8d10bba2f","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGQ0YTczN2QxNjFkNzllZjhjYzRmOTYxM2FjYTY1MWE4ZDEwYmJhMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/b6f508079dbf079f8b8b0a379fdd8d1dd71bb916","sha":"b6f508079dbf079f8b8b0a379fdd8d1dd71bb916","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/b6f508079dbf079f8b8b0a379fdd8d1dd71bb916"}],"sha":"d4a737d161d79ef8cc4f9613aca651a8d10bba2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/d4a737d161d79ef8cc4f9613aca651a8d10bba2f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/b6f508079dbf079f8b8b0a379fdd8d1dd71bb916/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:04:28Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:04:28Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(wakeword): show what was recorded, not how many files\n\n\"1 files stored\" answers neither question anybody has on that screen: whose\nvoice is captured, and which rooms and distances are still missing. It also\ncounted sidecars, so one recording read as two.\n\nEach segment now lists its set name, room, distance and background, with its\nduration, newest first — read back from the sidecars the recorder already\nwrites, so nothing new is stored to support it.\n\nparseWakeSampleSidecar is the inverse of wakeSampleSidecar and the round trip\nis tested, because a silent drift between the two would empty this list without\nfailing anything.\n\nAn unrecognised condition keeps its raw slug rather than leaving a blank or\ndropping the row. A sidecar written by a later build should still say something\ntrue on a list whose entire job is showing what has been captured.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6cebccc5e150f64d75d7690f70dce3511b118cf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/6cebccc5e150f64d75d7690f70dce3511b118cf3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/b6f508079dbf079f8b8b0a379fdd8d1dd71bb916","verification":{"payload":"tree 6cebccc5e150f64d75d7690f70dce3511b118cf3\nparent 2f7c0678ce4376ea29b4449df5d102db1cb89f48\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789128268 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789128268 +0100\n\nfeat(wakeword): show what was recorded, not how many files\n\n\"1 files stored\" answers neither question anybody has on that screen: whose\nvoice is captured, and which rooms and distances are still missing. It also\ncounted sidecars, so one recording read as two.\n\nEach segment now lists its set name, room, distance and background, with its\nduration, newest first — read back from the sidecars the recorder already\nwrites, so nothing new is stored to support it.\n\nparseWakeSampleSidecar is the inverse of wakeSampleSidecar and the round trip\nis tested, because a silent drift between the two would empty this list without\nfailing anything.\n\nAn unrecognised condition keeps its raw slug rather than leaving a blank or\ndropping the row. A sidecar written by a later build should still say something\ntrue on a list whose entire job is showing what has been captured.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEPGrHQNw0HcsJzl8iyBNf+uZyGT8BFSCgtBW5SSG+3t/PyrIGlAHNtlSQ8rmSajrH\nwf93ho3evj5KhrKdWf8gk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/b6f508079dbf079f8b8b0a379fdd8d1dd71bb916","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGI2ZjUwODA3OWRiZjA3OWY4YjhiMGEzNzlmZGQ4ZDFkZDcxYmI5MTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/2f7c0678ce4376ea29b4449df5d102db1cb89f48","sha":"2f7c0678ce4376ea29b4449df5d102db1cb89f48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/2f7c0678ce4376ea29b4449df5d102db1cb89f48"}],"sha":"b6f508079dbf079f8b8b0a379fdd8d1dd71bb916","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/b6f508079dbf079f8b8b0a379fdd8d1dd71bb916"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/2f7c0678ce4376ea29b4449df5d102db1cb89f48/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:15:22Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:15:22Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"docs(wakeword): retract section 2.3, the loudness-shortcut diagnosis\n\nReading the trainer that produced hey_ari contradicts it. It configures\nupstream''s Augmentation with \"Gain\": 0.8 across the default -45 to 0 dB, plus\nCHiME/FMA/AudioSet backgrounds and room impulses at p=0.7. The volume\naugmentation section 2.3 said was skipped was applied, and more widely than our\nown pipeline applies it.\n\nSection 2.3 now states the retraction rather than being quietly rewritten, and\nlists what survives: the sensitivity sweep result, ok_ari and hey_jarvis working\nfor the same speaker on the same device, and the measured saturation — cutoff\n0.50 to 0.95 changes nothing, and at 0.999 nine of sixteen known-hard negatives\nstill fire.\n\nThe mechanism is open. Section 2.4, the phoneme ceiling, is now the strongest\nsurviving explanation and is independent of any training setting — which the\nok_ari and hey_jarvis evidence directly supports.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9dc59a31fc837facbbfca8134fe800c7589919d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/9dc59a31fc837facbbfca8134fe800c7589919d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/2f7c0678ce4376ea29b4449df5d102db1cb89f48","verification":{"payload":"tree 9dc59a31fc837facbbfca8134fe800c7589919d9\nparent 767b0c3eb7e6b1b01fc3a6dc5c0a46e3f3e8603b\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789118122 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789118122 +0100\n\ndocs(wakeword): retract section 2.3, the loudness-shortcut diagnosis\n\nReading the trainer that produced hey_ari contradicts it. It configures\nupstream''s Augmentation with \"Gain\": 0.8 across the default -45 to 0 dB, plus\nCHiME/FMA/AudioSet backgrounds and room impulses at p=0.7. The volume\naugmentation section 2.3 said was skipped was applied, and more widely than our\nown pipeline applies it.\n\nSection 2.3 now states the retraction rather than being quietly rewritten, and\nlists what survives: the sensitivity sweep result, ok_ari and hey_jarvis working\nfor the same speaker on the same device, and the measured saturation — cutoff\n0.50 to 0.95 changes nothing, and at 0.999 nine of sixteen known-hard negatives\nstill fire.\n\nThe mechanism is open. Section 2.4, the phoneme ceiling, is now the strongest\nsurviving explanation and is independent of any training setting — which the\nok_ari and hey_jarvis evidence directly supports.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAE+ppUQEECwSAFnZn8OdV8WWVh5RGbaif4G+pgxNjjTzcNyVT3iJZDiZ07CF6AyDy\n7ZGQQukMQvW+clgrZR9wY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/2f7c0678ce4376ea29b4449df5d102db1cb89f48","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDJmN2MwNjc4Y2U0Mzc2ZWEyOWI0NDQ5ZGY1ZDEwMmRiMWNiODlmNDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/767b0c3eb7e6b1b01fc3a6dc5c0a46e3f3e8603b","sha":"767b0c3eb7e6b1b01fc3a6dc5c0a46e3f3e8603b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/767b0c3eb7e6b1b01fc3a6dc5c0a46e3f3e8603b"}],"sha":"2f7c0678ce4376ea29b4449df5d102db1cb89f48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/2f7c0678ce4376ea29b4449df5d102db1cb89f48"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/767b0c3eb7e6b1b01fc3a6dc5c0a46e3f3e8603b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:53:30Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:53:30Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(wakeword): don''t stand down before we''ve stood up\n\nReported as \"I disabled listening then it crashes\" (#16). The crash is\nForegroundServiceDidNotStartInTimeException, and logcat shows the service being\nbrought down while still waiting for start foreground.\n\nonCreate() runs before onStartCommand(). The decisions collector is launched in\nonCreate, and `decisions` is built on DataStore flows that emit as soon as their\ncached read lands — so on a cold start it can fire while startForeground() is\nstill pending. A decision of Off then reaches stopSelf() with the foreground\npromise outstanding, and Android answers that with a crash rather than letting\nus stand down quietly.\n\nGuarded on isRunning, matching the captureMode collector directly above it.\nNothing is lost by waiting: onStartCommand seeds `decision` itself and applies\nit once we are genuinely foreground, so this collector only ever needed to\nhandle later changes.\n\nThe other two stopSelf() paths that sit before startForeground() were checked.\nThe notification''s stop action uses PendingIntent.getService, not\ngetForegroundService, so it creates no promise. The RECORD_AUDIO-revoked path\nis real but cannot be fixed the same way — startForeground with a MICROPHONE\ntype throws without the permission — and is left alone deliberately.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cb6c2b8a37544cf955abe5e830ab8f8afa64e8f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/cb6c2b8a37544cf955abe5e830ab8f8afa64e8f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/767b0c3eb7e6b1b01fc3a6dc5c0a46e3f3e8603b","verification":{"payload":"tree cb6c2b8a37544cf955abe5e830ab8f8afa64e8f8\nparent fd02336556c611701924f056f5000b45f3999e25\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789116810 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789116810 +0100\n\nfix(wakeword): don''t stand down before we''ve stood up\n\nReported as \"I disabled listening then it crashes\" (#16). The crash is\nForegroundServiceDidNotStartInTimeException, and logcat shows the service being\nbrought down while still waiting for start foreground.\n\nonCreate() runs before onStartCommand(). The decisions collector is launched in\nonCreate, and `decisions` is built on DataStore flows that emit as soon as their\ncached read lands — so on a cold start it can fire while startForeground() is\nstill pending. A decision of Off then reaches stopSelf() with the foreground\npromise outstanding, and Android answers that with a crash rather than letting\nus stand down quietly.\n\nGuarded on isRunning, matching the captureMode collector directly above it.\nNothing is lost by waiting: onStartCommand seeds `decision` itself and applies\nit once we are genuinely foreground, so this collector only ever needed to\nhandle later changes.\n\nThe other two stopSelf() paths that sit before startForeground() were checked.\nThe notification''s stop action uses PendingIntent.getService, not\ngetForegroundService, so it creates no promise. The RECORD_AUDIO-revoked path\nis real but cannot be fixed the same way — startForeground with a MICROPHONE\ntype throws without the permission — and is left alone deliberately.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQBiCNPh4aPjeHK8Q2dJG9aw+i4UA3u09jXsdXZaXTHTKgqVypHS2Rj5Iz2UPlD7rde\nypuwq7pNH5ra19RaUbWQg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/767b0c3eb7e6b1b01fc3a6dc5c0a46e3f3e8603b","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDc2N2IwYzNlYjdlNmIxYjAxZmMzYTZkYzVjMGE0NmUzZjNlODYwM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/fd02336556c611701924f056f5000b45f3999e25","sha":"fd02336556c611701924f056f5000b45f3999e25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/fd02336556c611701924f056f5000b45f3999e25"}],"sha":"767b0c3eb7e6b1b01fc3a6dc5c0a46e3f3e8603b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/767b0c3eb7e6b1b01fc3a6dc5c0a46e3f3e8603b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/fd02336556c611701924f056f5000b45f3999e25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:53:21Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:53:21Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(wakeword): a debug recorder, so the eval set can have more than one voice\n\nEvery positive we hold is one man standing near his phone giving a command.\nThe retrain cannot be measured against that, and the shipped false-accept\ncapture will never help: a miss produces no artefact, so it collects the\nsounds that wake Ari and nothing at all about the people it ignores. That\naudio only exists if somebody deliberately records it.\n\nSettings > Debug > Record wake word samples. Name the set once, pick room,\ndistance and background, then record one continuous stretch per position. Two\ntaps per room and none while speaking — which is the point, because the\nacross-the-room takes are the ones that matter most and nobody can reach the\nbutton from there. Splitting into individual takes happens off-device, where\nthe thresholds can be chosen after hearing the room.\n\nIt reads CaptureBus rather than opening its own AudioRecord. That is the whole\njustification for building this instead of using a recorder app: the eval set\nhas to come down the same path production audio does, and sharing the producer\nmakes that true by construction instead of by keeping two sets of capture flags\nin step. Arming the bus also suppresses wake detection for free, so saying the\nphrase forty times does not launch forty voice turns.\n\nAudio flow is verified before the countdown, not after. If the mic is not\nrunning you get told in one second, rather than after somebody has walked to\nthe far corner and said it eight times into nothing.\n\nCaps are far above any plausible session. The other capture stores evict\noldest; here that would silently destroy a recording session with a real person\nin it, which is the one thing the retrain cannot proceed without.\n\nItalian is a draft and wants a human read.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c69f2e2958e2ac45b1bd12a6ad68fcb7d3c700d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/c69f2e2958e2ac45b1bd12a6ad68fcb7d3c700d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/fd02336556c611701924f056f5000b45f3999e25","verification":{"payload":"tree c69f2e2958e2ac45b1bd12a6ad68fcb7d3c700d7\nparent 46bf4e771d282f9672d049a75097a555ca654463\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789116801 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789116801 +0100\n\nfeat(wakeword): a debug recorder, so the eval set can have more than one voice\n\nEvery positive we hold is one man standing near his phone giving a command.\nThe retrain cannot be measured against that, and the shipped false-accept\ncapture will never help: a miss produces no artefact, so it collects the\nsounds that wake Ari and nothing at all about the people it ignores. That\naudio only exists if somebody deliberately records it.\n\nSettings > Debug > Record wake word samples. Name the set once, pick room,\ndistance and background, then record one continuous stretch per position. Two\ntaps per room and none while speaking — which is the point, because the\nacross-the-room takes are the ones that matter most and nobody can reach the\nbutton from there. Splitting into individual takes happens off-device, where\nthe thresholds can be chosen after hearing the room.\n\nIt reads CaptureBus rather than opening its own AudioRecord. That is the whole\njustification for building this instead of using a recorder app: the eval set\nhas to come down the same path production audio does, and sharing the producer\nmakes that true by construction instead of by keeping two sets of capture flags\nin step. Arming the bus also suppresses wake detection for free, so saying the\nphrase forty times does not launch forty voice turns.\n\nAudio flow is verified before the countdown, not after. If the mic is not\nrunning you get told in one second, rather than after somebody has walked to\nthe far corner and said it eight times into nothing.\n\nCaps are far above any plausible session. The other capture stores evict\noldest; here that would silently destroy a recording session with a real person\nin it, which is the one thing the retrain cannot proceed without.\n\nItalian is a draft and wants a human read.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQK4YkoK10SH8L9Zr9JCYfDhOkKJMLT17BGir5XSqVblo777YAc2l40x5e7GmpFoh/4\nRjxsvb8K1uNgW1YtJpoAU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/fd02336556c611701924f056f5000b45f3999e25","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGZkMDIzMzY1NTZjNjExNzAxOTI0ZjA1NmY1MDAwYjQ1ZjM5OTllMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/46bf4e771d282f9672d049a75097a555ca654463","sha":"46bf4e771d282f9672d049a75097a555ca654463","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/46bf4e771d282f9672d049a75097a555ca654463"}],"sha":"fd02336556c611701924f056f5000b45f3999e25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/fd02336556c611701924f056f5000b45f3999e25"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/46bf4e771d282f9672d049a75097a555ca654463/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:53:08Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:53:08Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"docs(wakeword): rewrite the retrain design around what the evidence showed\n\nThe July design assumed a weak negative set was the whole fault. It is not.\nGathered on device: sensitivity swept MEDIUM to HIGH changes nothing for a\nsecond speaker, the same speaker wakes it by shouting the stressed syllable,\nand both ok_ari and hey_jarvis work for her at a normal speaking volume.\n\nOne mechanism explains all of it. The model discriminates on loudness rather\nthan on phonetic content, because Piper positives are uniformly loud and\nstandard negatives are ambient and quieter — so in that training distribution\namplitude genuinely IS discriminative and the shortcut was free. She is not\nfailing to say \"Hey Ari\", she is failing to sound like a TTS engine at full\noutput.\n\nThe audio pipeline was audited first and cleared: PCAN is on, the filterbank\nruns 125-7500 Hz, the frontend is a faithful ESPHome port. Recorded so nobody\nre-investigates it.\n\nAlso here: the phoneme ceiling, so that \"better but still behind hey_jarvis\"\nreads as success rather than disappointment when it happens; the first capture\nreview, which found the real trigger class is non-English speech rather than\nthe loud transients everyone predicted; and the leakage route where two capture\nfeatures record the same utterance through different windows.\n\nSupersedes 2026-07-27-wake-word-model-retrain-design.md rather than editing it,\nbecause its premise changed and rewriting it in place would hide that.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1ab35558decb7dc94526af45273ee818bf51ef4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/1ab35558decb7dc94526af45273ee818bf51ef4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/46bf4e771d282f9672d049a75097a555ca654463","verification":{"payload":"tree 1ab35558decb7dc94526af45273ee818bf51ef4b\nparent 809fb924d649e8ed9f12ab70f3507fdfbf3055b9\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789116788 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1789116788 +0100\n\ndocs(wakeword): rewrite the retrain design around what the evidence showed\n\nThe July design assumed a weak negative set was the whole fault. It is not.\nGathered on device: sensitivity swept MEDIUM to HIGH changes nothing for a\nsecond speaker, the same speaker wakes it by shouting the stressed syllable,\nand both ok_ari and hey_jarvis work for her at a normal speaking volume.\n\nOne mechanism explains all of it. The model discriminates on loudness rather\nthan on phonetic content, because Piper positives are uniformly loud and\nstandard negatives are ambient and quieter — so in that training distribution\namplitude genuinely IS discriminative and the shortcut was free. She is not\nfailing to say \"Hey Ari\", she is failing to sound like a TTS engine at full\noutput.\n\nThe audio pipeline was audited first and cleared: PCAN is on, the filterbank\nruns 125-7500 Hz, the frontend is a faithful ESPHome port. Recorded so nobody\nre-investigates it.\n\nAlso here: the phoneme ceiling, so that \"better but still behind hey_jarvis\"\nreads as success rather than disappointment when it happens; the first capture\nreview, which found the real trigger class is non-English speech rather than\nthe loud transients everyone predicted; and the leakage route where two capture\nfeatures record the same utterance through different windows.\n\nSupersedes 2026-07-27-wake-word-model-retrain-design.md rather than editing it,\nbecause its premise changed and rewriting it in place would hide that.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMMYe3U0HSd0y+82IKUNHeb8jhd/sDGJSWVW7bJy3l5t7daTzwCA01+OQVNM4Znicn\n25bF5bjCAMcvn11JvQ9AQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:05:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/46bf4e771d282f9672d049a75097a555ca654463","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDQ2YmY0ZTc3MWQyODJmOTY3MmQwNDlhNzUwOTdhNTU1Y2E2NTQ0NjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/809fb924d649e8ed9f12ab70f3507fdfbf3055b9","sha":"809fb924d649e8ed9f12ab70f3507fdfbf3055b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/809fb924d649e8ed9f12ab70f3507fdfbf3055b9"}],"sha":"46bf4e771d282f9672d049a75097a555ca654463","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/46bf4e771d282f9672d049a75097a555ca654463"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/809fb924d649e8ed9f12ab70f3507fdfbf3055b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T10:08:03Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T10:08:03Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(bugreport): stop promising a withdrawal erases the words\n\nThe confirm dialog said the description would be \"removed from the\npublic issue\". It gets blanked, and GitHub keeps an edit history of\nevery issue body — so anyone who clicks through can still read what was\noriginally written. Someone who typed a hostname into that box and\nthought better of it was being told they had undone something they had\nnot, at the exact moment they were deciding.\n\nThe files are the part we can actually promise, because those are ours,\nso the dialog now leads with that and is straight about the rest. Same\nwording the privacy page took this morning; the two contradicted each\nother, and the one that overpromised was the one people read first.\n\n\"Delete\" becomes \"Withdraw\" throughout, keys and callback included. It\nwas the wrong verb, and a button that says Delete sets the expectation\nbefore anyone reaches the explanation.\n\nItalian is a draft for review.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"809669901307f95e10fa99578dbd7a6d1598dea9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/809669901307f95e10fa99578dbd7a6d1598dea9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/809fb924d649e8ed9f12ab70f3507fdfbf3055b9","verification":{"payload":"tree 809669901307f95e10fa99578dbd7a6d1598dea9\nparent e882d28ee3582590624e3e7082eac66f1f0f6376\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788430083 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788430083 +0100\n\nfix(bugreport): stop promising a withdrawal erases the words\n\nThe confirm dialog said the description would be \"removed from the\npublic issue\". It gets blanked, and GitHub keeps an edit history of\nevery issue body — so anyone who clicks through can still read what was\noriginally written. Someone who typed a hostname into that box and\nthought better of it was being told they had undone something they had\nnot, at the exact moment they were deciding.\n\nThe files are the part we can actually promise, because those are ours,\nso the dialog now leads with that and is straight about the rest. Same\nwording the privacy page took this morning; the two contradicted each\nother, and the one that overpromised was the one people read first.\n\n\"Delete\" becomes \"Withdraw\" throughout, keys and callback included. It\nwas the wrong verb, and a button that says Delete sets the expectation\nbefore anyone reaches the explanation.\n\nItalian is a draft for review.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCjxXtv3yTLL9Cq4MLO1ya+HtJQJcwR8QlYq+8lTRWgxjhOF8r2hH3dZT7C7miWJfM\nA3zIoDgSUKz4cH1CFfuwI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T10:08:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/809fb924d649e8ed9f12ab70f3507fdfbf3055b9","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDgwOWZiOTI0ZDY0OWU4ZWQ5ZjEyYWI3MGYzNTA3ZmRmYmYzMDU1Yjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/e882d28ee3582590624e3e7082eac66f1f0f6376","sha":"e882d28ee3582590624e3e7082eac66f1f0f6376","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/e882d28ee3582590624e3e7082eac66f1f0f6376"}],"sha":"809fb924d649e8ed9f12ab70f3507fdfbf3055b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/809fb924d649e8ed9f12ab70f3507fdfbf3055b9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/e882d28ee3582590624e3e7082eac66f1f0f6376/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T09:59:42Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T09:59:42Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(permissions): surface battery optimisation and send people to fix it\n\nThe first real bug report came back with \"Battery optimisation: not\nexempt\", which is the usual reason a wake word quietly stops working in\nthe background. The app already read that state to put it in a report;\nit just never mentioned it to anyone.\n\nIt is now a row in the permissions section, so it appears in onboarding\nand in Settings > Permissions from one change, and joins the nudge shown\non the way out of the onboarding step.\n\nDeliberately a trip to Android settings rather than the one-tap system\ndialog. That dialog needs REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS, which is\non Play''s restricted-permissions list, and arguing our case at review is\na bad trade for two taps when a Play submission is the next thing on the\nlist. The optimisation list screen goes first with Ari''s app info page\nbehind it for ROMs that don''t ship one; each is tried until one starts\nrather than asked about with resolveActivity, because on Android 11 and\nup that answer is filtered by package visibility and a screen that\nexists can report itself missing.\n\nItalian is a draft for review, as always.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d40e9065789439d550c76aca0ca7d0447f29b88d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/d40e9065789439d550c76aca0ca7d0447f29b88d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/e882d28ee3582590624e3e7082eac66f1f0f6376","verification":{"payload":"tree d40e9065789439d550c76aca0ca7d0447f29b88d\nparent 7102d0d24289570f623dfe71eccbe7e3030f7cd4\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788429582 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788429582 +0100\n\nfeat(permissions): surface battery optimisation and send people to fix it\n\nThe first real bug report came back with \"Battery optimisation: not\nexempt\", which is the usual reason a wake word quietly stops working in\nthe background. The app already read that state to put it in a report;\nit just never mentioned it to anyone.\n\nIt is now a row in the permissions section, so it appears in onboarding\nand in Settings > Permissions from one change, and joins the nudge shown\non the way out of the onboarding step.\n\nDeliberately a trip to Android settings rather than the one-tap system\ndialog. That dialog needs REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS, which is\non Play''s restricted-permissions list, and arguing our case at review is\na bad trade for two taps when a Play submission is the next thing on the\nlist. The optimisation list screen goes first with Ari''s app info page\nbehind it for ROMs that don''t ship one; each is tried until one starts\nrather than asked about with resolveActivity, because on Android 11 and\nup that answer is filtered by package visibility and a screen that\nexists can report itself missing.\n\nItalian is a draft for review, as always.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOQhX63tXzSycN5v9s2FbYbmjFLS7JGc6SaSPy8l9o9jYQxSQAZS6UOO5j70OAHkvo\n4/cDw+jspfQcOHbe+rEgQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T09:59:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/e882d28ee3582590624e3e7082eac66f1f0f6376","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGU4ODJkMjhlZTM1ODI1OTA2MjRlM2U3MDgyZWFjNjZmMWYwZjYzNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/7102d0d24289570f623dfe71eccbe7e3030f7cd4","sha":"7102d0d24289570f623dfe71eccbe7e3030f7cd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/7102d0d24289570f623dfe71eccbe7e3030f7cd4"}],"sha":"e882d28ee3582590624e3e7082eac66f1f0f6376","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/e882d28ee3582590624e3e7082eac66f1f0f6376"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/7102d0d24289570f623dfe71eccbe7e3030f7cd4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T09:51:48Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T09:51:48Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"docs: fill in CONTRIBUTING''s testing section\n\nIt promised build/run instructions, Hilt test setup and Compose-test\nconventions, and delivered a TODO. Two of those three don''t exist, so\nthis documents what''s actually here rather than what the placeholder\nimagined: 466 JVM unit tests, no Hilt in any of them, and an androidTest\ndirectory holding nothing but AGP''s scaffold. Said plainly, with a note\nto replace the paragraph when someone writes the first UI test.\n\nThe part worth writing down is the convention the setup forces. Stubbed\nAndroid APIs return defaults, so anything reaching into a real Android\nclass can''t be tested here — hence logic in plain Kotlin with the\nCompose layer calling it, and hence no mocking framework. Also the trap\nthat falls out of the same setting: org.json is stubbed too, which is\nwhy the real one is a test dependency.\n\nBoth documented commands were run before committing them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"727fe35beee54989ecccd3c6726b4882e5b5b1cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/727fe35beee54989ecccd3c6726b4882e5b5b1cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/7102d0d24289570f623dfe71eccbe7e3030f7cd4","verification":{"payload":"tree 727fe35beee54989ecccd3c6726b4882e5b5b1cd\nparent 4d503cbf882b6291c3b9db193170484f531f6c9a\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788429108 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788429108 +0100\n\ndocs: fill in CONTRIBUTING''s testing section\n\nIt promised build/run instructions, Hilt test setup and Compose-test\nconventions, and delivered a TODO. Two of those three don''t exist, so\nthis documents what''s actually here rather than what the placeholder\nimagined: 466 JVM unit tests, no Hilt in any of them, and an androidTest\ndirectory holding nothing but AGP''s scaffold. Said plainly, with a note\nto replace the paragraph when someone writes the first UI test.\n\nThe part worth writing down is the convention the setup forces. Stubbed\nAndroid APIs return defaults, so anything reaching into a real Android\nclass can''t be tested here — hence logic in plain Kotlin with the\nCompose layer calling it, and hence no mocking framework. Also the trap\nthat falls out of the same setting: org.json is stubbed too, which is\nwhy the real one is a test dependency.\n\nBoth documented commands were run before committing them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOzf/wLkgz2g44mB2I0HO6D1ugocxvpLdOw+ESfazXa8wmziFuCBcR9hwdD0vKzdKm\nd2FPuHUOTdWWbqKsPBHAk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T09:51:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/7102d0d24289570f623dfe71eccbe7e3030f7cd4","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDcxMDJkMGQyNDI4OTU3MGY2MjNkZmU3MWVjY2JlN2UzMDMwZjdjZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/4d503cbf882b6291c3b9db193170484f531f6c9a","sha":"4d503cbf882b6291c3b9db193170484f531f6c9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/4d503cbf882b6291c3b9db193170484f531f6c9a"}],"sha":"7102d0d24289570f623dfe71eccbe7e3030f7cd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/7102d0d24289570f623dfe71eccbe7e3030f7cd4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/4d503cbf882b6291c3b9db193170484f531f6c9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T09:48:32Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T09:48:32Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"docs: stop CONTRIBUTING linking to a file outside the repo\n\nBoth references pointed at ../CLAUDE.md, which lives in the workspace and\nnot in this repository — so on GitHub they were 404s that rendered as\nworking links, which is worse than no link at all.\n\nThe intro now points at the README and names the sibling repositories\ndirectly. The no-machine-translation rule is stated as a rule rather than\ncited from somewhere the reader cannot open; it was always the rule, and\nit does not need a footnote to be binding.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1b1cc6ded7aa0e2bf45b53872ec9ac899b9ccb81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/1b1cc6ded7aa0e2bf45b53872ec9ac899b9ccb81"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/4d503cbf882b6291c3b9db193170484f531f6c9a","verification":{"payload":"tree 1b1cc6ded7aa0e2bf45b53872ec9ac899b9ccb81\nparent d6d216f6607d99d442e855e78e13969281534db2\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788428912 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788428912 +0100\n\ndocs: stop CONTRIBUTING linking to a file outside the repo\n\nBoth references pointed at ../CLAUDE.md, which lives in the workspace and\nnot in this repository — so on GitHub they were 404s that rendered as\nworking links, which is worse than no link at all.\n\nThe intro now points at the README and names the sibling repositories\ndirectly. The no-machine-translation rule is stated as a rule rather than\ncited from somewhere the reader cannot open; it was always the rule, and\nit does not need a footnote to be binding.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAAXs7CoVEdPyjtj+ZgKjS33e+8bFOdmi1OF1ESRFedmzYl+6SsLtgJTP3IfxoOxOY\noCDX2XEkl0VVYMcO2pzA4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T09:48:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/4d503cbf882b6291c3b9db193170484f531f6c9a","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDRkNTAzY2JmODgyYjYyOTFjM2I5ZGIxOTMxNzA0ODRmNTMxZjZjOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/d6d216f6607d99d442e855e78e13969281534db2","sha":"d6d216f6607d99d442e855e78e13969281534db2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/d6d216f6607d99d442e855e78e13969281534db2"}],"sha":"4d503cbf882b6291c3b9db193170484f531f6c9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/4d503cbf882b6291c3b9db193170484f531f6c9a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/d6d216f6607d99d442e855e78e13969281534db2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T09:45:25Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T09:45:25Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"docs: give ari-android a README, and restore the two B7 pointers\n\nThe repo has had no README since it started, which stopped being merely\nuntidy once the issue templates wanted somewhere to send people. Both\ncarried a RESTORE WITH B7 comment marking a link left out because its\ntarget did not exist; the README now has a \"Reporting bugs\" section and\nboth pointers are back — the in-app reporter first in config.yml, and a\nline at the top of the bug form telling testers the button collects all\nof it for them.\n\nThe README leads with reporting rather than with building, because the\npeople arriving from an issue template outnumber the people cloning it.\nTwo things it makes loud, both of which cost me time: the app will not\nbuild without a sibling ari-engine checkout, and a release or beta build\nneeds the NDK''s own cmake or llama-cpp-sys dies without explaining why.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3b1a7bf9941035a94367376bd9a214cd0b70c7b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/3b1a7bf9941035a94367376bd9a214cd0b70c7b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/d6d216f6607d99d442e855e78e13969281534db2","verification":{"payload":"tree 3b1a7bf9941035a94367376bd9a214cd0b70c7b6\nparent aa3ec6d9e08bbc0f938bff1d4c38b17069ff86ae\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788428725 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788428725 +0100\n\ndocs: give ari-android a README, and restore the two B7 pointers\n\nThe repo has had no README since it started, which stopped being merely\nuntidy once the issue templates wanted somewhere to send people. Both\ncarried a RESTORE WITH B7 comment marking a link left out because its\ntarget did not exist; the README now has a \"Reporting bugs\" section and\nboth pointers are back — the in-app reporter first in config.yml, and a\nline at the top of the bug form telling testers the button collects all\nof it for them.\n\nThe README leads with reporting rather than with building, because the\npeople arriving from an issue template outnumber the people cloning it.\nTwo things it makes loud, both of which cost me time: the app will not\nbuild without a sibling ari-engine checkout, and a release or beta build\nneeds the NDK''s own cmake or llama-cpp-sys dies without explaining why.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAGZCVF5ccUt2akiDbyH4W1iQG3MLNr4FKwkG6qPK2jb0Olz9q/eU6rb4axW0hQhiu\n9k++sWLvGFczqZcosNsgU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T09:45:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/d6d216f6607d99d442e855e78e13969281534db2","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGQ2ZDIxNmY2NjA3ZDk5ZDQ0MmU4NTVlNzhlMTM5NjkyODE1MzRkYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/aa3ec6d9e08bbc0f938bff1d4c38b17069ff86ae","sha":"aa3ec6d9e08bbc0f938bff1d4c38b17069ff86ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/aa3ec6d9e08bbc0f938bff1d4c38b17069ff86ae"}],"sha":"d6d216f6607d99d442e855e78e13969281534db2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/d6d216f6607d99d442e855e78e13969281534db2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/aa3ec6d9e08bbc0f938bff1d4c38b17069ff86ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:53:06Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:53:06Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(bugreport): the attachments the spec asked for, and honest sizes\n\nThree items from the backlog were missing, and one screen was lying.\n\nThe screenshot had plumbing at both ends and nothing in the middle — the\nreport screen passed null unconditionally, so it could never be offered. It is\nnow captured with PixelCopy at the moment the button is tapped, before\nnavigating, because a moment later the screen worth photographing is the\nreport form. PixelCopy rather than drawing the view tree, so anything backed\nby a surface comes out as the user saw it instead of as a blank rectangle.\n\n\"All recordings\" was simply absent from the offer list. It is the union of the\ntwo specific audio kinds rather than a third store, so ticking it unticks them\nand vice versa — sending both would upload every clip twice and charge the\ntester''s daily budget for the privilege.\n\nThe crash prompt was dead. CrashRecorder wrote the trace on the way down and\nnothing ever read it, so every crash was recorded and silently discarded. It\nnow offers on the next launch, once, and consuming the record clears it. A\ndeliberate \"Crash Ari now\" button under Debug makes the path testable rather\nthan something we wait for; it is gated on the same flag as the reporter,\nbecause a button that kills the app has no place in a release.\n\nAnd the review screen quoted 0 bytes for the log, the screenshot and the\nconversation. Those three are synthesised at send time, so at review time\nthere was nothing to measure and it printed a zero rather than admitting it.\nStaging now happens BEFORE the review screen renders, so every size is read\noff the file that is actually about to be uploaded, with a total beneath them.\nA kind that produced nothing disappears before anyone is asked to approve it.\nA screen whose entire purpose is showing what leaves the phone cannot be the\none making numbers up.\n\nAll five paths driven on a Pixel 10 Pro Fold: report, crash, screenshot,\nwithdraw, and the sizes.\n\nItalian drafted. 584/584 parity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"66188e535cde0c04b6da384d95f4929d83961da4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/66188e535cde0c04b6da384d95f4929d83961da4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/aa3ec6d9e08bbc0f938bff1d4c38b17069ff86ae","verification":{"payload":"tree 66188e535cde0c04b6da384d95f4929d83961da4\nparent ea1e82f6170ff9ab8b63c4f56c226e32303dd49c\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788353586 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788353586 +0100\n\nfix(bugreport): the attachments the spec asked for, and honest sizes\n\nThree items from the backlog were missing, and one screen was lying.\n\nThe screenshot had plumbing at both ends and nothing in the middle — the\nreport screen passed null unconditionally, so it could never be offered. It is\nnow captured with PixelCopy at the moment the button is tapped, before\nnavigating, because a moment later the screen worth photographing is the\nreport form. PixelCopy rather than drawing the view tree, so anything backed\nby a surface comes out as the user saw it instead of as a blank rectangle.\n\n\"All recordings\" was simply absent from the offer list. It is the union of the\ntwo specific audio kinds rather than a third store, so ticking it unticks them\nand vice versa — sending both would upload every clip twice and charge the\ntester''s daily budget for the privilege.\n\nThe crash prompt was dead. CrashRecorder wrote the trace on the way down and\nnothing ever read it, so every crash was recorded and silently discarded. It\nnow offers on the next launch, once, and consuming the record clears it. A\ndeliberate \"Crash Ari now\" button under Debug makes the path testable rather\nthan something we wait for; it is gated on the same flag as the reporter,\nbecause a button that kills the app has no place in a release.\n\nAnd the review screen quoted 0 bytes for the log, the screenshot and the\nconversation. Those three are synthesised at send time, so at review time\nthere was nothing to measure and it printed a zero rather than admitting it.\nStaging now happens BEFORE the review screen renders, so every size is read\noff the file that is actually about to be uploaded, with a total beneath them.\nA kind that produced nothing disappears before anyone is asked to approve it.\nA screen whose entire purpose is showing what leaves the phone cannot be the\none making numbers up.\n\nAll five paths driven on a Pixel 10 Pro Fold: report, crash, screenshot,\nwithdraw, and the sizes.\n\nItalian drafted. 584/584 parity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMNuieXRnkGoT+C/kNDs/8rWmXho6DQZsPEyRT4MYCuKTS7ckix8fiWiPqKetZ2IR+\nyeAO5eWnLmX7OvXSZvBww=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T12:53:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/aa3ec6d9e08bbc0f938bff1d4c38b17069ff86ae","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGFhM2VjNmQ5ZTA4YmJjMGY5MzhiZmYxZDRjMzhiMTcwNjlmZjg2YWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/ea1e82f6170ff9ab8b63c4f56c226e32303dd49c","sha":"ea1e82f6170ff9ab8b63c4f56c226e32303dd49c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/ea1e82f6170ff9ab8b63c4f56c226e32303dd49c"}],"sha":"aa3ec6d9e08bbc0f938bff1d4c38b17069ff86ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/aa3ec6d9e08bbc0f938bff1d4c38b17069ff86ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/ea1e82f6170ff9ab8b63c4f56c226e32303dd49c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:34:44Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:34:44Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(bugreport): My Reports, so a tester can withdraw one\n\nThe consent text has been promising this since B7: delete a report and the\nfiles you sent are erased. Until now there was no way to ask.\n\nThe record is written the instant a report is filed, before the screen even\nchanges, because the delete token exists nowhere else — the server keeps only\na hash of it. Lose it and the report can never be withdrawn by hand, which is\nexactly what the footnote warns happens if you uninstall Ari.\n\nAn expired report keeps its row and loses its Delete button. Its files are\nalready gone by then and the issue was never the reporter''s to remove, so the\nbutton would only ever produce \"no such report\".\n\nA failed withdrawal leaves the row alone. Removing it locally would strand a\nreport the server still holds while throwing away the only token that could\nwithdraw it — worse than the failure it was papering over.\n\nThe confirm dialog is careful about what it promises: the files are erased and\nthe description goes, but the issue itself stays, because other people may have\nreplied to it and their words are not the reporter''s to bury.\n\nTwo fixes from driving it on a real phone. The sending spinner had a height\nbut no width, so it drew as an ellipse and appeared to wobble; and three cards\nsized to their content rather than the screen, so a short description gave a\nnarrow card. Both now explicit.\n\nItalian drafted. 577/577 parity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b284215a5c8b16de2cded91671556955ed82a876","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/b284215a5c8b16de2cded91671556955ed82a876"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/ea1e82f6170ff9ab8b63c4f56c226e32303dd49c","verification":{"payload":"tree b284215a5c8b16de2cded91671556955ed82a876\nparent 5b1fd5e806bea74a78111d54522dd06d11a0f948\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788352484 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788352484 +0100\n\nfeat(bugreport): My Reports, so a tester can withdraw one\n\nThe consent text has been promising this since B7: delete a report and the\nfiles you sent are erased. Until now there was no way to ask.\n\nThe record is written the instant a report is filed, before the screen even\nchanges, because the delete token exists nowhere else — the server keeps only\na hash of it. Lose it and the report can never be withdrawn by hand, which is\nexactly what the footnote warns happens if you uninstall Ari.\n\nAn expired report keeps its row and loses its Delete button. Its files are\nalready gone by then and the issue was never the reporter''s to remove, so the\nbutton would only ever produce \"no such report\".\n\nA failed withdrawal leaves the row alone. Removing it locally would strand a\nreport the server still holds while throwing away the only token that could\nwithdraw it — worse than the failure it was papering over.\n\nThe confirm dialog is careful about what it promises: the files are erased and\nthe description goes, but the issue itself stays, because other people may have\nreplied to it and their words are not the reporter''s to bury.\n\nTwo fixes from driving it on a real phone. The sending spinner had a height\nbut no width, so it drew as an ellipse and appeared to wobble; and three cards\nsized to their content rather than the screen, so a short description gave a\nnarrow card. Both now explicit.\n\nItalian drafted. 577/577 parity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJU+7xYmzzXlGFKeZ1hHS5n8yCStY1ii23HYQGB06T3qKACSbCv4JKDWpenYOpBwtB\nVUwadiClraPtPsGed82Qg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T12:34:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/ea1e82f6170ff9ab8b63c4f56c226e32303dd49c","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGVhMWU4MmY2MTcwZmY5YWI4YjYzYzRmNTZjMjI2ZTMyMzAzZGQ0OWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/5b1fd5e806bea74a78111d54522dd06d11a0f948","sha":"5b1fd5e806bea74a78111d54522dd06d11a0f948","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/5b1fd5e806bea74a78111d54522dd06d11a0f948"}],"sha":"ea1e82f6170ff9ab8b63c4f56c226e32303dd49c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/ea1e82f6170ff9ab8b63c4f56c226e32303dd49c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/5b1fd5e806bea74a78111d54522dd06d11a0f948/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:26:28Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:26:28Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"fix(bugreport): keep the FAB out of the system bars and the app bar\n\nThe app draws edge to edge, so the Box hosting the button spans the whole\ndisplay — an offset of zero put it underneath the status bar, and top right is\nwhere the listening-mode switch already lives.\n\nThe drag area now starts below the status bar and the app bar and stops above\nthe navigation bar, and the default corner sits just under the app bar rather\nthan behind the clock.\n\nFound by putting it on a real phone. There is no unit test that would have\ncaught it; the geometry only exists once there are real insets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6bed9213988ad657a985ffdc502002d63237a9b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/6bed9213988ad657a985ffdc502002d63237a9b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/5b1fd5e806bea74a78111d54522dd06d11a0f948","verification":{"payload":"tree 6bed9213988ad657a985ffdc502002d63237a9b9\nparent 1cd028668bef3c825bb07780e625a414b639303a\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788351988 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788351988 +0100\n\nfix(bugreport): keep the FAB out of the system bars and the app bar\n\nThe app draws edge to edge, so the Box hosting the button spans the whole\ndisplay — an offset of zero put it underneath the status bar, and top right is\nwhere the listening-mode switch already lives.\n\nThe drag area now starts below the status bar and the app bar and stops above\nthe navigation bar, and the default corner sits just under the app bar rather\nthan behind the clock.\n\nFound by putting it on a real phone. There is no unit test that would have\ncaught it; the geometry only exists once there are real insets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQETCSObqGmyIQFfs+OgnkcGQhnIoY1y0pQP/6fiNxiGMRTSQO8JERGRfbWQxHokjfv\n8dpWabbqxmacfahosJ8QI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T12:26:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/5b1fd5e806bea74a78111d54522dd06d11a0f948","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDViMWZkNWU4MDZiZWE3NGE3ODExMWQ1NDUyMmRkMDZkMTFhMGY5NDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/1cd028668bef3c825bb07780e625a414b639303a","sha":"1cd028668bef3c825bb07780e625a414b639303a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/1cd028668bef3c825bb07780e625a414b639303a"}],"sha":"5b1fd5e806bea74a78111d54522dd06d11a0f948","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/5b1fd5e806bea74a78111d54522dd06d11a0f948"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/1cd028668bef3c825bb07780e625a414b639303a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:12:27Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:12:27Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(bugreport): the report screen, the FAB and the crash handler\n\nEverything that makes the reporter reachable and usable.\n\nThe review step is a step rather than a dialog. The promise it keeps — that a\ntester knows exactly what leaves their phone — is not one a summary can keep,\nso it shows the actual text and the actual file list with real sizes.\n\nConsent gates the files and nothing else. Leave it unticked and the button\nstill says \"Review and send\", because a report with a description and a device\nblock is worth having and making consent mandatory in practice would be a dark\npattern wearing a checkbox.\n\nThe FAB is round, parked top right, and draggable, with its position kept as\nfractions of the screen so a rotation moves it proportionally rather than off\nthe edge. Both bottom corners already belong to the mic button and the input\nbar, and a permanent overlay will eventually cover something a tester needs —\nso rather than guess a corner that is always safe, let them move it. It snaps\nto the nearer side on release and hides itself inside the reporter.\n\nThe crash handler writes the trace on the way down, because nobody can tap a\nbutton in a process that has already died; without it we would only ever hear\nabout bugs that did not crash the app. It stays deliberately dull — one\nsynchronous write, no injection, no coroutines — and hands straight back to\nthe previous handler.\n\nTwo things this changes that were not strictly asked for. The capture toggles\nnow default on in testing builds, which made three existing blurbs untrue:\nthey claimed \"never uploaded\" and \"off by default\", and both had to go. And\nlint was already red on a SEND_SMS permission with no matching uses-feature,\nwhich would have hidden Ari from every device without a radio — fixed while\npassing, since it was one line and the check is now green.\n\nItalian is drafted, not authoritative. 562/562 parity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b6904f14d9d87795f154188047b838926f3a51f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/7b6904f14d9d87795f154188047b838926f3a51f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/1cd028668bef3c825bb07780e625a414b639303a","verification":{"payload":"tree 7b6904f14d9d87795f154188047b838926f3a51f\nparent 19a51eab4cf18e4321c8a074db20e10ab90696d9\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788351147 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788351147 +0100\n\nfeat(bugreport): the report screen, the FAB and the crash handler\n\nEverything that makes the reporter reachable and usable.\n\nThe review step is a step rather than a dialog. The promise it keeps — that a\ntester knows exactly what leaves their phone — is not one a summary can keep,\nso it shows the actual text and the actual file list with real sizes.\n\nConsent gates the files and nothing else. Leave it unticked and the button\nstill says \"Review and send\", because a report with a description and a device\nblock is worth having and making consent mandatory in practice would be a dark\npattern wearing a checkbox.\n\nThe FAB is round, parked top right, and draggable, with its position kept as\nfractions of the screen so a rotation moves it proportionally rather than off\nthe edge. Both bottom corners already belong to the mic button and the input\nbar, and a permanent overlay will eventually cover something a tester needs —\nso rather than guess a corner that is always safe, let them move it. It snaps\nto the nearer side on release and hides itself inside the reporter.\n\nThe crash handler writes the trace on the way down, because nobody can tap a\nbutton in a process that has already died; without it we would only ever hear\nabout bugs that did not crash the app. It stays deliberately dull — one\nsynchronous write, no injection, no coroutines — and hands straight back to\nthe previous handler.\n\nTwo things this changes that were not strictly asked for. The capture toggles\nnow default on in testing builds, which made three existing blurbs untrue:\nthey claimed \"never uploaded\" and \"off by default\", and both had to go. And\nlint was already red on a SEND_SMS permission with no matching uses-feature,\nwhich would have hidden Ari from every device without a radio — fixed while\npassing, since it was one line and the check is now green.\n\nItalian is drafted, not authoritative. 562/562 parity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMTHZvmbas7ZnvnViHPOQ4I08CU4UaSGv/7tMQAZzpfAIFvLMVIA21OaIotTDolLWp\n1CRShre/uZxO2YVy2nLw0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T12:12:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/1cd028668bef3c825bb07780e625a414b639303a","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDFjZDAyODY2OGJlZjNjODI1YmIwNzc4MGU2MjVhNDE0YjYzOTMwM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/19a51eab4cf18e4321c8a074db20e10ab90696d9","sha":"19a51eab4cf18e4321c8a074db20e10ab90696d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/19a51eab4cf18e4321c8a074db20e10ab90696d9"}],"sha":"1cd028668bef3c825bb07780e625a414b639303a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/1cd028668bef3c825bb07780e625a414b639303a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/19a51eab4cf18e4321c8a074db20e10ab90696d9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:52:38Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:52:38Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(bugreport): gather a report and send it to heyari.dev\n\nThe half of the reporter that has no UI: the wire model, the client, and the\ncollector that fills it in.\n\nSending is three steps, not one — create the report and get somewhere to put\nthe files, upload them straight to storage, then finalise, which is what files\nthe public issue. An issue is therefore never filed pointing at attachments\nthat failed to upload, because evidence that does not exist is worse than no\nissue at all.\n\nAbsent fields are omitted rather than blanked, so \"not recorded\" reads as\nabsent on the issue instead of as a measurement of nothing. Two exceptions\ncarry tests: an unset battery-optimisation exemption and zero free storage are\nboth findings, and dropping them would hide the answer to the question.\n\nThe collector reads only what the app already keeps and never starts recording\nanything of its own. Logcat goes through the scrubber before it touches disk,\nso even the staged copy is redacted. `files()` on the two capture stores is\nexposed rather than new — both already composed exactly that list for their\nshare sheets.\n\nThe conversation attachment covers the current session only; the log is held\nin memory and dies with the process. That matters less than it sounds, because\nthe utterance captures already carry transcripts in their sidecars, so a crash\nreport is not blind.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"691e97e39a7413941519f7df3c246642fc12778a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/691e97e39a7413941519f7df3c246642fc12778a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/19a51eab4cf18e4321c8a074db20e10ab90696d9","verification":{"payload":"tree 691e97e39a7413941519f7df3c246642fc12778a\nparent 3758b5681d6fb3df5e94112627e6eceb2fd46cbe\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788349958 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788349958 +0100\n\nfeat(bugreport): gather a report and send it to heyari.dev\n\nThe half of the reporter that has no UI: the wire model, the client, and the\ncollector that fills it in.\n\nSending is three steps, not one — create the report and get somewhere to put\nthe files, upload them straight to storage, then finalise, which is what files\nthe public issue. An issue is therefore never filed pointing at attachments\nthat failed to upload, because evidence that does not exist is worse than no\nissue at all.\n\nAbsent fields are omitted rather than blanked, so \"not recorded\" reads as\nabsent on the issue instead of as a measurement of nothing. Two exceptions\ncarry tests: an unset battery-optimisation exemption and zero free storage are\nboth findings, and dropping them would hide the answer to the question.\n\nThe collector reads only what the app already keeps and never starts recording\nanything of its own. Logcat goes through the scrubber before it touches disk,\nso even the staged copy is redacted. `files()` on the two capture stores is\nexposed rather than new — both already composed exactly that list for their\nshare sheets.\n\nThe conversation attachment covers the current session only; the log is held\nin memory and dies with the process. That matters less than it sounds, because\nthe utterance captures already carry transcripts in their sidecars, so a crash\nreport is not blind.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMq3nJKk3anMx2LbJj8jtkN0fJ27B6JO2xGGdKB5B9FFoB2gq+xqoNo8Cadba5r9Hf\nuIoj5XbNY12kWP67JSpg4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T11:52:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/19a51eab4cf18e4321c8a074db20e10ab90696d9","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDE5YTUxZWFiNGNmMThlNDMyMWM4YTA3NGRiMjBlMTBhYjkwNjk2ZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/3758b5681d6fb3df5e94112627e6eceb2fd46cbe","sha":"3758b5681d