thored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0823cf1980faea367cd311051fa4fde696ccef9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/0823cf1980faea367cd311051fa4fde696ccef9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/3758b5681d6fb3df5e94112627e6eceb2fd46cbe","verification":{"payload":"tree 0823cf1980faea367cd311051fa4fde696ccef9a\nparent d61b30daa2a1f1fe7d67ac3664e277f18dc7c24b\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788349958 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788349958 +0100\n\nffi(bindings): regenerate for engine_version()\n\nGenerated, not hand-edited: the engine change landed on ari-engine main first,\nthen `uniffi-bindgen generate --library` against the built cdylib. Purely\nadditive — the checksum table, the extern, and the one function.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLZ1UbnxzMGYNsffQk3J1vndzSR3mJsPYLc20Rr4M9JWjpLn/tQAw2HCctARkHYJpQ\n7V5iQzCCUK55RlsE2aqgg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T11:52:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/3758b5681d6fb3df5e94112627e6eceb2fd46cbe","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDM3NThiNTY4MWQ2ZmIzZGY1ZTk0MTEyNjI3ZTZlY2ViMmZkNDZjYmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/d61b30daa2a1f1fe7d67ac3664e277f18dc7c24b","sha":"d61b30daa2a1f1fe7d67ac3664e277f18dc7c24b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/d61b30daa2a1f1fe7d67ac3664e277f18dc7c24b"}],"sha":"3758b5681d6fb3df5e94112627e6eceb2fd46cbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/3758b5681d6fb3df5e94112627e6eceb2fd46cbe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/d61b30daa2a1f1fe7d67ac3664e277f18dc7c24b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:31:54Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:31:54Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"chore: add issue forms for bugs and feature requests\n\nPer-repo rather than an org-wide default: defaults in the .github repo are\nonly a fallback that any repo-level template overrides, and the fields differ\ntoo much between the app, the engine and the skills to share one.\n\nThe device questions carry their weight — ROM and battery-optimisation state\nare behind most of the \"it just stopped working\" reports we are going to get.\n\nTwo pointers to the in-app reporter are deliberately missing and carry a\nRESTORE WITH B7 comment at the exact spot: the button does not exist yet, and\nthe link would point at a README section in a repo that has no README.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fca83424d2c231f83a810dfc96c6283b7486b9b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/fca83424d2c231f83a810dfc96c6283b7486b9b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/d61b30daa2a1f1fe7d67ac3664e277f18dc7c24b","verification":{"payload":"tree fca83424d2c231f83a810dfc96c6283b7486b9b2\nparent 9c016a7e5c2c1a3981a2c34f5e0753da3adb19bd\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788348714 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788348714 +0100\n\nchore: add issue forms for bugs and feature requests\n\nPer-repo rather than an org-wide default: defaults in the .github repo are\nonly a fallback that any repo-level template overrides, and the fields differ\ntoo much between the app, the engine and the skills to share one.\n\nThe device questions carry their weight — ROM and battery-optimisation state\nare behind most of the \"it just stopped working\" reports we are going to get.\n\nTwo pointers to the in-app reporter are deliberately missing and carry a\nRESTORE WITH B7 comment at the exact spot: the button does not exist yet, and\nthe link would point at a README section in a repo that has no README.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJZ0ExVLuJ3pHF0it7hVXnUO7+oUfE1vvcWoQWSFO7/jzgvwk96ZTCdgeSfnufnv3i\nZR0DUrW4osGTPI/pdNZAI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T11:32:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/d61b30daa2a1f1fe7d67ac3664e277f18dc7c24b","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGQ2MWIzMGRhYTJhMWYxZmU3ZDY3YWMzNjY0ZTI3N2YxOGRjN2MyNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/9c016a7e5c2c1a3981a2c34f5e0753da3adb19bd","sha":"9c016a7e5c2c1a3981a2c34f5e0753da3adb19bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/9c016a7e5c2c1a3981a2c34f5e0753da3adb19bd"}],"sha":"d61b30daa2a1f1fe7d67ac3664e277f18dc7c24b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/d61b30daa2a1f1fe7d67ac3664e277f18dc7c24b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/9c016a7e5c2c1a3981a2c34f5e0753da3adb19bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:31:54Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:31:54Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(bugreport): scrub credentials and personal data out of a log\n\nFirst pass over the values the app actually holds — SecretStore entries,\nconfigured endpoints — because those are exact and can be redacted with\ncertainty. A stored URL takes its bare host with it, since DNS and TLS\nfailures log the host on its own. Then a short list of patterns for things\nthe app never stored.\n\nRedactions are named: `<redacted: ha_token>` still tells a maintainer which\ncredential was in play, which a row of asterisks does not.\n\nDeliberately conservative, with tests pinning the restraint. Routing\nconfidences, timestamps and stack traces survive intact — a rule that ate\nthose would leave a scrubbed log nobody can debug from. Phone numbers match\nonly with a country prefix, and coordinates only as a pair, because eight\nbare digits is also a timestamp and a lone decimal is also a confidence.\n\nBare local numbers will get through. That is why a scrubbed log still goes to\nprivate storage rather than a public issue, and why the report screen will\noffer a separate private note instead of asking anyone to trust this with\nfree text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f1abc12546b1b9455e866fa330d4a5971c4edeed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/f1abc12546b1b9455e866fa330d4a5971c4edeed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/9c016a7e5c2c1a3981a2c34f5e0753da3adb19bd","verification":{"payload":"tree f1abc12546b1b9455e866fa330d4a5971c4edeed\nparent cb0ab41ed463f14c413eb6f4d8d5af46ec5f6920\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788348714 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788348714 +0100\n\nfeat(bugreport): scrub credentials and personal data out of a log\n\nFirst pass over the values the app actually holds — SecretStore entries,\nconfigured endpoints — because those are exact and can be redacted with\ncertainty. A stored URL takes its bare host with it, since DNS and TLS\nfailures log the host on its own. Then a short list of patterns for things\nthe app never stored.\n\nRedactions are named: `<redacted: ha_token>` still tells a maintainer which\ncredential was in play, which a row of asterisks does not.\n\nDeliberately conservative, with tests pinning the restraint. Routing\nconfidences, timestamps and stack traces survive intact — a rule that ate\nthose would leave a scrubbed log nobody can debug from. Phone numbers match\nonly with a country prefix, and coordinates only as a pair, because eight\nbare digits is also a timestamp and a lone decimal is also a confidence.\n\nBare local numbers will get through. That is why a scrubbed log still goes to\nprivate storage rather than a public issue, and why the report screen will\noffer a separate private note instead of asking anyone to trust this with\nfree text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQID4qEecP5lNL9Joda4xOo1i3MJuIExv83YEhxcP59n3uwUlbimAWVdQFxxVrxwFHG\nMrS9QTm20svV86J7jA9gs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T11:32:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/9c016a7e5c2c1a3981a2c34f5e0753da3adb19bd","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKDljMDE2YTdlNWMyYzFhMzk4MWEyYzM0ZjVlMDc1M2RhM2FkYjE5YmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/cb0ab41ed463f14c413eb6f4d8d5af46ec5f6920","sha":"cb0ab41ed463f14c413eb6f4d8d5af46ec5f6920","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/cb0ab41ed463f14c413eb6f4d8d5af46ec5f6920"}],"sha":"9c016a7e5c2c1a3981a2c34f5e0753da3adb19bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/9c016a7e5c2c1a3981a2c34f5e0753da3adb19bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/cb0ab41ed463f14c413eb6f4d8d5af46ec5f6920/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:31:54Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:31:54Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"build: add a beta build type for testers, gated on ARI_TESTING\n\nBuild type, minification, signing key and the debuggable flag are four\nindependent knobs, and treating them as one would have left testers on a\nbuild whose stack traces are unreadable.\n\n`beta` is release-signed and not debuggable, so it behaves like the shipped\napp and Play would accept it, but it is NOT minified — an R8-mangled trace in\na bug report is worth nothing, and retracing server-side is work we do not\nneed yet. The price is that it is not byte-identical to what ships.\n\nNamed `beta` rather than `testing` because AGP rejects any build type whose\nname starts with `test`; it collides with the test source sets.\n\nEverything tester-facing gates on BuildConfig.ARI_TESTING rather than\nBuildConfig.DEBUG. DEBUG is false on a release-signed beta, so gating on it\nwould hide the bug reporter from exactly the people who need it. True for\nbeta and debug, false for release: the question it answers is whether this\nbuild went to someone who might file a report.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"48c6ccf9be7f00e0d06d5a4f7c7fb4c715e87fb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/48c6ccf9be7f00e0d06d5a4f7c7fb4c715e87fb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/cb0ab41ed463f14c413eb6f4d8d5af46ec5f6920","verification":{"payload":"tree 48c6ccf9be7f00e0d06d5a4f7c7fb4c715e87fb0\nparent fc482b8c73ccb321ad7b928b8ccc4ac36782a1c4\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788348714 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788348714 +0100\n\nbuild: add a beta build type for testers, gated on ARI_TESTING\n\nBuild type, minification, signing key and the debuggable flag are four\nindependent knobs, and treating them as one would have left testers on a\nbuild whose stack traces are unreadable.\n\n`beta` is release-signed and not debuggable, so it behaves like the shipped\napp and Play would accept it, but it is NOT minified — an R8-mangled trace in\na bug report is worth nothing, and retracing server-side is work we do not\nneed yet. The price is that it is not byte-identical to what ships.\n\nNamed `beta` rather than `testing` because AGP rejects any build type whose\nname starts with `test`; it collides with the test source sets.\n\nEverything tester-facing gates on BuildConfig.ARI_TESTING rather than\nBuildConfig.DEBUG. DEBUG is false on a release-signed beta, so gating on it\nwould hide the bug reporter from exactly the people who need it. True for\nbeta and debug, false for release: the question it answers is whether this\nbuild went to someone who might file a report.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQE67O9lTa04LzRu4CB+21OLcxW7sBvyUkXHDD97dIGXIu6vWPzx9MhW1V2RlmCuKoL\nvOK2dFY2x5dTwLCnr1PA8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T11:32:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/cb0ab41ed463f14c413eb6f4d8d5af46ec5f6920","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGNiMGFiNDFlZDQ2M2YxNGM0MTNlYjZmNGQ4ZDVhZjQ2ZWM1ZjY5MjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/fc482b8c73ccb321ad7b928b8ccc4ac36782a1c4","sha":"fc482b8c73ccb321ad7b928b8ccc4ac36782a1c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/fc482b8c73ccb321ad7b928b8ccc4ac36782a1c4"}],"sha":"cb0ab41ed463f14c413eb6f4d8d5af46ec5f6920","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/cb0ab41ed463f14c413eb6f4d8d5af46ec5f6920"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/fc482b8c73ccb321ad7b928b8ccc4ac36782a1c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T09:13:00Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T09:13:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"UI/UX pass: navigation, tappable rows, wizard performance, keyboard insets, dynamic colour, i18n (#3)\n\n* fix(android): slide between pages instead of showing the window through\n\nNavigation-compose crossfades between destinations by default. Both\nscreens are semi-transparent halfway through that, so whatever sits\nbehind them shows — and what sat behind them was the window background,\nwhich the theme hardcoded to Material Light. Hence the white flash on\nthe way into every Settings page, in dark mode as much as light.\n\nSlide forward/back instead, which is what Android does everywhere else,\nand stop the window from being able to show through at all: an opaque\nthemed Surface behind the NavHost, and a windowBackground that has a\nvalues-night twin rather than being white in both themes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(settings): make the whole row tappable, not just the radio\n\nEvery choice row in the wizard and in Settings only responded to a tap\non the radio button or switch itself, which is a small target and not\nhow Android behaves anywhere else.\n\nThe row now carries the selectable/toggleable modifier with the right\nsemantic role, and the control takes a null callback so screen readers\nsee one control per row rather than two. That null callback is also why\nthe controls now ask for the interactive size explicitly: Material only\ngrants it when a control handles its own clicks, and without it the\nlabel sits flush against the radio and the model rows stop lining up\nwith the 48dp indent their secondary text already assumed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(settings): stop every preference write waking every reader\n\nFlipping one toggle in the wizard could visibly stall the UI. DataStore\nre-emits the whole preference blob on any write and none of the two\ndozen flows deduped, so writing one key woke every reader in\nSettingsViewModel. Several of those readers did real work on the main\nthread: re-enumerating every TTS voice installed on the phone (a binder\ncall, then a sort over the lot), FFI calls into the engine to rebuild\nthe assistant list, and a stat of every model directory on disk.\n\nThree fixes, all needed. The preference flows dedupe, so a no-op write\nwakes nobody. The readers that touch the TTS service, the engine, the\nfilesystem or the keystore moved off the main thread. And the wizard\nshares one SettingsViewModel across its steps instead of standing up a\nfresh one — with all of the above in its constructor — six times over.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(stt): stop re-encrypting the cloud API key on every keystroke\n\nEvery character typed into the cloud transcriber''s API key field ran an\nAES-GCM encryption through the Android keystore and committed a\nSharedPreferences write, on the main thread.\n\nThe field holds the key locally and hands it over once, on dispose —\nthe same shape as the secret fields in SkillSettingsPanel. That means\nthe save now fires as the screen is being popped, so it persists on the\napplication scope rather than viewModelScope, which is about to be\ncancelled; SkillsViewModel already learned that lesson the hard way.\n\nSeeding needs care in the other direction: the stored key is read off\nthe main thread now, so it can land after the field first composes. The\nfield takes the stored value only until the user starts typing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(android): keep the keyboard from covering the field it opened for\n\nTapping an API key field brought up the keyboard on top of the field.\n\nThe manifest does ask for adjustResize, but enableEdgeToEdge() opts the\nwindow out of being resized at all — the app draws behind the keyboard\ninstead — so that request has been dead since edge-to-edge went in.\nConversationScreen had already worked around it locally with\nimePadding(); nothing else had.\n\nFixed in the two shared scaffolds plus the two screens that build their\nown, which covers every text field in the app. Making room is also what\nlets Compose do the other half: text fields already ask to be scrolled\ninto view on focus, but the container had no idea it was any shorter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* i18n: pull the last hardcoded strings out of the UI\n\nTwenty-one strings were still English literals in Kotlin, so they stayed\nEnglish no matter what language the app was set to. The worst of them\nwere on the timer card itself — \"Remaining\", \"Ringing\", \"Done\" and the\n\"Stop\" button — which meant setting a timer in Italian got you an\nEnglish card back from a skill that is fully translated.\n\nAlso covered: the assistant settings page, the TTS voice picker, the\ncalendar and tasks permission blurbs, the model-size hint in the wizard,\nand the full-screen alert''s timestamp and Dismiss button.\n\n`actionsForState` builds the Stop action and is not a composable, so the\nlabel is resolved by its caller and passed in rather than dragging a\nContext into what is otherwise a plain data transform.\n\nItalian is a first draft for review. The only literals left in the UI\nare animation labels, which never reach a user.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): stop picking colours by role name under dynamic colour\n\nSeveral surfaces were unreadable: pink button labels on the yellow\n\"install a cloud assistant\" and \"set location to always\" prompts, and a\ntimer card whose progress bar and Cancel button all but vanished.\n\nTwo causes. The prompts were the simple one — a TextButton defaults its\nlabel to `primary`, which has nothing to do with the tertiary container\nit sits on, and under dynamic colour those are unrelated hues.\n\nThe timer card was not. This device reports `tertiaryContainer` as\n#F0EFAB — a light yellow — in a *dark* scheme, while primaryContainer\nand secondaryContainer come back properly dark. So a role''s name tells\nyou nothing about its lightness, and the usual fix of pairing role\nfamilies correctly does not help: `error` is a light pink there, fine on\na dark card and invisible on that one. Card accents now measure contrast\nagainst the container they actually landed on and fall back to its own\non* role, which is the one colour guaranteed to read.\n\nSkill card icons had the same problem from the other direction. They are\nbitmaps inside signed bundles, both of them pale grey glyphs drawn for a\ndark card, and a skill cannot know what colour its card will be. The\nrenderer now tints a silhouette to the card''s content colour, detecting\nand leaving alone anything with real colour in it so a picture icon\nisn''t flattened to a blob.\n\nSeparately, the permission ticks and pro/con bullets were literal hex\nand so didn''t move with the theme. Material has no success or warning\nrole, which is why they were hardcoded; the theme now carries its own\nwith light and dark variants. No hardcoded colour remains outside the\ntheme package.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(settings): give URL fields a URL keyboard\n\nA prose keyboard capitalises the first letter and puts a space after\nevery dot, which is no way to type a server address.\n\nSkill config fields honour the manifest''s new `keyboard: url` hint; an\nunrecognised value falls back to the ordinary text keyboard so a\nmanifest written against a newer schema still renders. The cloud\ntranscriber''s endpoint field is set directly, since the app owns that\none and already knows it''s a URL.\n\nBindings regenerated for FfiConfigField''s new `keyboard` field, with\n`cargo run -p ari-ffi --bin uniffi-bindgen -- generate --library\ntarget/debug/libari_ffi.so --language kotlin`.\n\nNeeds the matching ari-engine change: the Rust is built from the\nsibling checkout, so that one merges first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"86de23d1dfc98f4c1a9ff20c7ae5314460658d6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/86de23d1dfc98f4c1a9ff20c7ae5314460658d6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/fc482b8c73ccb321ad7b928b8ccc4ac36782a1c4","verification":{"payload":"tree 86de23d1dfc98f4c1a9ff20c7ae5314460658d6a\nparent 80425ce7c0aa98e8c909acb9376233f247a11940\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788340380 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788340380 +0100\n\nUI/UX pass: navigation, tappable rows, wizard performance, keyboard insets, dynamic colour, i18n (#3)\n\n* fix(android): slide between pages instead of showing the window through\n\nNavigation-compose crossfades between destinations by default. Both\nscreens are semi-transparent halfway through that, so whatever sits\nbehind them shows — and what sat behind them was the window background,\nwhich the theme hardcoded to Material Light. Hence the white flash on\nthe way into every Settings page, in dark mode as much as light.\n\nSlide forward/back instead, which is what Android does everywhere else,\nand stop the window from being able to show through at all: an opaque\nthemed Surface behind the NavHost, and a windowBackground that has a\nvalues-night twin rather than being white in both themes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(settings): make the whole row tappable, not just the radio\n\nEvery choice row in the wizard and in Settings only responded to a tap\non the radio button or switch itself, which is a small target and not\nhow Android behaves anywhere else.\n\nThe row now carries the selectable/toggleable modifier with the right\nsemantic role, and the control takes a null callback so screen readers\nsee one control per row rather than two. That null callback is also why\nthe controls now ask for the interactive size explicitly: Material only\ngrants it when a control handles its own clicks, and without it the\nlabel sits flush against the radio and the model rows stop lining up\nwith the 48dp indent their secondary text already assumed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(settings): stop every preference write waking every reader\n\nFlipping one toggle in the wizard could visibly stall the UI. DataStore\nre-emits the whole preference blob on any write and none of the two\ndozen flows deduped, so writing one key woke every reader in\nSettingsViewModel. Several of those readers did real work on the main\nthread: re-enumerating every TTS voice installed on the phone (a binder\ncall, then a sort over the lot), FFI calls into the engine to rebuild\nthe assistant list, and a stat of every model directory on disk.\n\nThree fixes, all needed. The preference flows dedupe, so a no-op write\nwakes nobody. The readers that touch the TTS service, the engine, the\nfilesystem or the keystore moved off the main thread. And the wizard\nshares one SettingsViewModel across its steps instead of standing up a\nfresh one — with all of the above in its constructor — six times over.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(stt): stop re-encrypting the cloud API key on every keystroke\n\nEvery character typed into the cloud transcriber''s API key field ran an\nAES-GCM encryption through the Android keystore and committed a\nSharedPreferences write, on the main thread.\n\nThe field holds the key locally and hands it over once, on dispose —\nthe same shape as the secret fields in SkillSettingsPanel. That means\nthe save now fires as the screen is being popped, so it persists on the\napplication scope rather than viewModelScope, which is about to be\ncancelled; SkillsViewModel already learned that lesson the hard way.\n\nSeeding needs care in the other direction: the stored key is read off\nthe main thread now, so it can land after the field first composes. The\nfield takes the stored value only until the user starts typing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(android): keep the keyboard from covering the field it opened for\n\nTapping an API key field brought up the keyboard on top of the field.\n\nThe manifest does ask for adjustResize, but enableEdgeToEdge() opts the\nwindow out of being resized at all — the app draws behind the keyboard\ninstead — so that request has been dead since edge-to-edge went in.\nConversationScreen had already worked around it locally with\nimePadding(); nothing else had.\n\nFixed in the two shared scaffolds plus the two screens that build their\nown, which covers every text field in the app. Making room is also what\nlets Compose do the other half: text fields already ask to be scrolled\ninto view on focus, but the container had no idea it was any shorter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* i18n: pull the last hardcoded strings out of the UI\n\nTwenty-one strings were still English literals in Kotlin, so they stayed\nEnglish no matter what language the app was set to. The worst of them\nwere on the timer card itself — \"Remaining\", \"Ringing\", \"Done\" and the\n\"Stop\" button — which meant setting a timer in Italian got you an\nEnglish card back from a skill that is fully translated.\n\nAlso covered: the assistant settings page, the TTS voice picker, the\ncalendar and tasks permission blurbs, the model-size hint in the wizard,\nand the full-screen alert''s timestamp and Dismiss button.\n\n`actionsForState` builds the Stop action and is not a composable, so the\nlabel is resolved by its caller and passed in rather than dragging a\nContext into what is otherwise a plain data transform.\n\nItalian is a first draft for review. The only literals left in the UI\nare animation labels, which never reach a user.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): stop picking colours by role name under dynamic colour\n\nSeveral surfaces were unreadable: pink button labels on the yellow\n\"install a cloud assistant\" and \"set location to always\" prompts, and a\ntimer card whose progress bar and Cancel button all but vanished.\n\nTwo causes. The prompts were the simple one — a TextButton defaults its\nlabel to `primary`, which has nothing to do with the tertiary container\nit sits on, and under dynamic colour those are unrelated hues.\n\nThe timer card was not. This device reports `tertiaryContainer` as\n#F0EFAB — a light yellow — in a *dark* scheme, while primaryContainer\nand secondaryContainer come back properly dark. So a role''s name tells\nyou nothing about its lightness, and the usual fix of pairing role\nfamilies correctly does not help: `error` is a light pink there, fine on\na dark card and invisible on that one. Card accents now measure contrast\nagainst the container they actually landed on and fall back to its own\non* role, which is the one colour guaranteed to read.\n\nSkill card icons had the same problem from the other direction. They are\nbitmaps inside signed bundles, both of them pale grey glyphs drawn for a\ndark card, and a skill cannot know what colour its card will be. The\nrenderer now tints a silhouette to the card''s content colour, detecting\nand leaving alone anything with real colour in it so a picture icon\nisn''t flattened to a blob.\n\nSeparately, the permission ticks and pro/con bullets were literal hex\nand so didn''t move with the theme. Material has no success or warning\nrole, which is why they were hardcoded; the theme now carries its own\nwith light and dark variants. No hardcoded colour remains outside the\ntheme package.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(settings): give URL fields a URL keyboard\n\nA prose keyboard capitalises the first letter and puts a space after\nevery dot, which is no way to type a server address.\n\nSkill config fields honour the manifest''s new `keyboard: url` hint; an\nunrecognised value falls back to the ordinary text keyboard so a\nmanifest written against a newer schema still renders. The cloud\ntranscriber''s endpoint field is set directly, since the app owns that\none and already knows it''s a URL.\n\nBindings regenerated for FfiConfigField''s new `keyboard` field, with\n`cargo run -p ari-ffi --bin uniffi-bindgen -- generate --library\ntarget/debug/libari_ffi.so --language kotlin`.\n\nNeeds the matching ari-engine change: the Rust is built from the\nsibling checkout, so that one merges first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql+idCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtbIQAJaO5W9Tl9UAUOi4s1ZmYEIV\nfeJxdU9zjD1ZmXrfbFCp8NnrRgfyyt3+4F+gvG3hDVHFb9mWXulbICe6+2xSki6C\nGDTweIsGND5SMdTO2iRg5gxBItGZINOnffyDdarpUyt5k5h6S5lzNR30bQfRh9Nj\nFNmhzTv8XPYq923XHVyRAzdS/psWpg+7DyGCfySHht7H3LGpU8gQsLJ1KGKmHfkV\n2eSSqCz3icbyJHhZHgHQKuwpuk8nk1CbnZhG68QLDzGh//XkjXa+Hpcfm4nbJM0y\nr4M/ti6BGzJMmR12KOGCxRkfz2UCZt/QeHezDqmUXszl7xLNO+6ax6/GimFRAt45\nYySo2U74dP2nxWvXfQ0zlStXRAJmmYlUgZzXFOvVbG3qUNt64YfVGnKPqJ0yX9Sr\nsVswQZKfI2cnV8IjcisImfy1OoRiuISs3hjhl/FsXFek2usO4qwt6d6aAhE9IHue\nQljahcRHnkz7Du/Drr4f+5plTMf1t4+k7KwDVp0B+LKNsP3KVzu7I2tveheTT7rH\nV8cOJHtJt3xIor84mOckoWSHxzd/EyOR4rDw7qjO/i9CDe0SAk51nBL6Gm7HGJmO\n/lousYkab7McI9QGPVF5K9UZdpuhr06sci8UlZHoV8t4d/l60X+7gSgBo87SxPWw\nZhahr9l1+UiAICLE58fO\n=DSDT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T09:13:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/fc482b8c73ccb321ad7b928b8ccc4ac36782a1c4","node_id":"C_kwDOR736EdoAKGZjNDgyYjhjNzNjY2IzMjFhZDdiOTI4YjhjY2M0YWMzNjc4MmExYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commit/80425ce7c0aa98e8c909acb9376233f247a11940","sha":"80425ce7c0aa98e8c909acb9376233f247a11940","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/80425ce7c0aa98e8c909acb9376233f247a11940"}],"sha":"fc482b8c73ccb321ad7b928b8ccc4ac36782a1c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/fc482b8c73ccb321ad7b928b8ccc4ac36782a1c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keithvassallomt","id":5295061,"login":"keithvassallomt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyOTUwNjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/commits/80425ce7c0aa98e8c909acb9376233f247a11940/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:33:33Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:33:33Z","email":"keith@vassallo.cloud","name":"Keith Vassallo"},"message":"feat(router): push the user''s task lists into the engine\n\nThe engine can now constrain a phrase slot to a runtime vocabulary, but\nonly the frontend can see what is in one. Task lists are the first:\n\"add bananas to family shopping\" is a list add and \"add cream to the\ncoffee\" is not, and the list names are the only thing that says so.\n\nPushed at engine build and again on every return-to-foreground — lists\nare created and renamed in a separate app, which broadcasts nothing we\ncould listen for, so a stale snapshot is the only way the slot goes\nwrong.\n\nBindings regenerated for setVocabulary.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"67ca53b660168bee1b4f39ad5daac6378ecbec26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/trees/67ca53b660168bee1b4f39ad5daac6378ecbec26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ari-digital-assistant/ari-android/git/commits/80425ce7c0aa98e8c909acb9376233f247a11940","verification":{"payload":"tree 67ca53b660168bee1b4f39ad5daac6378ecbec26\nparent 890f0945271b01223e2be79996aa7491fd49dec3\nauthor Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788280413 +0100\ncommitter Keith Vassallo <keith@vassallo.cloud> 1788280413 +0100\n\nfeat(router): push the user''s task lists into the engine\n\nThe engine can now constrain a phrase slot to a runtime vocabulary, but\nonly the frontend can see what is in one. Task lists are the first:\n\"add bananas to family shopping\" is a list add and \"add cream to the\ncoffee\" is not, and the list names are the only thing that says so.\n\nPushed at engine build and again on every return-to-foreground — lists\nare created and renamed in a separate app, which broadcasts nothing we\ncould listen for, so a stale snapshot is the only way the slot goes\nwrong.\n\nBindings regenerated for setVocabulary.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBwuNMZ9IHCIvq+SKh0ksD1v+0n\n2JyY0wAMl9Z5mLJ/QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQO8kZpGJBV8jB5PWOG8f32W21fNZgA5J6KNECqZ1gTIR6xOe/8Mdu/ncxDlPRUgk/9\njgTMVcEW5LPwwU5T3xhA0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T16:39:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5295061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithvassallomt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keithv